% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GSC: the syntactically-grassroots checker.
%
% Decides def:syntactically-grassroots of /Grassroots/GSC, Section 3, one
% definition for a contract of agent roles and listed roles (GSC ac7ad63),
% with the values of its appendix "Values in Speech-Act Schemas" (app:numbers).
% The signed term, reflexive predicates and contracts with wards are GAI's
% extension of the language (GAI's appendix "Contracts with Wards"; GSC
% 83b951c and 1a2a5f3), held here for GAI.  The papers are the specification
% and no definition of them is restated here; each procedure names the
% definition it decides.  README.md maps the two.
%
% This file is the directory's shared scope: the representation of a contract,
% the substitution and matching machinery every condition needs, and the
% directory's entry points.
%
% The condition on a contract with wards is GAI's (Coordination Appendix B;
% Udi, 2026-10-20) and lives in the child directory wards/, entered through
% its self.glp by the qualifier wards (TGLP, Section "Module System",
% "Cross-module type checking": a qualifier is a child directory or module
% file of the caller's directory).  It reads the introductions of a schema,
% intro_act_bindings/2 of unobstructed.glp, which this file exposes to its
% subtree (TGLP, "The -expose directive").
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-expose(unobstructed).

% --- The syntax of a schema (def:role, def:schema) -------------------------
% A name term (def:role, GSC f5b3f06: "<pi> for an agent variable pi of it"):
% own(I) is <pi_I>, for pi_I a role of its schema, own_var(X) is <x> for an
% agent variable x that is no role, and ext(Sigma, Y) is Sigma.y.
%
% The wildcard _ may stand anywhere an argument may, and in place of the
% speech-act variable of a name term (def:schema, GSC f5b3f06): any is the
% wildcard as an argument, and ext_any(Sigma) the name term Sigma._.  In an
% unnegated atom it is "a variable of its own, one per occurrence"; in a
% negated one it is universally quantified, the atom forbidding, in the body,
% and deleting, in the head, every atom that matches it.  A negated atom of
% the head with a wildcard is a cleared atom, of *(i): it requires none
% (def:schema, def:binding, def:compile's K_p).  The term form writes it
% among a role's deleted atoms; rs_del below gives -(i), the deleted atoms
% with no wildcard, and rs_clear *(i).
NameTerm  ::= own(Integer) ; own_var(Constant)
            ; ext(NameTerm, Constant) ; ext_any(NameTerm).
NameTerms ::= [] ; [NameTerm | NameTerms].

% An argument is a role, named by its index in the schema, a party variable, a
% speech-act variable, a name term or a signed term: sgn(Y, I) is the signed
% term sgn(y, pi_I) of def:schema, the speech act y signed by the agent in
% role I.  Speech-act schemas allow numbers (GSC, Section 3.2, the paragraph after
% the example of def:schema, and def:numbers): num(X) is a value argument,
% the value variable X where X is a name and the number X where X is a
% number.
% A value variable has a type, which the term form writes (GSC 8b1460f, the
% appendix "Values in Speech-Act Schemas": "a value variable of a schema has
% a type, which the schema's term form writes, so that the same clauses are
% realised over whole or over fractional amounts by the schemas' choice"):
% among a schema's variables, num(X) is a whole value variable and real(X) a
% real one; an atom, a multiplicity and a constraint write the value argument
% num(X) of either, the variable's type being its head's.
% item_of(svar(Y)) is the item item(y) of the speech-act variable y, the
% utterance under the signatures of y, an argument of an atom and an
% expression of a constraint (def:numbers, GSC 4401dd6); it names no agent and
% has no base (the appendix, after def:binding-numbers: "A value, and an
% utterance, is no agent role, no agent variable and no name term, so it has
% no base"), and a binding sends it to the utterance beta(y) carries.
Arg   ::= role(Integer) ; pvar(Constant) ; svar(Constant) ; nterm(NameTerm)
        ; sgn(Constant, Integer) ; num(Constant) ; real(Constant) ; any
        ; item_of(Arg).
Args  ::= [] ; [Arg | Args].
Atom  ::= atom(Constant, Args).
Atoms ::= [] ; [Atom | Atoms].

% --- The values speech-act schemas allow (GSC, def:numbers) -----------------------
% "Speech-act schemas allow values of any type: an argument of an atom may be a
% value or a value variable, a schema may carry a constraint on its value
% variables, which every binding satisfies, and an atom added or deleted may
% carry a multiplicity, a count of copies and so a positive whole number"
% (Section 3.2; def:numbers and def:binding-numbers in the appendix).  times(K, A) is the
% atom A with the multiplicity K, K a value argument; a constraint is
% Constraint below, extending the term form of Currencies' GB.glp.  A
% schema with a constraint is nschema(Name, Vars, Constraint, Roles), its
% value variables listed in Vars with its other variables, in the order of
% its head.  The contract as written is of the types N...; traceable
% provenance and volition are decided on its plain form, plain_decl below,
% the multiplicities and the constraint dropped and the value arguments
% kept, since "a number names no agent, so the conditions below do not
% concern them" (GSC, ibid.; the appendix, after def:binding-numbers).
% def:unobstructed is decided on the contract as written (unobstructed.glp):
% its clauses ask that an atom be added at a binding, so a number is matched
% by equality under that binding, "no condition reading a constraint" (the
% appendix).
% rest(K, J, A) is the copies of K.A a role requires beyond the J copies of
% A it deletes, K or J a value variable: def:numbers admits a required k.A
% with j copies deleted where "the schema's constraint ensures j <= k, so
% that -(i) is a subset of =(i) at every binding", and the denotation
% deletes the j copies (Definition Denotation).  -(i) and =(i) are multisets,
% so i.A and j.A deleted are (i + j).A deleted, J then plus(i, j), and k1.A
% and k2.A required are (k1 + k2).A required, K then plus(k1, k2).  It
% occurs only among a role's Keep, beside the copies of A among its Del; the
% role requires k.A (nrs_req), deletes j copies, and its plain form keeps
% the copies deleted (plain_mults).
Mult       ::= Atom ; times(Arg, Atom) ; rest(Expr, Expr, Atom).
Mults      ::= [] ; [Mult | Mults].
% A constraint is "a decidable condition on the values assigned to its value
% variables, written in the relations and functions the types of the values
% provide ... combined by the connectives" (def:numbers, GSC c8c5ead): true,
% and(C1, C2), or(C1, C2), not(C), implies(C1, C2); eq, ne, le, lt, ge and
% gt of two expressions, X = Y, X != Y, X =< Y, X < Y, X >= Y and X > Y, with
% succ(X, Y), Y = X + 1, as Currencies' GB.glp writes it; and rel(Name,
% Args), a relation a type provides.  An expression is a value argument,
% plus(X, Y), minus(X, Y), mul(X, Y), fn(Name, Args), a function a type
% provides, cardinality(Xs, H, A, Phi), "the number of instances of its
% anchor A at which phi holds, each counted as many times as its
% multiplicity", A held by H, or sum(Xs, H, A, Phi, U), "the sum of a numeric
% term u over the instances of its anchor A at which phi holds, each taken
% as many times as its multiplicity" (def:numbers, GSC 67a7da0): the domain
% is multisets, so k copies of an atom count k, and Xs may be empty, the one
% instance of A then having the multiplicity of A (def:extent).  A term with
% an agent in it is no numeric term (check.glp).  eq and ne also compare two
% agent variables, two speech-act variables or two name terms, u = v and
% u != v (def:numbers, GSC 6f0bda1).  "No condition reading a
% constraint" (the appendix, after def:binding-numbers), the checker reads
% one only where def:numbers has a schema's constraint imply a sum of deleted
% multiplicities (sas_implies_le).
% author_of(Y) and item_of(Y) are the author author(y), the first, innermost,
% signer of y, and the item item(y), the utterance under the signatures of y,
% and program(item_of(Y)) the decidable condition on that utterance that its
% type provides, named program as GSA's GPD.glp names it (def:numbers and def:binding-numbers
% at GSC 6df39d4: "the author author(y), the first signer of y, in an
% equality with an agent role or agent variable, the item item(y), the
% utterance under the signatures of y, in an equality with another, and a
% decidable condition on that utterance that its type provides, as that it is
% a grassroots contract with its schemas and pragmas"; GFP:1 and GFP:2, "the
% author of an item is its first signer").  Y is svar(Y), each variable listed
% in the head: eq(author_of(Y), U), U role(I) or pvar(X), either way round,
% eq(item_of(Y), item_of(Y1)), and ne of each, its negation, the connectives
% combining them; any other Y is signing_not_speech_act(Schema, Y), and
% author_of and item_of anywhere else in a constraint, or program on what is no item,
% constraint_not_numeric (check.glp).  No condition reads them (the appendix,
% after def:binding-numbers), so the checker takes each as true, as it takes a
% signing condition.  item_of(Y) is also an argument of an atom (def:numbers
% at GSC 4401dd6: "an argument of an atom may be a value or a value variable,
% or the item item(y) of a speech-act variable y of the schema that an agent
% role requires, the utterance under the signatures of y, which names no
% agent"), item_of(svar(Y)) in the checker's form (Arg, below): Y not svar(Y)
% is signing_not_speech_act(Schema, Y), and Y in no atom an agent role
% requires item_argument(Schema, Y) (check.glp, item_schemas).
% signed(U, Y) and unsigned(U, Y) are the signing conditions signed(u, y) and unsigned(u, y), u an agent role or agent variable and y a speech-act variable of the schema (def:numbers, GSC 10fcc92): U is role(I), I an agent role of the schema, or pvar(X), and Y is svar(Y), each variable listed in the head; any other U is a fault signing_not_agent(Schema, U) and any other Y a fault signing_not_speech_act(Schema, Y) (check.glp).  The conditions of def:syntactically-grassroots read no signing condition (the appendix, after def:binding-numbers), so the checker takes each as true.
Constraint ::= true ; and(Constraint, Constraint)
             ; eq(Expr, Expr) ; le(Expr, Expr) ; lt(Expr, Expr)
             ; ge(Expr, Expr) ; gt(Expr, Expr) ; succ(Arg, Arg)
             ; or(Constraint, Constraint) ; not(Constraint)
             ; implies(Constraint, Constraint)
             ; ne(Expr, Expr) ; rel(Constant, Exprs)
             ; signed(Arg, Arg) ; unsigned(Arg, Arg)
             ; program(Expr).
Constraints ::= [] ; [Constraint | Constraints].
Expr       ::= Arg ; plus(Expr, Expr) ; minus(Expr, Expr) ; mul(Expr, Expr)
             ; fn(Constant, Exprs) ; cardinality(Args, Arg, Atom, Form)
             ; sum(Args, Arg, Atom, Form, Expr)
             ; author_of(Arg).
Exprs      ::= [] ; [Expr | Exprs].
% A safe formula (def:role, GSC c8c5ead), built from atoms and constraints by
% the connectives and the anchored quantifiers: fa(H, M) the atom or
% multiplicity M held by H, fnot, fand and for; fexists(Xs, H, A, Phi) the
% formula exists Xs (A and Phi), A held by H, and fforall(Xs, H, A, Phi, Psi)
% the formula forall Xs (A and Phi -> Psi), Psi the conjunction of a list;
% and fcons(C) a constraint.  The conditions read none of it (def:schema,
% "conditions on the agents' states, which the denotation reads and the
% three conditions read only as stated"); the notation and the compiler
% print it.
Form       ::= fa(Arg, Mult) ; fnot(Form) ; fand(Form, Form) ; for(Form, Form)
             ; fexists(Args, Arg, Atom, Form)
             ; fforall(Args, Arg, Atom, Form, Forms)
             ; fcons(Constraint).
Forms      ::= [] ; [Form | Forms].
% A schema's constraint, and the value variables it uses as multiplicities,
% which a binding sends to positive whole numbers (def:binding-numbers).
NumCtx     ::= nc(Constraint, Args).

% The base of an argument, of a name term and of a role (def:role,
% def:grounded).
% A value argument names no agent, and its base, b_num, is the base of no
% role (GSC, Section 3.2); prov.glp and volition.glp pass it by.
% The wildcard is no agent role, variable or name term, and has no base
% either (def:grounded, def:schema), b_any; it occurs only in a cleared
% atom, which no condition reads.
Base  ::= b_role(Integer) ; b_pvar(Constant) ; b_svar(Constant) ; b_num ; b_any.
Bases ::= [] ; [Base | Bases].

% rs(Guard, Add, Del, Keep, Forb) holds an agent role's four multisets in the
% order +(i), -(i), =(i), not(i); Guard records the mark ?.
% crs(Kind, Guard, Add, Del, Keep, Forb) is the same for a listed role
% (def:role), and a listed role in the guard is a guarding role, every member
% of its extent then a guard (def:schema; Definition Denotation).
% listed(I, Rho, Args) is the listed role pi_I[rho(*, u_2, ..., u_r)] of the
% agent role pi_I, the role of a conjunct quantifying one variable, the
% second argument of its condition, with no constraint on it (GSC 8064cfb);
% any other is qlisted(I, Rho, Args, Xs), the listed role bound by Xs in its
% anchor rho(pi_I, Args), written pi_I[A] with the bound variables replaced
% by _ in A (def:role).
Guard     ::= guarded ; unguarded.
RoleKind  ::= listed(Integer, Constant, Args)
            ; qlisted(Integer, Constant, Args, Args).
RoleSpec  ::= rs(Guard, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms)
            ; crs(RoleKind, Guard, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms, Atoms).
RoleSpecs ::= [] ; [RoleSpec | RoleSpecs].

% A schema with a listed role may be written cschema(Name, Vars, [], Roles),
% as the owners' contracts write close: its third argument is the empty
% list, where reach conditions stood until GSC f3c4f43 removed them.  A
% schema's second argument is its variables, pvar(X) and svar(Y), in the
% order of its head (def:schema, GSC 0228e79).
% A quantified conjunct of the head, forall Xs (A and Phi -> L_1, ..., L_m)
% (def:role): conjunct(Xs, I, A, Phi, Add, Del, Lits), I the index of the
% agent role holding the anchor A, A written without its holder, Add and Del
% its conditional literals (def:schema), each hm(J, M) the atom M at the agent
% role J, and Lits all its literals, for the printer.  A listed role's
% literals are in its crs as well; a conditional literal is in none of the
% five multisets.  A schema whose quantifiers are all listed/3's conjuncts is
% written as it was; any other is qschema(Name, Vars, Bound, Constraint,
% Roles, Conjuncts, Forms), which the reader of the clause syntax alone
% writes, Bound the variables its quantifiers bind and Forms the safe
% formulas of its body, a body conjunct among them.
HMult     ::= hm(Integer, Mult).
HMults    ::= [] ; [HMult | HMults].
Conjunct  ::= conjunct(Args, Integer, Atom, Form, HMults, HMults, Forms).
Conjuncts ::= [] ; [Conjunct | Conjuncts].
Nil       ::= [].
Schema    ::= schema(Constant, Args, RoleSpecs)
            ; cschema(Constant, Args, Nil, RoleSpecs)
            ; qschema(Constant, Args, Args, Constraint, RoleSpecs, Conjuncts, Forms).
Contract  ::= [] ; [Schema | Contract].

% A contract may declare predicates of arity one reflexive (GAI's appendix
% "Contracts with Wards", "Reflexive predicates"); one that does is written
% reflexive(Preds, Schemas), and one that does not is the list of its
% schemas.
Declared  ::= Contract ; reflexive(Preds, Contract).

% The contract as written, with the values speech-act schemas allow: a role's
% four multisets may carry multiplicities, which def:numbers admits on an
% atom of the head or the body with no wildcard, the role forbidding that
% many copies where the atom is negated in the body, and a schema may be
% written nschema, with a constraint.  A contract with no number is of these
% types as it is of the plain ones.
NRoleSpec  ::= rs(Guard, Mults, Mults, Mults, Mults)
             ; crs(RoleKind, Guard, Mults, Mults, Mults, Mults).
NRoleSpecs ::= [] ; [NRoleSpec | NRoleSpecs].
NSchema    ::= schema(Constant, Args, NRoleSpecs)
             ; cschema(Constant, Args, Nil, NRoleSpecs)
             ; nschema(Constant, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs)
             ; qschema(Constant, Args, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs, Conjuncts, Forms).
NContract  ::= [] ; [NSchema | NContract].
NDeclared  ::= NContract ; reflexive(Preds, NContract).

% The contract as its owner writes it (GSC 25b6b3c, Section 2: "A name in a
% pragma is the schema's role of that name, the schemas naming their roles as
% the clauses do"; GKK.glp, GSG.glp and GSN.glp at GLP ec7c578c): a schema's
% head lists its roles by the clause's names, schema(Name, Names, Vars,
% Roles), cschema(Name, Names, Vars, [], Roles) and nschema(Name, Names, Vars,
% Constraint, Roles), Names the names of its roles in order, the name at a
% listed role's place not read (as_read names a listed role of the clause
% syntax by the variable its quantifier binds, GSC 7324ec7); a schema
% written without them, as the owners' contracts
% not yet rewritten write it, is read as before.  A contract may name its
% environment predicates (GSC 25b6b3c, Section 3.2 and the appendix "Values
% in Speech-Act Schemas": "whose atoms are over values, which the machine holds from
% startup and the platform keeps current, and which no schema adds or
% deletes"), environment(Preds, Body), Body the contract with or without its
% reflexive predicates.  The checker, the compiler to VMAT and the printer
% read it through unnamed/2, which drops the names and the environment
% predicates, and env_preds/2, which gives the environment predicates; the
% printer prints each role by its name (notation.glp).
% A name in the head is a role's name, or one(Name, Other), the role Name
% possibly the person of the role Other (GSC 316d875, Section 2: "a clause
% that admits one person in both writes 'Alice and Bob, possibly one
% person'; the schema's head writes the second name as one('Bob', 'Alice')").
RName     ::= Constant ; one(Constant, Constant).
Names      ::= [] ; [RName | Names].
RChunks     ::= [] ; [RName | RChunks].
% The clause syntax (GSC 859a007, Sections 3.1 and 3.2, Definitions Name
% term, role, Speech-act schema and Schema with values), as GSC #11 Cowork
% settled its term (Code inbox, 2026-11-04 19:57 UTC and 2026-11-05 06:28
% UTC): sas(Name, Names, Vars, Head, Body, Constraint, Guards), the schema
% tau: H <- B, gamma guarded by G.  Names is every agent variable of the
% schema in order, written one(Name, Other) where its clause admits the two
% as one person, a bound variable holding an atom being among them or read as
% if it stood after them (sas_names); Vars is every variable of the schema that no conjunct
% quantifies and that is no role, its agent variables, its speech-act
% variables and its value variables (def:schema, "its variables";
% def:numbers); Head is its literals, an atom atom(Pred, [Holder|Args]) or
% not(Atom), and its quantified conjuncts forall(Xs, A, Phi, Lits), the
% conjunct forall Xs (A and Phi -> Lits) of def:role, Xs bound variables of
% any kind, an agent variable being among Names or holding an atom, a value
% variable written num(X) and any other a speech-act variable; Body is its literals and its
% safe formulas, built from atoms and constraints by and(F, G), or(F, G),
% not(F), exists(Xs, A, Phi) and forall(Xs, A, Phi, Psi), Psi a list of
% literals or any safe formula; forall(X, A, Lits) is forall([X], A, true,
% Lits); a multiplicity is times(K, Atom) (def:numbers), in not(...) of Body
% that many copies forbidden; Constraint is gamma, true where the schema has
% none, in which cardinality(Xs, A, Phi) is a whole number and sum(Xs, A,
% Phi, U) a value of a numeric type, U a numeric term under the binders Xs;
% Guards the names of its guards.  An argument is a name
% or a variable of Vars, a constant either way, own(Name) for <Name>,
% ext(Sigma, Y) for Sigma.y, the wildcard the constant '_' and
% ext(Sigma, '_') for Sigma._, a value num(X), and a signed term sgn(Y,
% Name).  A constant is read by =?= against Names and Vars, and its
% constant taken from there (sas_bare below).
SNT    ::= own(Constant) ; ext(SNT, Constant).
SArg   ::= Constant ; own(Constant) ; ext(SNT, Constant) ; num(Constant)
         ; real(Constant) ; sgn(Constant, Constant) ; item_of(Constant).
SArgs  ::= [] ; [SArg | SArgs].
SAtom  ::= atom(Constant, SArgs).
SAtoms ::= [] ; [SAtom | SAtoms].
SMult  ::= SAtom ; times(SArg, SAtom).
SQLit  ::= SMult ; not(SMult).
SQLits ::= [] ; [SQLit | SQLits].
SExpr  ::= SArg ; plus(SExpr, SExpr) ; minus(SExpr, SExpr) ; mul(SExpr, SExpr)
         ; fn(Constant, SExprs) ; cardinality(PNames, SAtom, SConstraint)
         ; sum(PNames, SAtom, SConstraint, SExpr) ; author_of(Constant).
SExprs ::= [] ; [SExpr | SExprs].
% A safe formula and a constraint are one type, a constraint being a safe
% formula with no atom and no quantifier.
SConstraint ::= true ; and(SConstraint, SConstraint)
              ; eq(SExpr, SExpr) ; le(SExpr, SExpr) ; lt(SExpr, SExpr)
              ; ge(SExpr, SExpr) ; gt(SExpr, SExpr) ; succ(SArg, SArg)
              ; or(SConstraint, SConstraint) ; not(SConstraint)
              ; implies(SConstraint, SConstraint)
              ; ne(SExpr, SExpr) ; rel(Constant, SExprs)
              ; signed(SArg, SArg) ; unsigned(SArg, SArg) ; program(SExpr)
              ; atom(Constant, SArgs) ; times(SArg, SAtom)
              ; exists(PNames, SAtom, SConstraint)
              ; forall(PNames, SAtom, SConstraint, SConstraint)
              ; forall(Constant, SAtom, SQLits)
              ; [] ; [SConstraint | SLits].
SLits  ::= [] ; [SConstraint | SLits].
PNames ::= [] ; [Constant | PNames].
WSchema    ::= schema(Constant, Args, NRoleSpecs)
             ; cschema(Constant, Args, Nil, NRoleSpecs)
             ; nschema(Constant, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs)
             ; schema(Constant, Names, Args, NRoleSpecs)
             ; cschema(Constant, Names, Args, Nil, NRoleSpecs)
             ; nschema(Constant, Names, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs)
             ; qschema(Constant, Args, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs, Conjuncts, Forms)
             ; qschema(Constant, Names, Args, Args, Constraint, NRoleSpecs, Conjuncts, Forms)
             ; SSchema.
WContract  ::= [] ; [WSchema | WContract].
% The clause syntax's own types, which every contract's NAME.glp declares its
% term by and declares no copy of (GSC #13, 2026-11-09, by claude.md's rule
% against duplicating content): a schema sas(Name, Names, Vars, Head, Body,
% Constraint, Guards), a contract the list of its schemas, and a contract
% declared with its reflexive or its environment predicates.  A contract
% under programs/gsc sees them by its directory's self.glp.
SSchema    ::= sas(Constant, Names, PNames, SLits, SLits, SConstraint, PNames).
SContract  ::= [] ; [SSchema | SContract].
SDeclared  ::= SContract ; reflexive(Preds, SContract)
             ; environment(Preds, SContract).
WBody      ::= WContract ; reflexive(Preds, WContract).
WDeclared  ::= WBody ; environment(Preds, WBody).

% The contract as the checker reads it, its names and environment predicates
% dropped.
procedure unnamed(WDeclared?, NDeclared).
unnamed([], []).
unnamed([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c([S?|Ss?], C).
unnamed(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c(Ss?, C).
unnamed(environment(_, B), D?) :- ground(B?) | unnamed_b(B?, D).
procedure unnamed_b(WBody?, NDeclared).
unnamed_b([], []).
unnamed_b([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c([S?|Ss?], C).
unnamed_b(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Ss?) | unnamed_c(Ss?, C).
procedure unnamed_c(WContract?, NContract).
unnamed_c([], []).
unnamed_c([S|Ss], [S1?|Ss1?]) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    unnamed_s(S?, S1),
    unnamed_c(Ss?, Ss1).
procedure unnamed_s(WSchema?, NSchema).
unnamed_s(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(cschema(Nm, Vs, X, Rs), cschema(Nm?, Vs?, X?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(nschema(Nm, Vs, Cn, Rs), nschema(Nm?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(schema(Nm, _, Vs, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(cschema(Nm, _, Vs, X, Rs), cschema(Nm?, Vs?, X?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(nschema(Nm, _, Vs, Cn, Rs), nschema(Nm?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)).
unnamed_s(qschema(Nm, Vs, Bd, Cn, Rs, Cj, Fs), qschema(Nm?, Vs?, Bd?, Cn?, Rs?, Cj?, Fs?)).
unnamed_s(qschema(Nm, _, Vs, Bd, Cn, Rs, Cj, Fs), qschema(Nm?, Vs?, Bd?, Cn?, Rs?, Cj?, Fs?)).
unnamed_s(sas(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G), S?) :-
    ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?), ground(Vs?), ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?), ground(G?) |
    sas_schema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, H?, B?, Cn?, G?, S).
% The names of a schema's roles in order, for the printer (notation.glp):
% nm(Name) for a role its schema names, dflt for one it does not --- each
% role of a schema written without names, and a listed role of one written
% schema(Name, Names, Vars, Roles), which names it by its base.
NameOf  ::= nm(RName) ; dflt.
NameOfs ::= [] ; [NameOf | NameOfs].
procedure wsch_rnames(WSchema?, NameOfs).
wsch_rnames(schema(_, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(nschema(_, _, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(schema(_, Ns, _, Rs), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(cschema(_, Ns, _, _, Rs), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(nschema(_, Ns, _, _, Rs), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, _, _), []).
wsch_rnames(qschema(_, Ns, _, _, _, Rs, _, _), R?) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
wsch_rnames(sas(_, Ns, _, H, B, Cn, G), R?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?), ground(G?) |
    sas_ana(H?, B?, Cn?, S),
    sas_table_of(Ns?, S?, G?, E),
    sas_rnames(E?, R).
procedure old_rnames(Names?, NRoleSpecs?, NameOfs).
old_rnames(_, [], []).
old_rnames([], [_|Rs], [dflt|R?]) :- old_rnames([], Rs?, R).
old_rnames([N|Ns], [rs(_, _, _, _, _)|Rs], [nm(N?)|R?]) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
old_rnames([_|Ns], [crs(_, _, _, _, _, _)|Rs], [dflt|R?]) :- old_rnames(Ns?, Rs?, R).
% The environment predicates a contract names, [] where it names none.
procedure env_preds(WDeclared?, Preds).
env_preds([], []).
env_preds([_|_], []).
env_preds(reflexive(_, _), []).
env_preds(environment(Ps, _), Ps?).

% --- Reading the clause syntax (GSC 859a007, def:role, def:schema, def:numbers)
% sas_schema reads sas(Name, Names, Vars, Head, Body, Constraint, Guards)
% into the form the checker decides.  Its roles are numbered in the order of
% Names (def:role, GSC c8c5ead): a name no quantifier binds that holds an atom
% or is a guard is an agent role, a bound name that holds an atom a listed
% role, and any other an agent variable, of the schema (av) or bound (qv).
% An agent role pi_i has +(i) the atoms of Head outside its conjuncts with
% holder pi_i, -(i) and the cleared atoms _(i) those negated there, =(i) the
% atoms of Body with holder pi_i and not(i) those negated there; a listed
% role reads the same off the literals it holds in the conclusions of the
% quantified conjuncts of Head and Body that bind it (def:schema), its kind
% off the anchor of a quantifier binding it.  A literal an agent role holds
% in a conjunct of Head is conditional, in none of the five multisets
% (def:schema), and goes to the schema's conjunct/7; the safe formulas of
% Body, a conjunct among them, go to its Forms, which no condition reads.
% A safe formula written in the place of the constraint is read as a
% formula of the body.  Definition
% Speech-act schema requires -(i) a subset of =(i), and the checker's form
% holds =(i) less -(i), its role requiring the two together (nrs_req), so
% Keep is =(i) less -(i), a copy for each copy deleted (sas_minus).  Each
% atom is written without its holder (def:schema: "Each such atom is
% written without its holder").  The variables of the checker's form are
% Vars in order, an agent variable pvar(X), a value variable --- one the
% schema writes num(X) --- num(X), and any other svar(X).

% Whether a constant is the name N, one(N, Other) being N.
procedure(X) sas_nameq(X?, RName?, Ans).
sas_nameq(X, one(M, _), yes) :- X? =?= M? | true.
sas_nameq(X, M, yes) :- otherwise, X? =?= M? | true.
sas_nameq(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure(X) sas_in_names(X?, Names?, Ans).
sas_in_names(_, [], no).
sas_in_names(X, [N|Ns], R?) :- ground(X?), ground(N?), ground(Ns?) |
    sas_nameq(X?, N?, A),
    sas_in_names1(A?, X?, Ns?, R).

procedure(X) sas_in_names1(Ans?, X?, Names?, Ans).
sas_in_names1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_in_names1(no, X, Ns, R?) :- sas_in_names(X?, Ns?, R).

% A variable of Vars, by =?=, and its constant.
VFound ::= vfound(Constant) ; vnone.
procedure(X) sas_var(X?, PNames?, VFound).
sas_var(_, [], vnone).
sas_var(X, [V|_], vfound(V?)) :- X? =?= V? | true.
sas_var(X, [_|Vs], R?) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | sas_var(X?, Vs?, R).

procedure sas_in(Constant?, PNames?, Ans).
sas_in(_, [], no).
sas_in(X, [Y|_], yes) :- X? =?= Y? | true.
sas_in(X, [_|Ys], R?) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | sas_in(X?, Ys?, R).

procedure sas_qapp(SQLits?, SQLits?, SQLits).
sas_qapp([], T, T?).
sas_qapp([L|Ls], T, [L?|R?]) :- sas_qapp(Ls?, T?, R).

procedure sas_aapp(SAtoms?, SAtoms?, SAtoms).
sas_aapp([], T, T?).
sas_aapp([A|As], T, [A?|R?]) :- sas_aapp(As?, T?, R).

% The literals of a list, its quantified conjuncts q(Xs, A, Phi, Lits), and
% its other safe formulas.
Quant  ::= q(PNames, SAtom, SConstraint, SQLits).
Quants ::= [] ; [Quant | Quants].
procedure sas_quapp(Quants?, Quants?, Quants).
sas_quapp([], T, T?).
sas_quapp([Q|Qs], T, [Q?|R?]) :- sas_quapp(Qs?, T?, R).

procedure sas_split(SLits?, SQLits, Quants, SLits).
sas_split([], [], [], []).
sas_split([atom(F, As)|Ls], [atom(F?, As?)|P?], Q?, R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, Q, R).
sas_split([times(K, A)|Ls], [times(K?, A?)|P?], Q?, R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, Q, R).
sas_split([not(atom(F, As))|Ls], [not(atom(F?, As?))|P?], Q?, R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, Q, R).
sas_split([not(times(K, A))|Ls], [not(times(K?, A?))|P?], Q?, R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, Q, R).
sas_split([forall(X, C, L)|Ls], P?, [q([X?], C?, true, L?)|Q?], R?) :- sas_split(Ls?, P, Q, R).
sas_split([forall(Xs, C, Phi, Psi)|Ls], P?, Q?, R?) :-
    ground(Xs?), ground(C?), ground(Phi?), ground(Psi?) |
    sas_conc(Psi?, A),
    sas_split(Ls?, P, Q1, R1),
    sas_split1(A?, forall(Xs?, C?, Phi?, Psi?), Xs?, C?, Phi?, Q1?, R1?, Q, R).
sas_split([F|Ls], P?, Q?, [F?|R?]) :- otherwise | sas_split(Ls?, P, Q, R).

procedure sas_split1(Conc?, SConstraint?, PNames?, SAtom?, SConstraint?, Quants?, SLits?, Quants, SLits).
sas_split1(clits(L), _, Xs, C, Phi, Q, R, [q(Xs?, C?, Phi?, L?)|Q?], R?).
sas_split1(cnone, F, _, _, _, Q, R, Q?, [F?|R?]).

% The conclusion of a quantifier as a conjunction of literals (def:role, a
% quantified conjunct), if it is one.
Conc ::= clits(SQLits) ; cnone.
procedure sas_conc(SConstraint?, Conc).
sas_conc([], clits([])).
sas_conc([L|Ls], R?) :- sas_conc(L?, A), sas_conc(Ls?, B), sas_conc2(A?, B?, R).
sas_conc(atom(F, As), clits([atom(F?, As?)])).
sas_conc(times(K, A), clits([times(K?, A?)])).
sas_conc(not(atom(F, As)), clits([not(atom(F?, As?))])).
sas_conc(not(times(K, A)), clits([not(times(K?, A?))])).
sas_conc(and(A, B), R?) :- sas_conc(A?, X), sas_conc(B?, Y), sas_conc2(X?, Y?, R).
sas_conc(_, cnone) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_conc2(Conc?, Conc?, Conc).
sas_conc2(clits(A), clits(B), clits(R?)) :- sas_qapp(A?, B?, R).
sas_conc2(_, _, cnone) :- otherwise | true.

% A constraint is a safe formula with no atom and no quantifier.
procedure sas_pure(SConstraint?, Ans).
sas_pure(and(A, B), R?) :- sas_pure(A?, X), sas_pure(B?, Y), both_yes(X?, Y?, R).
sas_pure(or(A, B), R?) :- sas_pure(A?, X), sas_pure(B?, Y), both_yes(X?, Y?, R).
sas_pure(implies(A, B), R?) :- sas_pure(A?, X), sas_pure(B?, Y), both_yes(X?, Y?, R).
sas_pure(not(A), R?) :- sas_pure(A?, R).
sas_pure(atom(_, _), no).
sas_pure(times(_, _), no).
sas_pure(exists(_, _, _), no).
sas_pure(forall(_, _, _, _), no).
sas_pure(forall(_, _, _), no).
sas_pure([], no).
sas_pure([_|_], no).
sas_pure(_, yes) :- otherwise | true.

% The binders of a schema, bnd(Xs, A) for a quantifier, a cardinality or a sum; and
% what a walk over its literals and formulas collects: its atoms, anchors
% among them, its binders, its leaves that are constraints, and its
% multiplicities.
Bnd   ::= bnd(PNames, SAtom).
Bnds  ::= [] ; [Bnd | Bnds].
SW    ::= sw(SAtoms, Bnds, SLits, SArgs).

procedure sas_walk(SConstraint?, SW?, SW).
sas_walk(true, W, W?).
sas_walk(atom(P, As), sw(A, B, C, K), sw([atom(P?, As?)|A?], B?, C?, K?)).
sas_walk(times(K0, At), sw(A, B, C, K), sw([At?|A?], B?, C?, [K0?|K?])).
sas_walk(not(X), W, R?) :- sas_walk(X?, W?, R).
sas_walk(and(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk(X?, W?, W1), sas_walk(Y?, W1?, R).
sas_walk(or(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk(X?, W?, W1), sas_walk(Y?, W1?, R).
sas_walk(implies(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk(X?, W?, W1), sas_walk(Y?, W1?, R).
sas_walk(exists(Xs, At, Phi), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(At?) |
    sas_walk(Phi?, sw([At?|A?], [bnd(Xs?, At?)|B?], C?, K?), R).
sas_walk(forall(Xs, At, Phi, Psi), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(At?) |
    sas_walk(Phi?, sw([At?|A?], [bnd(Xs?, At?)|B?], C?, K?), W1),
    sas_walk(Psi?, W1?, R).
sas_walk(forall(X, At, Ls), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(At?) |
    sas_walk_lits(Ls?, sw([At?|A?], [bnd([X?], At?)|B?], C?, K?), R).
sas_walk([], W, W?).
sas_walk([L|Ls], W, R?) :- sas_walk(L?, W?, W1), sas_walk(Ls?, W1?, R).
sas_walk(eq(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], sw(A?, B?, [eq(X?, Y?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(ne(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], sw(A?, B?, [ne(X?, Y?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(le(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], sw(A?, B?, [le(X?, Y?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(lt(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], sw(A?, B?, [lt(X?, Y?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(ge(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], sw(A?, B?, [ge(X?, Y?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(gt(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], sw(A?, B?, [gt(X?, Y?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(rel(N, Xs), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Xs?) |
    sas_walk_xs(Xs?, sw(A?, B?, [rel(N?, Xs?)|C?], K?), R).
sas_walk(succ(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), sw(A?, B?, [succ(X?, Y?)|C?], K?)).
sas_walk(signed(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), sw(A?, B?, [signed(X?, Y?)|C?], K?)).
sas_walk(unsigned(X, Y), sw(A, B, C, K), sw(A?, B?, [unsigned(X?, Y?)|C?], K?)).
sas_walk(program(X), sw(A, B, C, K), sw(A?, B?, [program(X?)|C?], K?)).

procedure sas_walk_lits(SQLits?, SW?, SW).
sas_walk_lits([], W, W?).
sas_walk_lits([atom(P, As)|Ls], W, R?) :- sas_walk(atom(P?, As?), W?, W1), sas_walk_lits(Ls?, W1?, R).
sas_walk_lits([times(K, A)|Ls], W, R?) :- sas_walk(times(K?, A?), W?, W1), sas_walk_lits(Ls?, W1?, R).
sas_walk_lits([not(M)|Ls], W, R?) :- sas_walk_mult(M?, W?, W1), sas_walk_lits(Ls?, W1?, R).

procedure sas_walk_mult(SMult?, SW?, SW).
sas_walk_mult(atom(P, As), W, R?) :- sas_walk(atom(P?, As?), W?, R).
sas_walk_mult(times(K, A), W, R?) :- sas_walk(times(K?, A?), W?, R).

procedure sas_walk_xs(SExprs?, SW?, SW).
sas_walk_xs([], W, W?).
sas_walk_xs([X|Xs], W, R?) :- sas_walk_x(X?, W?, W1), sas_walk_xs(Xs?, W1?, R).

procedure sas_walk_x(SExpr?, SW?, SW).
sas_walk_x(plus(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_walk_x(minus(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_walk_x(mul(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_walk_x(fn(_, Xs), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs(Xs?, W?, R).
sas_walk_x(cardinality(Xs, At, Phi), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(At?) |
    sas_walk(Phi?, sw([At?|A?], [bnd(Xs?, At?)|B?], C?, K?), R).
sas_walk_x(sum(Xs, At, Phi, U), sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(At?) |
    sas_walk(Phi?, sw([At?|A?], [bnd(Xs?, At?)|B?], C?, K?), W1),
    sas_walk_x(U?, W1?, R).
sas_walk_x(_, W, W?) :- otherwise | true.

% The quantified conjuncts, walked.
procedure sas_walk_qs(Quants?, SW?, SW).
sas_walk_qs([], W, W?).
sas_walk_qs([q(Xs, At, Phi, L)|Qs], sw(A, B, C, K), R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(At?) |
    sas_walk(Phi?, sw([At?|A?], [bnd(Xs?, At?)|B?], C?, K?), W1),
    sas_walk_lits(L?, W1?, W2),
    sas_walk_qs(Qs?, W2?, R).

% A schema analysed: the literals, conjuncts and other formulas of its head
% and of its body, its constraint, its plain literals, the atoms and the
% constraints of its conjuncts and formulas, and its atoms, binders,
% constraints and multiplicities, all of them.
SA ::= sa(SQLits, Quants, SLits, SQLits, Quants, SLits, SConstraint, SQLits,
          SAtoms, SLits, SAtoms, Bnds, SLits, SArgs).

procedure sas_ana(SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, SA).
sas_ana(H, B, Cn, R?) :- ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?) |
    sas_pure(Cn?, Pu),
    sas_ana1(Pu?, H?, B?, Cn?, R).

procedure sas_ana1(Ans?, SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, SA).
sas_ana1(yes, H, B, Cn, R?) :- sas_ana2(H?, B?, Cn?, R).
sas_ana1(no, H, B, Cn, R?) :- ground(B?), ground(Cn?) |
    sas_lapp(B?, Cn?, B1),
    sas_ana2(H?, B1?, true, R).

procedure sas_lapp(SLits?, SConstraint?, SLits).
sas_lapp([], X, [X?]).
sas_lapp([L|Ls], X, [L?|R?]) :- sas_lapp(Ls?, X?, R).

procedure sas_ana2(SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, SA).
sas_ana2(H, B, Cn, R?) :- ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?) |
    sas_split(H?, HP, HQ, HF),
    sas_split(B?, BP, BQ, BF),
    sas_ana3(HP?, HQ?, HF?, BP?, BQ?, BF?, Cn?, R).

procedure sas_ana3(SQLits?, Quants?, SLits?, SQLits?, Quants?, SLits?, SConstraint?, SA).
sas_ana3(HP, HQ, HF, BP, BQ, BF, Cn, sa(HP?, HQ?, HF?, BP?, BQ?, BF?, Cn?, PP?, AQ?, CQ?, AA?, Bs?, Cs?, Ks?)) :-
    ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(HF?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?), ground(BF?), ground(Cn?) |
    sas_qapp(HP?, BP?, PP),
    sas_walk_qs(HQ?, sw([], [], [], []), W1),
    sas_walk_qs(BQ?, W1?, W2),
    sas_walk(HF?, W2?, W3),
    sas_walk(BF?, W3?, W4),
    sas_ana4(W4?, Cn?, AQ, CQ, W5),
    sas_qapp(HP?, BP?, PP2),
    sas_walk_lits(PP2?, W5?, W6),
    sas_walk(Cn?, W6?, W7),
    sas_ana5(W7?, AA, Bs, Cs, Ks).

procedure sas_ana5(SW?, SAtoms, Bnds, SLits, SArgs).
sas_ana5(sw(A, B, C, K), A?, B?, C?, K?).

% AQ and CQ, the atoms and the constraints the faults of the reading ask of
% the formulas: those of the conjuncts and formulas, and those a cardinality
% or a sum of the constraint holds, an anchored safe formula as a
% quantifier's is (def:numbers).
procedure sas_ana4(SW?, SConstraint?, SAtoms, SLits, SW).
sas_ana4(sw(A, B, C, K), Cn, AQ?, CQ?, sw(A?, B?, C?, K?)) :- ground(A?), ground(C?) |
    sas_cons_x(Cn?, sw(A?, [], C?, []), W),
    sas_ana5(W?, AQ, _, CQ, _).

% What the cardinalities and sums of a constraint hold, the constraint itself
% left to sas_cons_vf.
procedure sas_cons_x(SConstraint?, SW?, SW).
sas_cons_x(and(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_cons_x(X?, W?, W1), sas_cons_x(Y?, W1?, R).
sas_cons_x(or(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_cons_x(X?, W?, W1), sas_cons_x(Y?, W1?, R).
sas_cons_x(implies(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_cons_x(X?, W?, W1), sas_cons_x(Y?, W1?, R).
sas_cons_x(not(X), W, R?) :- sas_cons_x(X?, W?, R).
sas_cons_x(eq(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_cons_x(ne(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_cons_x(le(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_cons_x(lt(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_cons_x(ge(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_cons_x(gt(X, Y), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs([X?, Y?], W?, R).
sas_cons_x(rel(_, Xs), W, R?) :- sas_walk_xs(Xs?, W?, R).
sas_cons_x(_, W, W?) :- otherwise | true.

% A literal's atom, its multiplicity and whether it is negated.
procedure sas_lit_atom(SQLit?, SAtom).
sas_lit_atom(atom(F, As), atom(F?, As?)).
sas_lit_atom(times(_, A), A?).
sas_lit_atom(not(atom(F, As)), atom(F?, As?)).
sas_lit_atom(not(times(_, A)), A?).

procedure sas_lit_mult(SQLit?, SMult).
sas_lit_mult(atom(F, As), atom(F?, As?)).
sas_lit_mult(times(K, A), times(K?, A?)).
sas_lit_mult(not(M), M?).

procedure sas_lit_neg(SQLit?, Ans).
sas_lit_neg(not(_), yes).
sas_lit_neg(atom(_, _), no).
sas_lit_neg(times(_, _), no).

procedure sas_pred(SAtom?, Constant).
sas_pred(atom(P, _), P?).

% Whether the name N is the holder of an atom.
procedure sas_atom_held(SAtom?, RName?, Ans).
sas_atom_held(atom(_, []), _, no).
sas_atom_held(atom(_, [H|_]), N, R?) :- sas_nameq(H?, N?, R).

procedure sas_lit_held(SQLit?, RName?, Ans).
sas_lit_held(L, N, R?) :- ground(L?) |
    sas_lit_atom(L?, A),
    sas_atom_held(A?, N?, R).

% Whether N holds some literal of a list, and whether some conjunct
% quantifies it.
procedure sas_holds(SQLits?, RName?, Ans).
sas_holds([], _, no).
sas_holds([L|Ls], N, R?) :- ground(Ls?), ground(N?) |
    sas_lit_held(L?, N?, A),
    sas_holds1(A?, Ls?, N?, R).

procedure sas_holds1(Ans?, SQLits?, RName?, Ans).
sas_holds1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_holds1(no, Ls, N, R?) :- sas_holds(Ls?, N?, R).

% Whether a binder binds N; whether N holds an atom of a list.
procedure sas_bound(Bnds?, RName?, Ans).
sas_bound([], _, no).
sas_bound([bnd(Xs, _)|Bs], N, R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(Bs?), ground(N?) |
    sas_ing(Xs?, N?, A),
    sas_bound1(A?, Bs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_bound1(Ans?, Bnds?, RName?, Ans).
sas_bound1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_bound1(no, Bs, N, R?) :- sas_bound(Bs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_aheld(SAtoms?, RName?, Ans).
sas_aheld([], _, no).
sas_aheld([A|As], N, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(N?) |
    sas_atom_held(A?, N?, H),
    sas_aheld1(H?, As?, N?, R).

procedure sas_aheld1(Ans?, SAtoms?, RName?, Ans).
sas_aheld1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_aheld1(no, As, N, R?) :- sas_aheld(As?, N?, R).

% The names of a schema: those it writes, then each bound variable holding an
% atom that it does not, a listed role whatever its head says (def:role; GSC
% #12, Code_inbox.md 2026-11-06 11:26 UTC: "inferring the bound variables is
% fine"), in the order of their binders.
procedure sas_names(Names?, SA?, Names).
sas_names(Ns, sa(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, AA, Bs, _, _), R?) :-
    ground(Ns?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?) |
    sas_bnds_rev(Bs?, [], Bs1),
    sas_qvars(Bs1?, [], Xs),
    sas_prev(Xs?, [], Xs1),
    sas_names1(Xs1?, AA?, Ns?, Ys),
    sas_names_app(Ns?, Ys?, R).

procedure sas_table_of(Names?, SA?, PNames?, REnts).
sas_table_of(Ns, A, G, E?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(A?), ground(G?) |
    sas_names(Ns?, A?, Ns1),
    sas_table(Ns1?, A?, G?, 1, E).

procedure sas_bnds_rev(Bnds?, Bnds?, Bnds).
sas_bnds_rev([], T, T?).
sas_bnds_rev([B|Bs], T, R?) :- sas_bnds_rev(Bs?, [B?|T?], R).

procedure sas_prev(PNames?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_prev([], T, T?).
sas_prev([X|Xs], T, R?) :- sas_prev(Xs?, [X?|T?], R).

procedure sas_names_app(Names?, Names?, Names).
sas_names_app([], T, T?).
sas_names_app([N|Ns], T, [N?|R?]) :- sas_names_app(Ns?, T?, R).

% The variables among Xs holding an atom and not among Ns.
procedure sas_names1(PNames?, SAtoms?, Names?, Names).
sas_names1([], _, _, []).
sas_names1([X|Xs], AA, Ns, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Xs?), ground(AA?), ground(Ns?) |
    sas_aheld(AA?, X?, H),
    sas_in_names(X?, Ns?, In),
    flip(In?, Out),
    both_yes(H?, Out?, A),
    sas_names1(Xs?, AA?, Ns?, R1),
    sas_names2(A?, X?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_names2(Ans?, Constant?, Names?, Names).
sas_names2(no, _, T, T?).
sas_names2(yes, X, T, [X?|T?]).

% The roles of a schema, numbered in the order of its names: ar(Name, I) an
% agent role, lr(Name, I) a listed role, av(Name) an agent variable of the
% schema and qv(Name) a bound one.
REnt  ::= ar(RName, Integer) ; lr(RName, Integer) ; av(RName) ; qv(RName).
REnts ::= [] ; [REnt | REnts].

procedure sas_table(Names?, SA?, PNames?, Integer?, REnts).
sas_table([], _, _, _, []).
sas_table([N|Ns], S, G, I, R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Ns?), ground(S?), ground(G?), integer(I?) |
    sas_tabn(S?, N?, G?, T),
    sas_table1(T?, N?, Ns?, S?, G?, I?, R).

TN ::= tn(Ans, Ans, Ans, Ans).
procedure sas_tabn(SA?, RName?, PNames?, TN).
sas_tabn(sa(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, PP, _, _, AA, Bs, _, _), N, G, tn(A?, Q?, H?, B?)) :-
    ground(PP?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?), ground(N?), ground(G?) |
    sas_holds(PP?, N?, A),
    sas_bound(Bs?, N?, Q),
    sas_aheld(AA?, N?, H),
    sas_aheld(AA?, N?, H2),
    sas_ing(G?, N?, Gi),
    or_yes(H2?, Gi?, B).

procedure sas_table1(TN?, RName?, Names?, SA?, PNames?, Integer?, REnts).
sas_table1(tn(yes, _, _, _), N, Ns, S, G, I, [ar(N?, I?)|R?]) :- integer(I?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    sas_table(Ns?, S?, G?, I1?, R).
sas_table1(tn(no, yes, yes, _), N, Ns, S, G, I, [lr(N?, I?)|R?]) :- integer(I?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    sas_table(Ns?, S?, G?, I1?, R).
sas_table1(tn(no, yes, no, _), N, Ns, S, G, I, [qv(N?)|R?]) :- sas_table(Ns?, S?, G?, I?, R).
sas_table1(tn(no, no, _, yes), N, Ns, S, G, I, [ar(N?, I?)|R?]) :- integer(I?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    sas_table(Ns?, S?, G?, I1?, R).
sas_table1(tn(no, no, _, no), N, Ns, S, G, I, [av(N?)|R?]) :- sas_table(Ns?, S?, G?, I?, R).

% The names of the roles, for the printer (wsch_rnames).
procedure sas_rnames(REnts?, NameOfs).
sas_rnames([], []).
sas_rnames([ar(N, _)|Es], [nm(N?)|R?]) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).
sas_rnames([lr(N, _)|Es], [nm(N?)|R?]) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).
sas_rnames([av(_)|Es], R?) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).
sas_rnames([qv(_)|Es], R?) :- sas_rnames(Es?, R).

Look ::= lrole(Integer) ; lvar ; lnone.
procedure(X) sas_look(X?, REnts?, Look).
sas_look(_, [], lnone).
sas_look(N, [ar(M, I)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lrole(I?), N?, Es?, R).
sas_look(N, [lr(M, I)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lrole(I?), N?, Es?, R).
sas_look(N, [av(M)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lvar, N?, Es?, R).
sas_look(N, [qv(M)|Es], R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Es?) |
    sas_nameq(N?, M?, A),
    sas_look1(A?, lvar, N?, Es?, R).

procedure(X) sas_look1(Ans?, Look?, X?, REnts?, Look).
sas_look1(yes, L, _, _, L?).
sas_look1(no, _, N, Es, R?) :- sas_look(N?, Es?, R).

procedure sas_index(Look?, Integer).
sas_index(lrole(I), I?).
sas_index(lvar, 0).
sas_index(lnone, 0).

% An argument (def:role, def:schema, def:numbers).  A constant is the
% wildcard, a role, an agent variable or another variable of Vars; one that
% is none of these is a fault of the reading, not_in_vars (sas_faults), and
% is read as the wildcard, which no condition reads.
procedure sas_arg(SArg?, REnts?, PNames?, Arg).
sas_arg(own(N), E, _, nterm(R?)) :- sas_nt(own(N?), E?, R).
sas_arg(ext(S, Y), E, _, nterm(R?)) :- sas_nt(ext(S?, Y?), E?, R).
sas_arg(num(X), _, _, any) :- X? =?= '_' | true.
sas_arg(num(X), _, _, num(X?)) :- otherwise | true.
% real(X) is the real value variable X, or the number X: a value argument
% as num(X) is, its type the head's (Arg, above).
sas_arg(real(X), _, _, any) :- X? =?= '_' | true.
sas_arg(real(X), _, _, num(X?)) :- otherwise | true.
sas_arg(sgn(Y, N), E, _, sgn(Y?, I?)) :-
    sas_look(N?, E?, L),
    sas_index(L?, I).
% item_of(Y), the item of Y, is an argument of an atom (def:numbers, GSC
% 4401dd6), item_of(svar(Y)), Y read as a bare argument is: check.glp asks
% that Y be a speech-act variable an agent role requires (item_schemas).
sas_arg(item_of(Y), E, V, item_of(R?)) :- sas_bare(Y?, E?, V?, R).
sas_arg(C, E, V, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare(C?, E?, V?, R).

procedure(X) sas_bare(X?, REnts?, PNames?, Arg).
sas_bare(C, _, _, any) :- C? =?= '_' | true.
sas_bare(C, E, V, R?) :- otherwise, ground(C?) |
    sas_look(C?, E?, L),
    sas_var(C?, V?, F),
    sas_bare1(L?, F?, R).

procedure sas_bare1(Look?, VFound?, Arg).
sas_bare1(lrole(I), _, role(I?)).
sas_bare1(lvar, vfound(X), pvar(X?)).
sas_bare1(lnone, vfound(X), svar(X?)).
sas_bare1(lvar, vnone, any).
sas_bare1(lnone, vnone, any).

procedure sas_nt(SNT?, REnts?, NameTerm).
sas_nt(own(N), E, R?) :- ground(N?) |
    sas_look(N?, E?, L),
    sas_own(L?, N?, R).
sas_nt(ext(S, Y), E, ext_any(R?)) :- Y? =?= '_' | sas_nt(S?, E?, R).
sas_nt(ext(S, Y), E, ext(R?, Y?)) :- otherwise | sas_nt(S?, E?, R).

procedure sas_own(Look?, Constant?, NameTerm).
sas_own(lrole(I), _, own(I?)).
sas_own(lvar, N, own_var(N?)).
sas_own(lnone, N, own_var(N?)).

procedure sas_args(SArgs?, REnts?, PNames?, Args).
sas_args([], _, _, []).
sas_args([A|As], E, V, [B?|Bs?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(A?, E?, V?, B),
    sas_args(As?, E?, V?, Bs).

% An atom with its holder dropped, and a multiplicity.
procedure sas_iatom(SAtom?, REnts?, PNames?, Atom).
sas_iatom(atom(P, [_|As]), E, V, atom(P?, R?)) :- sas_args(As?, E?, V?, R).
sas_iatom(atom(P, []), _, _, atom(P?, [])).

procedure sas_imult(SMult?, REnts?, PNames?, Mult).
sas_imult(atom(P, As), E, V, R?) :- sas_iatom(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, R).
sas_imult(times(K, A), E, V, times(K1?, A1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(K?, E?, V?, K1),
    sas_iatom(A?, E?, V?, A1).

% The constraint (def:numbers), its arguments read as an atom's are.
procedure sas_cons(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Constraint).
sas_cons(true, _, _, true).
sas_cons(and(A, B), E, V, and(A1?, B1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_cons(A?, E?, V?, A1), sas_cons(B?, E?, V?, B1).
sas_cons(or(A, B), E, V, or(A1?, B1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_cons(A?, E?, V?, A1), sas_cons(B?, E?, V?, B1).
sas_cons(not(A), E, V, not(A1?)) :- sas_cons(A?, E?, V?, A1).
sas_cons(implies(A, B), E, V, implies(A1?, B1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_cons(A?, E?, V?, A1), sas_cons(B?, E?, V?, B1).
sas_cons(rel(N, Xs), E, V, rel(N?, Xs1?)) :- sas_exprs(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1).
sas_cons(ne(X, Y), E, V, ne(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(eq(X, Y), E, V, eq(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(le(X, Y), E, V, le(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(lt(X, Y), E, V, lt(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(ge(X, Y), E, V, ge(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(gt(X, Y), E, V, gt(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(succ(X, Y), E, V, succ(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_arg(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(signed(X, Y), E, V, signed(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_arg(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(unsigned(X, Y), E, V, unsigned(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_arg(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_arg(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_cons(program(X), E, V, program(X1?)) :- sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1).
% An atom or a quantifier is no constraint: sas_ana moves a formula out of the
% place of the constraint, and sas_form reads what is above a constraint.
sas_cons(_, _, _, true) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_expr(SExpr?, REnts?, PNames?, Expr).
sas_expr(plus(X, Y), E, V, plus(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_expr(minus(X, Y), E, V, minus(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_expr(mul(X, Y), E, V, mul(X1?, Y1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1), sas_expr(Y?, E?, V?, Y1).
sas_expr(fn(N, Xs), E, V, fn(N?, Xs1?)) :- sas_exprs(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1).
sas_expr(cardinality(Xs, At, Phi), E, V, cardinality(Xs1?, H?, A?, F?)) :-
    ground(Xs?), ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_papp(Xs?, V?, V1),
    sas_card(Xs?, At?, Phi?, E?, V1?, Xs1, H, A, F).
sas_expr(sum(Xs, At, Phi, U), E, V, sum(Xs1?, H?, A?, F?, U1?)) :-
    ground(Xs?), ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_papp(Xs?, V?, V1),
    sas_sum(Xs?, At?, Phi?, U?, E?, V1?, Xs1, H, A, F, U1).
sas_expr(own(N), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(own(N?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(ext(S, Y), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(ext(S?, Y?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(num(X), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(num(X?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(real(X), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(real(X?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(sgn(Y, N), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(sgn(Y?, N?), E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(author_of(Y), E, V, author_of(R?)) :- sas_bare(Y?, E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(item_of(Y), E, V, item_of(R?)) :- sas_bare(Y?, E?, V?, R).
sas_expr(C, E, V, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare(C?, E?, V?, R).

% A cardinality's anchor and phi, V1 the variables with those it binds.
procedure sas_card(PNames?, SAtom?, SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Args, Arg, Atom, Form).
sas_card(Xs, At, Phi, E, V, Xs1?, H?, A?, F?) :- ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_bvars(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1),
    sas_aholder(At?, E?, V?, H),
    sas_iatom(At?, E?, V?, A),
    sas_form(Phi?, E?, V?, F).

% A sum's anchor, phi and term, V1 the variables with those it binds.
procedure sas_sum(PNames?, SAtom?, SConstraint?, SExpr?, REnts?, PNames?, Args, Arg, Atom, Form, Expr).
sas_sum(Xs, At, Phi, U, E, V, Xs1?, H?, A?, F?, U1?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_card(Xs?, At?, Phi?, E?, V?, Xs1, H, A, F),
    sas_expr(U?, E?, V?, U1).

procedure sas_exprs(SExprs?, REnts?, PNames?, Exprs).
sas_exprs([], _, _, []).
sas_exprs([X|Xs], E, V, [X1?|Xs1?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_expr(X?, E?, V?, X1),
    sas_exprs(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1).

% The value variables a schema writes, num(X) for X no number.
procedure sas_nums_arg(SArg?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_arg(num(X), T, T?) :- X? =?= '_' | true.
sas_nums_arg(num(X), T, [X?|T?]) :- otherwise | true.
sas_nums_arg(real(X), T, T?) :- X? =?= '_' | true.
sas_nums_arg(real(X), T, [X?|T?]) :- otherwise | true.
sas_nums_arg(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

% The value variables a schema writes as of one type, K num or real: those
% written num(X), and those written real(X) (Arg, above).
procedure sas_vk_arg(Constant?, SArg?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_arg(_, num(X), T, T?) :- X? =?= '_' | true.
sas_vk_arg(_, real(X), T, T?) :- X? =?= '_' | true.
sas_vk_arg(_, num(X), T, T?) :- number(X?) | true.
sas_vk_arg(_, real(X), T, T?) :- number(X?) | true.
sas_vk_arg(K, num(X), T, [X?|T?]) :- otherwise, K? =?= num | true.
sas_vk_arg(K, real(X), T, [X?|T?]) :- otherwise, K? =?= real | true.
sas_vk_arg(_, _, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_vk_args(Constant?, SArgs?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_args(_, [], T, T?).
sas_vk_args(K, [A|As], T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_args(K?, As?, T?, R1), sas_vk_arg(K?, A?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_vk_atoms(Constant?, SAtoms?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_atoms(_, [], T, T?).
sas_vk_atoms(K, [atom(_, As)|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_atoms(K?, Xs?, T?, R1), sas_vk_args(K?, As?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_vk_leaves(Constant?, SLits?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_leaves(_, [], T, T?).
sas_vk_leaves(K, [C|Cs], T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_leaves(K?, Cs?, T?, R1), sas_vk_cons(K?, C?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_vk_cons(Constant?, SConstraint?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_cons(K, eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, ne(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, le(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, lt(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, ge(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, gt(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, succ(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_arg(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_arg(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_cons(K, rel(_, Xs), T, R?) :- sas_vk_exprs(K?, Xs?, T?, R).
sas_vk_cons(_, _, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_vk_expr(Constant?, SExpr?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_expr(K, plus(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_expr(K, minus(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_expr(K, mul(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_expr(K?, Y?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).
sas_vk_expr(K, fn(_, Xs), T, R?) :- sas_vk_exprs(K?, Xs?, T?, R).
sas_vk_expr(K, sum(_, _, _, U), T, R?) :- sas_vk_expr(K?, U?, T?, R).
sas_vk_expr(K, num(X), T, R?) :- sas_vk_arg(K?, num(X?), T?, R).
sas_vk_expr(K, real(X), T, R?) :- sas_vk_arg(K?, real(X?), T?, R).
sas_vk_expr(_, _, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_vk_exprs(Constant?, SExprs?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_vk_exprs(_, [], T, T?).
sas_vk_exprs(K, [X|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(K?) | sas_vk_exprs(K?, Xs?, T?, R1), sas_vk_expr(K?, X?, R1?, R).

% The value variables a schema writes real(X), and those it writes num(X).
procedure sas_vk_of(Constant?, SA?, PNames).
sas_vk_of(K, sa(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, AA, _, Cs, Ks), R?) :- ground(K?), ground(AA?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?) |
    sas_vk3(K?, AA?, Cs?, Ks?, R).

procedure sas_vk3(Constant?, SAtoms?, SLits?, SArgs?, PNames).
sas_vk3(K, AA, Cs, Ks, R?) :- ground(K?), ground(AA?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?) |
    sas_vk_args(K?, Ks?, [], N1),
    sas_vk_atoms(K?, AA?, N1?, N2),
    sas_vk_leaves(K?, Cs?, N2?, R).

procedure sas_nums_args(SArgs?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_args([], T, T?).
sas_nums_args([A|As], T, R?) :- sas_nums_args(As?, T?, R1), sas_nums_arg(A?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_nums_atoms(SAtoms?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_atoms([], T, T?).
sas_nums_atoms([atom(_, As)|Xs], T, R?) :- sas_nums_atoms(Xs?, T?, R1), sas_nums_args(As?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_nums_leaves(SLits?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_leaves([], T, T?).
sas_nums_leaves([C|Cs], T, R?) :- sas_nums_leaves(Cs?, T?, R1), sas_nums_cons(C?, R1?, R).

% The value variables of a constraint's leaf; the walk gives the leaves, and
% a leaf is one of these.
procedure sas_nums_cons(SConstraint?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_cons(eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(ne(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(le(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(lt(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(ge(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(gt(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(succ(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_arg(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_arg(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_cons(rel(_, Xs), T, R?) :- sas_nums_exprs(Xs?, T?, R).
sas_nums_cons(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_nums_expr(SExpr?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_expr(plus(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_expr(minus(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_expr(mul(X, Y), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(Y?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).
sas_nums_expr(fn(_, Xs), T, R?) :- sas_nums_exprs(Xs?, T?, R).
sas_nums_expr(cardinality(_, _, _), T, T?).
sas_nums_expr(sum(_, _, _, U), T, R?) :- sas_nums_expr(U?, T?, R).
sas_nums_expr(num(X), T, R?) :- sas_nums_arg(num(X?), T?, R).
sas_nums_expr(real(X), T, R?) :- sas_nums_arg(real(X?), T?, R).
sas_nums_expr(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_nums_exprs(SExprs?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_nums_exprs([], T, T?).
sas_nums_exprs([X|Xs], T, R?) :- sas_nums_exprs(Xs?, T?, R1), sas_nums_expr(X?, R1?, R).

% The variables of the checker's form, Vars in order.
% The bound variables of a quantifier, for the printer: a role, an agent
% variable, or another (Bound, below, holds each kind of each).
procedure sas_bvars(PNames?, REnts?, PNames?, Args).
sas_bvars(Xs, E, _, R?) :- sas_vars(Xs?, E?, [], [], R).

% Each bound name as a variable of each kind: a value variable is known by
% being written num(X), which the bound list need not say.
procedure sas_bound_args(Bnds?, Args?, Args).
sas_bound_args([], T, T?).
sas_bound_args([bnd(Xs, _)|Bs], T, R?) :- sas_bound_args(Bs?, T?, R1), sas_bnames(Xs?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_bnames(PNames?, Args?, Args).
sas_bnames([], T, T?).
sas_bnames([X|Xs], T, [pvar(X?), svar(X?), num(X?)|R?]) :- ground(X?) | sas_bnames(Xs?, T?, R).

% Ns the value variables of the schema, and Rl those it writes real(X): a
% value variable is num(X), whole, or real(X), real (Arg, above).
procedure sas_vars(PNames?, REnts?, PNames?, PNames?, Args).
sas_vars([], _, _, _, []).
sas_vars([X|Xs], E, Ns, Rl, [A?|R?]) :- ground(X?), ground(E?), ground(Ns?), ground(Rl?) |
    sas_look(X?, E?, L),
    sas_in(X?, Ns?, N),
    sas_in(X?, Rl?, Q),
    sas_var_arg(L?, N?, Q?, X?, A),
    sas_vars(Xs?, E?, Ns?, Rl?, R).

procedure sas_var_arg(Look?, Ans?, Ans?, Constant?, Arg).
sas_var_arg(lrole(I), _, _, _, role(I?)).
sas_var_arg(lvar, _, _, X, pvar(X?)).
sas_var_arg(lnone, yes, no, X, num(X?)).
sas_var_arg(lnone, yes, yes, X, real(X?)).
sas_var_arg(lnone, no, _, X, svar(X?)).

% The literals of a list with holder N, the atoms and the negated ones, in
% order, each without its holder.
procedure sas_part(SQLits?, RName?, REnts?, PNames?, Mults, Mults).
sas_part([], _, _, _, [], []).
sas_part([L|Ls], N, E, V, P?, Q?) :- ground(L?), ground(N?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_lit_held(L?, N?, A),
    sas_lit_neg(L?, G),
    sas_lit_mult(L?, M),
    sas_part1(A?, G?, M?, Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).

procedure sas_part1(Ans?, Ans?, SMult?, SQLits?, RName?, REnts?, PNames?, Mults, Mults).
sas_part1(yes, no, M, Ls, N, E, V, [X?|P?], Q?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_imult(M?, E?, V?, X),
    sas_part(Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).
sas_part1(yes, yes, M, Ls, N, E, V, P?, [X?|Q?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_imult(M?, E?, V?, X),
    sas_part(Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).
sas_part1(no, _, _, Ls, N, E, V, P?, Q?) :- sas_part(Ls?, N?, E?, V?, P, Q).

% The literals of the conjuncts binding the name N.
procedure sas_qlits(Quants?, RName?, SQLits).
sas_qlits([], _, []).
sas_qlits([q(Xs, _, _, Q)|Qs], N, R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(N?), ground(Qs?) |
    sas_ing(Xs?, N?, A),
    sas_qlits1(A?, Q?, Qs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_qlits1(Ans?, SQLits?, Quants?, RName?, SQLits).
sas_qlits1(yes, Q, Qs, N, R?) :- sas_qlits(Qs?, N?, R1), sas_qapp(Q?, R1?, R).
sas_qlits1(no, _, Qs, N, R?) :- sas_qlits(Qs?, N?, R).

% The binders binding the name N.
procedure sas_over(Bnds?, RName?, Bnds).
sas_over([], _, []).
sas_over([bnd(Xs, C)|Bs], N, R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(C?), ground(N?), ground(Bs?) |
    sas_ing(Xs?, N?, A),
    sas_over1(A?, Xs?, C?, Bs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_over1(Ans?, PNames?, SAtom?, Bnds?, RName?, Bnds).
sas_over1(yes, Xs, C, Bs, N, [bnd(Xs?, C?)|R?]) :- sas_over(Bs?, N?, R).
sas_over1(no, _, _, Bs, N, R?) :- sas_over(Bs?, N?, R).

% =(i) less -(i), a copy for each copy deleted, and the atoms deleted that
% =(i) does not hold: an atom required k times and deleted j < k times,
% k and j numbers, leaves k - j copies (def:numbers: "kappa copies of
% phi"), and k = j leaves none; an atom required k times and deleted j
% times, k or j a value variable, leaves rest(k, j, A) where the schema's
% constraint implies j <= k, and is refused otherwise (def:numbers: "where
% an atom is required with multiplicity kappa and deleted with multiplicity
% kappa', the schema's constraint ensures kappa' <= kappa, so that -(i) is
% a subset of =(i) at every binding").  The constraint implies j <= k when
% no values satisfy it with j > k, each multiplicity a positive whole number
% (def:binding-numbers): sas_implies_le, decided exactly by linear.glp, and
% the schema is refused where the constraint is not linear (def:numbers:
% "the checker decides the implication where the constraint is linear over
% whole numbers, and refuses the schema otherwise").  "Deleted with
% multiplicities kappa_1, ..., kappa_n, the schema's constraint implies
% kappa_1 + ... + kappa_n <= kappa": the second cut takes rest(k, i, A) to
% rest(k, plus(i, j), A); and an atom required twice is merged (sas_merged)
% where a deletion needs its copies together, =(i) being a multiset.
Count ::= cnt(Constant, Atom) ; vcnt(Expr, Atom) ; rcnt(Expr, Expr, Atom) ; nocnt.
procedure sas_count(Mult?, Count).
sas_count(atom(P, As), cnt(1, atom(P?, As?))).
sas_count(times(num(K), A), cnt(K?, A?)) :- number(K?) | true.
sas_count(times(num(K), A), vcnt(num(K?), A?)) :- otherwise, ground(K?), ground(A?) | true.
sas_count(times(real(K), A), cnt(K?, A?)) :- number(K?) | true.
sas_count(times(real(K), A), vcnt(num(K?), A?)) :- otherwise, ground(K?), ground(A?) | true.
sas_count(rest(K, J, A), rcnt(K?, J?, A?)).
sas_count(_, nocnt) :- otherwise | true.

Cut ::= cut(Mults) ; nocut.
procedure sas_cut(Count?, Count?, ICtx?, Cut).
sas_cut(cnt(K, A), cnt(J, B), _, cut(R?)) :- A? =?= B?, number(K?), number(J?), K? > J?, ground(A?) |
    N := K? - J?,
    sas_copies(N?, A?, R).
sas_cut(cnt(K, A), cnt(J, B), _, cut([])) :- A? =?= B?, number(K?), number(J?), K? =:= J? | true.
sas_cut(cnt(K, A), cnt(J, B), _, nocut) :- A? =?= B?, number(K?), number(J?), K? < J? | true.
sas_cut(CX, CD, IC, R?) :- otherwise, ground(CX?), ground(CD?), ground(IC?) | sas_cut_v(CX?, CD?, IC?, R).

% k.A required and j.A deleted, k or j a value variable.
procedure sas_cut_v(Count?, Count?, ICtx?, Cut).
sas_cut_v(vcnt(K, A), cnt(J, B), IC, R?) :- A? =?= B?, ground(K?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_cut_i(K?, num(J?), A?, IC?, R).
sas_cut_v(cnt(K, A), vcnt(J, B), IC, R?) :- A? =?= B?, ground(K?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_cut_i(num(K?), J?, A?, IC?, R).
sas_cut_v(vcnt(K, A), vcnt(J, B), IC, R?) :- A? =?= B?, ground(K?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_cut_i(K?, J?, A?, IC?, R).
sas_cut_v(rcnt(K, I, A), cnt(J, B), IC, R?) :- A? =?= B?, ground(K?), ground(I?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_cut_i(K?, plus(I?, num(J?)), A?, IC?, R).
sas_cut_v(rcnt(K, I, A), vcnt(J, B), IC, R?) :- A? =?= B?, ground(K?), ground(I?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_cut_i(K?, plus(I?, J?), A?, IC?, R).
sas_cut_v(_, _, _, nocut) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_cut_i(Expr?, Expr?, Atom?, ICtx?, Cut).
sas_cut_i(K, J, A, IC, R?) :- ground(K?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_implies_le(IC?, J?, K?, Ans),
    sas_cut_i1(Ans?, K?, J?, A?, R).

procedure sas_cut_i1(Ans?, Expr?, Expr?, Atom?, Cut).
sas_cut_i1(yes, K, J, A, cut([rest(K?, J?, A?)])).
sas_cut_i1(no, _, _, _, nocut).

% What a schema's multiplicities are compared under: its constraint in the
% checker's form, and its value variables as linear.glp's variables, whole
% where the schema writes them as a multiplicity and rational otherwise
% (linear.glp, the header).
ICtx ::= ictx(Constraint, VEnv, Conj).

% sas_implies_le(IC, J, K, A): the constraint implies J <= K, no values
% satisfying it, each multiplicity a positive whole number
% (def:binding-numbers), with J > K; no, where linear.glp cannot read the
% whole of the constraint (cons_cd).
imported procedure linear#cons_gt(Expr?, Expr?, VEnv?, Conj).
imported procedure linear#cons_cd(Constraint?, VEnv?, Ans?, Cd).
imported procedure linear#conj_app(Conj?, Conj?, Conj).
imported procedure linear#sat_prod(Conj?, DNFs?, Ans).
procedure sas_implies_le(ICtx?, Expr?, Expr?, Ans).
sas_implies_le(ictx(Cn, Env, Bn), J, K, R?) :- ground(Cn?), ground(Env?), ground(Bn?), ground(J?), ground(K?) |
    linear # cons_gt(J?, K?, Env?, C),
    linear # conj_app(Bn?, C?, BC),
    linear # cons_cd(Cn?, Env?, yes, Cd),
    sas_ensures(BC?, Cd?, R).

procedure sas_ensures(Conj?, Cd?, Ans).
sas_ensures(_, cd(_, no), no).
sas_ensures(B, cd(D, yes), R?) :- ground(B?), ground(D?) |
    linear # sat_prod(B?, [D?], S),
    flip(S?, R).

% Each variable written as a multiplicity, Ms, is at least one, a
% multiplicity being a positive whole number (def:binding-numbers); a whole
% value variable that is none is any whole number.
procedure sas_env_bounds(VEnv?, PNames?, Conj).
sas_env_bounds([], _, []).
sas_env_bounds([vb(X, V)|E], Ms, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(V?), ground(Ms?) |
    sas_in(X?, Ms?, A),
    sas_env_bounds(E?, Ms?, R1),
    sas_env_bound(A?, V?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_env_bound(Ans?, Var?, Conj?, Conj).
sas_env_bound(yes, z(N), T, [geq(lin([t(z(N?), 1)], -1))|T?]).
sas_env_bound(yes, q(_), T, T?).
sas_env_bound(no, _, T, T?).

% The context of a schema: its constraint read, a variable for each value
% variable it writes, whole where it is written num(X) or as a multiplicity,
% Ms, and real where it is written real(X), Rl, and the bounds of the
% multiplicities.
procedure sas_ictx(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, PNames?, PNames?, PNames?, ICtx).
sas_ictx(Cn, E, Vs, Nums, Ms, Rl, ictx(Cn1?, Env?, Bn?)) :- ground(Cn?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?), ground(Nums?), ground(Ms?), ground(Rl?) |
    sas_cons(Cn?, E?, Vs?, Cn1),
    sas_venv(Nums?, Ms?, Rl?, Env),
    sas_venv(Nums?, Ms?, Rl?, Env2),
    sas_env_bounds(Env2?, Ms?, Bn).

procedure sas_venv(PNames?, PNames?, PNames?, VEnv).
sas_venv([], _, _, []).
sas_venv([X|Xs], Ms, Rl, [vb(X?, V?)|R?]) :- ground(X?), ground(Ms?), ground(Rl?) |
    sas_in(X?, Ms?, A),
    sas_in(X?, Rl?, Q),
    flip(Q?, W),
    or_yes(A?, W?, Z),
    sas_kvar(Z?, X?, V),
    sas_venv(Xs?, Ms?, Rl?, R).

procedure sas_kvar(Ans?, Constant?, Var).
sas_kvar(yes, X, z(iv(X?))).
sas_kvar(no, X, q(iv(X?))).

% The value variables a schema writes, and those it writes as a multiplicity.
procedure sas_nums_of(SA?, PNames).
sas_nums_of(sa(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, AA, _, Cs, Ks), Nums?) :- ground(AA?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?) |
    sas_nums_args(Ks?, [], N1),
    sas_nums_atoms(AA?, N1?, N2),
    sas_nums_leaves(Cs?, N2?, Nums).

procedure sas_ictx_of(SA?, REnts?, PNames?, ICtx).
sas_ictx_of(S, E, Vs, IC?) :- ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_nums_of(S?, Nums),
    sas_ictx_of1(S?, Nums?, E?, Vs?, IC).

procedure sas_ictx_of1(SA?, PNames?, REnts?, PNames?, ICtx).
sas_ictx_of1(sa(HP, HQ, HF, BP, BQ, BF, Cn, PP, AQ, CQ, AA, Bs, Cs, Ks), Nums, E, Vs, IC?) :-
    ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(HF?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?), ground(BF?), ground(Cn?), ground(PP?),
    ground(AQ?), ground(CQ?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?), ground(Nums?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_nums_args(Ks?, [], Ms),
    sas_vk_of(real, sa(HP?, HQ?, HF?, BP?, BQ?, BF?, Cn?, PP?, AQ?, CQ?, AA?, Bs?, Cs?, Ks?), Rl),
    sas_ictx(Cn?, E?, Vs?, Nums?, Ms?, Rl?, IC).

procedure sas_copies(Constant?, Atom?, Mults).
sas_copies(N, A, [A?]) :- N? =:= 1 | true.
sas_copies(N, A, [times(num(N?), A?)]) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_take(Mults?, Mult?, ICtx?, Mults, Ans).
sas_take([], _, _, [], no).
sas_take([X|Xs], D, _, Xs?, yes) :- X? =?= D? | true.
sas_take([X|Xs], D, IC, R?, A?) :- otherwise, ground(X?), ground(D?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_count(X?, CX),
    sas_count(D?, CD),
    sas_cut(CX?, CD?, IC?, C),
    sas_take1(C?, X?, Xs?, D?, IC?, R, A).

procedure sas_take1(Cut?, Mult?, Mults?, Mult?, ICtx?, Mults, Ans).
sas_take1(cut(Ys), _, Xs, _, _, R?, yes) :- mults_app(Ys?, Xs?, R).
sas_take1(nocut, X, Xs, D, IC, [X?|R?], A?) :- sas_take(Xs?, D?, IC?, R, A).

procedure sas_minus(Mults?, Mults?, ICtx?, Mults, Mults).
sas_minus(Rq, [], _, Rq?, []).
sas_minus(Rq, [D|Ds], IC, K?, M?) :- ground(Rq?), ground(D?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_take(Rq?, D?, IC?, Rq1, A),
    sas_minus1(A?, D?, Rq?, Rq1?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).

procedure sas_minus1(Ans?, Mult?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, ICtx?, Mults, Mults).
sas_minus1(yes, _, _, Rq1, Ds, IC, K?, M?) :- sas_minus(Rq1?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).
sas_minus1(no, D, Rq, _, Ds, IC, K?, M?) :- ground(D?), ground(Rq?) |
    plain_mult(D?, A),
    sas_merged(Rq?, A?, Rq2, Ok),
    sas_minus2(Ok?, D?, Rq?, Rq2?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).

% No one entry of =(i) holds the copies deleted; several entries of the atom,
% merged, may.
procedure sas_minus2(Ans?, Mult?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, ICtx?, Mults, Mults).
sas_minus2(no, D, Rq, _, Ds, IC, K?, [D?|M?]) :- sas_minus(Rq?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).
sas_minus2(yes, D, _, Rq2, Ds, IC, K?, M?) :- ground(D?), ground(Rq2?), ground(IC?) |
    sas_take(Rq2?, D?, IC?, Rq3, A),
    sas_minus3(A?, D?, Rq2?, Rq3?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).

procedure sas_minus3(Ans?, Mult?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, ICtx?, Mults, Mults).
sas_minus3(yes, _, _, Rq3, Ds, IC, K?, M?) :- sas_minus(Rq3?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).
sas_minus3(no, D, Rq2, _, Ds, IC, K?, [D?|M?]) :- sas_minus(Rq2?, Ds?, IC?, K, M).

% sas_merged(Rq, A, R, Ok): the entries of the atom A among Rq, two or more
% (Ok yes), merged into one at the head of R: their sum where all are
% numbers, and otherwise rest(Sum, 0, A), the copies of Sum.A beyond none.
Parts ::= pts(Exprs, Mults).
procedure sas_parts(Mults?, Atom?, Parts).
sas_parts([], _, pts([], [])).
sas_parts([M|Ms], A, R?) :- ground(M?), ground(Ms?), ground(A?) |
    sas_parts(Ms?, A?, P),
    sas_entry(M?, A?, E),
    sas_parts1(E?, M?, P?, R).

Entry ::= en(Expr) ; en_no.
procedure sas_entry(Mult?, Atom?, Entry).
sas_entry(M, A, en(num(1))) :- M? =?= A? | true.
sas_entry(times(K, B), A, en(K?)) :- B? =?= A? | true.
sas_entry(_, _, en_no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_parts1(Entry?, Mult?, Parts?, Parts).
sas_parts1(en(K), _, pts(Ks, Os), pts([K?|Ks?], Os?)).
sas_parts1(en_no, M, pts(Ks, Os), pts(Ks?, [M?|Os?])).

procedure sas_merged(Mults?, Atom?, Mults, Ans).
sas_merged(Rq, A, R?, Ok?) :- ground(Rq?), ground(A?) |
    sas_parts(Rq?, A?, P),
    sas_merged1(P?, A?, R, Ok).

procedure sas_merged1(Parts?, Atom?, Mults, Ans).
sas_merged1(pts([], Os), _, Os?, no).
sas_merged1(pts([_], Os), _, Os?, no).
sas_merged1(pts([K, L|Ks], Os), A, [M?|Os?], yes) :- ground(K?), ground(L?), ground(Ks?), ground(A?) |
    sas_sum([K?, L?|Ks?], S),
    sas_merged_entry(S?, A?, M).

Sum ::= s_num(Constant) ; s_expr(Expr).
procedure sas_sum(Exprs?, Sum).
sas_sum([], s_num(0)).
sas_sum([X], R?) :- ground(X?) | sas_sum1(X?, R).
sas_sum([X, Y|Ys], R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(Ys?) |
    sas_sum([Y?|Ys?], S),
    sas_sum1(X?, S0),
    sas_sum2(S0?, S?, R).

procedure sas_sum1(Expr?, Sum).
sas_sum1(num(X), s_num(X?)) :- number(X?) | true.
sas_sum1(X, s_expr(X?)) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | true.

procedure sas_sum2(Sum?, Sum?, Sum).
sas_sum2(s_num(X), s_num(Y), s_num(Z?)) :- number(X?), number(Y?) | Z := X? + Y?.
sas_sum2(s_num(X), s_expr(Y), s_expr(plus(num(X?), Y?))).
sas_sum2(s_expr(X), s_num(Y), s_expr(plus(X?, num(Y?)))).
sas_sum2(s_expr(X), s_expr(Y), s_expr(plus(X?, Y?))).

procedure sas_merged_entry(Sum?, Atom?, Mult).
sas_merged_entry(s_num(N), A, times(num(N?), A?)).
sas_merged_entry(s_expr(X), A, rest(X?, num(0), A?)).

procedure sas_guard(Ans?, Guard).
sas_guard(yes, guarded).
sas_guard(no, unguarded).

procedure sas_ing(PNames?, RName?, Ans).
sas_ing([], _, no).
sas_ing([G|Gs], N, R?) :- ground(N?), ground(Gs?) |
    sas_nameq(G?, N?, A),
    sas_ing1(A?, Gs?, N?, R).

procedure sas_ing1(Ans?, PNames?, RName?, Ans).
sas_ing1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_ing1(no, Gs, N, R?) :- sas_ing(Gs?, N?, R).

% What a schema is read against: its plain literals and its conjuncts in
% Head and in Body, its guards, its role table, its Vars, the context of its
% multiplicities, Vars with the bound variables, its binders, and whether
% its quantifiers are all listed/3's.
SCtx ::= sctx(SQLits, Quants, SQLits, Quants, PNames, REnts, PNames, ICtx, PNames, Bnds, Ans).

% Vars with the bound variables.
procedure sas_allxs(Bnds?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_allxs([], T, T?).
sas_allxs([bnd(Xs, _)|Bs], T, R?) :- sas_allxs(Bs?, T?, R1), sas_papp(Xs?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_papp(PNames?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_papp([], T, T?).
sas_papp([X|Xs], T, [X?|R?]) :- sas_papp(Xs?, T?, R).

% An agent role N: what it adds and deletes, and requires and forbids.
procedure sas_rs(RName?, SCtx?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_rs(N, sctx(HP, _, BP, _, G, E, V, IC, _, _, _), R?, M?) :- ground(N?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_ing(G?, N?, Gi),
    sas_guard(Gi?, Gd),
    sas_part(HP?, N?, E?, V?, Add, Del),
    sas_part(BP?, N?, E?, V?, Req, Forb),
    sas_rs1(Gd?, Add?, Del?, Req?, Forb?, IC?, R, M).

% The role, and the atoms it deletes that it does not require.
procedure sas_rs1(Guard?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, ICtx?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_rs1(Gd, Add, Del, Req, Forb, IC, rs(Gd?, Add?, Del?, Keep?, Forb?), M?) :- ground(Del?), ground(IC?) |
    mults_cleared(Del?, no, D0),
    sas_minus(Req?, D0?, IC?, Keep, M).

% A listed role N, its kind read off the anchor of a quantifier binding it.
procedure sas_crs(RName?, SCtx?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_crs(N, sctx(_, HQ, _, BQ, G, E, _, IC, Vq, Bs, Smp), R?, M?) :-
    ground(N?), ground(HQ?), ground(BQ?), ground(E?), ground(Vq?), ground(Bs?) |
    sas_ing(G?, N?, Gi),
    sas_guard(Gi?, Gd),
    sas_qlits(HQ?, N?, HL),
    sas_qlits(BQ?, N?, BL),
    sas_part(HL?, N?, E?, Vq?, Add, Del),
    sas_part(BL?, N?, E?, Vq?, Req, Forb),
    sas_over(Bs?, N?, Over),
    sas_kind(Smp?, Over?, E?, Vq?, K),
    sas_crs1(K?, Gd?, Add?, Del?, Req?, Forb?, IC?, R, M).

procedure sas_crs1(RoleKind?, Guard?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, Mults?, ICtx?, NRoleSpec, Mults).
sas_crs1(K, Gd, Add, Del, Req, Forb, IC, crs(K?, Gd?, Add?, Del?, Keep?, Forb?), M?) :- ground(Del?), ground(IC?) |
    mults_cleared(Del?, no, D0),
    sas_minus(Req?, D0?, IC?, Keep, M).

% Whether the constant X occurs among arguments, or in a name term among them.
procedure sas_occ_nt(SNT?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_occ_nt(own(N), X, yes) :- N? =?= X? | true.
sas_occ_nt(own(_), _, no) :- otherwise | true.
sas_occ_nt(ext(_, Y), X, yes) :- Y? =?= X? | true.
sas_occ_nt(ext(S, _), X, R?) :- otherwise | sas_occ_nt(S?, X?, R).

procedure sas_occ_arg(SArg?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_occ_arg(own(N), X, R?) :- sas_occ_nt(own(N?), X?, R).
sas_occ_arg(ext(S, Y), X, R?) :- sas_occ_nt(ext(S?, Y?), X?, R).
sas_occ_arg(num(Y), X, yes) :- Y? =?= X? | true.
sas_occ_arg(real(Y), X, yes) :- Y? =?= X? | true.
sas_occ_arg(sgn(Y, N), X, yes) :- Y? =?= X?, ground(N?) | true.
sas_occ_arg(sgn(Y, N), X, yes) :- N? =?= X?, ground(Y?) | true.
sas_occ_arg(C, X, yes) :- C? =?= X? | true.
sas_occ_arg(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_occ(SArgs?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_occ([], _, no).
sas_occ([A|As], X, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(X?) |
    sas_occ_arg(A?, X?, O),
    sas_occ1(O?, As?, X?, R).

procedure sas_occ1(Ans?, SArgs?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_occ1(yes, _, _, yes).
sas_occ1(no, As, X, R?) :- sas_occ(As?, X?, R).

% Whether the quantifiers of a schema are all listed/3's: it has no formula
% but conjuncts, no binder but theirs, and each conjunct binds one variable,
% the second argument of its anchor and no other, with no phi, and every
% literal of it held by that variable, of which it has one.
procedure sas_simple(SA?, Ans).
sas_simple(sa(_, HQ, HF, _, BQ, BF, _, _, _, _, _, Bs, _, _), R?) :-
    ground(HQ?), ground(HF?), ground(BQ?), ground(BF?), ground(Bs?) |
    sas_no_forms(HF?, BF?, A1),
    sas_q_simple(HQ?, A2),
    sas_q_simple(BQ?, A3),
    sas_quapp(HQ?, BQ?, QQ),
    sas_same_len(QQ?, Bs?, A4),
    both_yes(A1?, A2?, A12),
    both_yes(A3?, A4?, A34),
    both_yes(A12?, A34?, R).

procedure sas_no_forms(SLits?, SLits?, Ans).
sas_no_forms([], [], yes).
sas_no_forms(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_same_len(Quants?, Bnds?, Ans).
sas_same_len([], [], yes).
sas_same_len([_|Qs], [_|Bs], R?) :- sas_same_len(Qs?, Bs?, R).
sas_same_len(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_q_simple(Quants?, Ans).
sas_q_simple([], yes).
sas_q_simple([q([X], atom(_, [_, Y|Us]), true, [L|Ls])|Qs], R?) :-
    X? =?= Y?, ground(X?), ground(Us?), ground(L?), ground(Ls?), ground(Qs?) |
    sas_occ(Us?, X?, O),
    flip(O?, A1),
    sas_all_held([L?|Ls?], X?, A2),
    both_yes(A1?, A2?, A),
    sas_q_simple1(A?, Qs?, R).
sas_q_simple(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_q_simple1(Ans?, Quants?, Ans).
sas_q_simple1(no, _, no).
sas_q_simple1(yes, Qs, R?) :- sas_q_simple(Qs?, R).

procedure sas_all_held(SQLits?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_all_held([], _, yes).
sas_all_held([L|Ls], X, R?) :- ground(Ls?), ground(X?) |
    sas_lit_held(L?, X?, A),
    sas_all_held1(A?, Ls?, X?, R).

procedure sas_all_held1(Ans?, SQLits?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_all_held1(no, _, _, no).
sas_all_held1(yes, Ls, X, R?) :- sas_all_held(Ls?, X?, R).

% The kind of a listed role, from the first binder binding it: pi[rho(_,
% u_2, ..., u_r)] in a schema whose quantifiers are all listed/3's, and
% qlisted otherwise (def:role).  An anchor with no holder gives a kind whose
% base, 0, is no agent role.
procedure sas_kind(Ans?, Bnds?, REnts?, PNames?, RoleKind).
sas_kind(yes, [bnd(_, atom(Rho, [P, _|Us]))|_], E, V, listed(I?, Rho?, Us1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_look(P?, E?, L),
    sas_index(L?, I),
    sas_args(Us?, E?, V?, Us1).
sas_kind(no, [bnd(Xs, atom(Rho, [P|As]))|_], E, V, qlisted(I?, Rho?, As1?, Xs1?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_look(P?, E?, L),
    sas_index(L?, I),
    sas_args(As?, E?, V?, As1),
    sas_bvars(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1).
sas_kind(_, _, _, _, listed(0, none, [])) :- otherwise | true.

% --- safe formulas (def:role) -------------------------------------------------
% The holder of an atom, as an argument.
procedure sas_aholder(SAtom?, REnts?, PNames?, Arg).
sas_aholder(atom(_, [H|_]), E, V, R?) :- sas_arg(H?, E?, V?, R).
sas_aholder(atom(_, []), _, _, any).

procedure sas_form(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Form).
sas_form(atom(P, As), E, V, fa(H?, A?)) :- ground(P?), ground(As?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_aholder(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, H),
    sas_iatom(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, A).
sas_form(times(K, At), E, V, fa(H?, M?)) :- ground(K?), ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_aholder(At?, E?, V?, H),
    sas_imult(times(K?, At?), E?, V?, M).
sas_form(not(X), E, V, fnot(F?)) :- sas_form(X?, E?, V?, F).
sas_form(and(X, Y), E, V, fand(A?, B?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_form(X?, E?, V?, A), sas_form(Y?, E?, V?, B).
sas_form(or(X, Y), E, V, for(A?, B?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_form(X?, E?, V?, A), sas_form(Y?, E?, V?, B).
sas_form(implies(X, Y), E, V, for(fnot(A?), B?)) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_form(X?, E?, V?, A), sas_form(Y?, E?, V?, B).
sas_form(exists(Xs, At, Phi), E, V, fexists(Xs1?, H?, A?, F?)) :-
    ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_bvars(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1),
    sas_aholder(At?, E?, V?, H),
    sas_iatom(At?, E?, V?, A),
    sas_form(Phi?, E?, V?, F).
sas_form(forall(Xs, At, Phi, Psi), E, V, fforall(Xs1?, H?, A?, F?, G?)) :-
    ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_bvars(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1),
    sas_aholder(At?, E?, V?, H),
    sas_iatom(At?, E?, V?, A),
    sas_form(Phi?, E?, V?, F),
    sas_forms(Psi?, E?, V?, G).
sas_form(C, E, V, fcons(R?)) :- otherwise | sas_cons(C?, E?, V?, R).

% A conclusion: a list is a conjunction, anything else one formula.
procedure sas_forms(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Forms).
sas_forms([], _, _, []).
sas_forms([L|Ls], E, V, [F?|R?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_form(L?, E?, V?, F),
    sas_forms(Ls?, E?, V?, R).
sas_forms(X, E, V, [F?]) :- otherwise | sas_form(X?, E?, V?, F).

% The literals of a conjunct, as formulas.
procedure sas_lit_forms(SQLits?, REnts?, PNames?, Forms).
sas_lit_forms([], _, _, []).
sas_lit_forms([atom(P, As)|Ls], E, V, [F?|R?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_form(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, F),
    sas_lit_forms(Ls?, E?, V?, R).
sas_lit_forms([times(K, A)|Ls], E, V, [F?|R?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_form(times(K?, A?), E?, V?, F),
    sas_lit_forms(Ls?, E?, V?, R).
sas_lit_forms([not(M)|Ls], E, V, [fnot(F?)|R?]) :- ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_mult_form(M?, E?, V?, F),
    sas_lit_forms(Ls?, E?, V?, R).

procedure sas_mult_form(SMult?, REnts?, PNames?, Form).
sas_mult_form(atom(P, As), E, V, F?) :- sas_form(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, F).
sas_mult_form(times(K, A), E, V, F?) :- sas_form(times(K?, A?), E?, V?, F).

% A conjunct of the body, as a formula, and the other formulas of the body.
procedure sas_body_forms(Quants?, SLits?, REnts?, PNames?, Forms).
sas_body_forms([], F, E, V, R?) :- sas_forms(F?, E?, V?, R).
sas_body_forms([q(Xs, At, Phi, L)|Qs], F, E, V, [fforall(Xs1?, H?, A?, P?, G?)|R?]) :-
    ground(At?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_bvars(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1),
    sas_aholder(At?, E?, V?, H),
    sas_iatom(At?, E?, V?, A),
    sas_form(Phi?, E?, V?, P),
    sas_lit_forms(L?, E?, V?, G),
    sas_body_forms(Qs?, F?, E?, V?, R).

% The conjuncts of the head (def:role).
procedure sas_conjs(Quants?, REnts?, PNames?, Conjuncts).
sas_conjs([], _, _, []).
sas_conjs([q(Xs, At, Phi, L)|Qs], E, V, [conjunct(Xs1?, I?, A?, P?, Add?, Del?, G?)|R?]) :-
    ground(At?), ground(L?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_bvars(Xs?, E?, V?, Xs1),
    sas_atom_ar(At?, E?, I),
    sas_iatom(At?, E?, V?, A),
    sas_form(Phi?, E?, V?, P),
    sas_lit_forms(L?, E?, V?, G),
    sas_hms(L?, E?, V?, Add, Del),
    sas_conjs(Qs?, E?, V?, R).

% The index of the agent role holding an atom, 0 if it is none.
procedure sas_atom_ar(SAtom?, REnts?, Integer).
sas_atom_ar(atom(_, []), _, 0).
sas_atom_ar(atom(_, [H|_]), E, R?) :- sas_ar_index(E?, H?, R).

% The conditional literals of a conjunct: those an agent role holds
% (def:schema).
procedure sas_hms(SQLits?, REnts?, PNames?, HMults, HMults).
sas_hms([], _, _, [], []).
sas_hms([L|Ls], E, V, P?, N?) :- ground(L?), ground(E?), ground(V?) |
    sas_lit_atom(L?, At),
    sas_atom_ar(At?, E?, J),
    sas_lit_neg(L?, G),
    sas_lit_mult(L?, M),
    sas_imult(M?, E?, V?, X),
    sas_hms(Ls?, E?, V?, P1, N1),
    sas_hm(J?, G?, X?, P1?, N1?, P, N).

procedure sas_hm(Integer?, Ans?, Mult?, HMults?, HMults?, HMults, HMults).
sas_hm(J, _, _, P, N, P?, N?) :- J? =:= 0 | true.
sas_hm(J, no, X, P, N, [hm(J?, X?)|P?], N?) :- J? > 0 | true.
sas_hm(J, yes, X, P, N, P?, [hm(J?, X?)|N?]) :- J? > 0 | true.

% The index of the agent role named H, 0 if it is none.
procedure(X) sas_ar_index(REnts?, X?, Integer).
sas_ar_index([], _, 0).
sas_ar_index([ar(M, I)|Es], P, R?) :- ground(M?), integer(I?), ground(Es?), ground(P?) |
    sas_nameq(P?, M?, A),
    sas_ar_index1(A?, I?, Es?, P?, R).
sas_ar_index([_|Es], P, R?) :- otherwise, ground(Es?), ground(P?) | sas_ar_index(Es?, P?, R).

procedure(X) sas_ar_index1(Ans?, Integer?, REnts?, X?, Integer).
sas_ar_index1(yes, I, _, _, I?).
sas_ar_index1(no, _, Es, P, R?) :- sas_ar_index(Es?, P?, R).

procedure sas_roles(REnts?, SCtx?, NRoleSpecs).
sas_roles([], _, []).
sas_roles([ar(N, _)|Ts], C, [RS?|R?]) :- ground(C?) |
    sas_rs(N?, C?, RS, _),
    sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).
sas_roles([lr(N, _)|Ts], C, [RS?|R?]) :- ground(C?) |
    sas_crs(N?, C?, RS, _),
    sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).
sas_roles([av(_)|Ts], C, R?) :- sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).
sas_roles([qv(_)|Ts], C, R?) :- sas_roles(Ts?, C?, R).

procedure sas_has_lr(REnts?, Ans).
sas_has_lr([], no).
sas_has_lr([lr(_, _)|_], yes).
sas_has_lr([ar(_, _)|Ts], R?) :- sas_has_lr(Ts?, R).
sas_has_lr([av(_)|Ts], R?) :- sas_has_lr(Ts?, R).
sas_has_lr([qv(_)|Ts], R?) :- sas_has_lr(Ts?, R).

procedure sas_true(SConstraint?, Ans).
sas_true(true, yes).
sas_true(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_schema(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, PNames?, NSchema).
sas_schema(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G, S?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?), ground(G?) |
    sas_ana(H?, B?, Cn?, A),
    sas_schema0(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, A?, G?, S).

procedure sas_schema0(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SA?, PNames?, NSchema).
sas_schema0(Nm, Ns, Vs, A, G, S?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(A?), ground(G?) |
    sas_table_of(Ns?, A?, G?, E),
    sas_schema1(Nm?, Vs?, A?, G?, E?, S).

% What a schema is read against (SCtx).
procedure sas_sctx(SA?, PNames?, REnts?, PNames?, SCtx).
sas_sctx(sa(HP, HQ, HF, BP, BQ, BF, Cn, PP, AQ, CQ, AA, Bs, Cs, Ks), G, E, Vs,
         sctx(HP?, HQ?, BP?, BQ?, G?, E?, Vs?, IC?, Vq?, Bs?, Smp?)) :-
    ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(HF?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?), ground(BF?), ground(Cn?), ground(PP?),
    ground(AQ?), ground(CQ?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_ictx_of(sa(HP?, HQ?, HF?, BP?, BQ?, BF?, Cn?, PP?, AQ?, CQ?, AA?, Bs?, Cs?, Ks?), E?, Vs?, IC),
    sas_allxs(Bs?, Vs?, Vq),
    sas_simple(sa(HP?, HQ?, HF?, BP?, BQ?, BF?, Cn?, PP?, AQ?, CQ?, AA?, Bs?, Cs?, Ks?), Smp).

procedure sas_schema1(Constant?, PNames?, SA?, PNames?, REnts?, NSchema).
sas_schema1(Nm, Vs, A, G, E, S?) :- ground(A?), ground(G?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_sctx(A?, G?, E?, Vs?, Cx),
    sas_schema2(Nm?, Vs?, A?, E?, Cx?, S).

procedure sas_schema2(Constant?, PNames?, SA?, REnts?, SCtx?, NSchema).
sas_schema2(Nm, Vs, sa(_, HQ, _, _, BQ, BF, Cn, _, _, _, AA, Bs, Cs, Ks), E,
            sctx(HP, HQ1, BP, BQ1, G, E1, Vs1, IC, Vq, Bs1, Smp), S?) :-
    ground(Vs?), ground(HQ?), ground(BQ?), ground(BF?), ground(Cn?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?),
    ground(E?), ground(HP?), ground(HQ1?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ1?), ground(G?), ground(E1?), ground(Vs1?),
    ground(IC?), ground(Vq?), ground(Bs1?), ground(Smp?) |
    sas_roles(E?, sctx(HP?, HQ1?, BP?, BQ1?, G?, E1?, Vs1?, IC?, Vq?, Bs1?, Smp?), Rs),
    sas_has_lr(E?, L),
    sas_true(Cn?, T),
    sas_nums_args(Ks?, [], N1),
    sas_nums_atoms(AA?, N1?, N2),
    sas_nums_leaves(Cs?, N2?, Nums),
    sas_vk3(real, AA?, Cs?, Ks?, Rl),
    sas_vars(Vs?, E?, Nums?, Rl?, Vars),
    sas_cons(Cn?, E?, Vs?, Cn1),
    sas_conjs(HQ?, E?, Vq?, Cj),
    sas_body_forms(BQ?, BF?, E?, Vq?, Fs),
    sas_bound_args(Bs?, [], Bd),
    sas_schema3(Smp?, L?, T?, Nm?, Vars?, Bd?, Cn1?, Rs?, Cj?, Fs?, S).

procedure sas_schema3(Ans?, Ans?, Ans?, Constant?, Args?, Args?, Constraint?, NRoleSpecs?, Conjuncts?, Forms?, NSchema).
sas_schema3(no, _, _, Nm, Vs, Bd, Cn, Rs, Cj, Fs, qschema(Nm?, Vs?, Bd?, Cn?, Rs?, Cj?, Fs?)).
sas_schema3(yes, no, yes, Nm, Vs, _, _, Rs, _, _, schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?)).
sas_schema3(yes, yes, yes, Nm, Vs, _, _, Rs, _, _, cschema(Nm?, Vs?, [], Rs?)).
sas_schema3(yes, _, no, Nm, Vs, _, Cn, Rs, _, _, nschema(Nm?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)).

% --- What the clause syntax requires, and its reading cannot carry ---------
% Each fault names the schema.  not_holder(Schema, Pred): an atom whose
% first argument is not a name of the schema ("the first argument of each
% its holder", Section 3.2; def:role).  not_in_vars(Schema, Pred): an
% argument of an atom of Pred, its multiplicity or its condition, or of the
% constraint (Pred constraint), that is a constant neither the wildcard, a
% role, nor a variable of Vars (def:schema: "its variables are its agent
% variables that are not agent roles and its speech-act variables";
% def:numbers, its value variables); a value variable, a speech-act variable
% of a name term or of a signed term, and a variable of Vars no atom writes
% are decided by the checker as before (not_in_head, head_not_variable).
% deleted_not_required(Schema, Role, Atom): an atom of -(i) not in =(i)
% (def:schema: "It is required that -(i) is a subset of =(i)").
% quantified_condition(Schema, X): X a bound variable absent from an anchor
% binding it (def:role: "among whose arguments, or in name terms among them,
% every variable of x-bar occurs"), or a listed role bound under two anchors
% (def:role: "every quantifier binding it having the same anchor").
% condition_holder(Schema, Pred): the anchor, of Pred, of a listed role held
% by no agent role (def:role).  head_formula(Schema): a formula of Head that is no
% literal and no quantified conjunct (def:schema: "H, its head, a finite
% multiset of literals and quantified conjuncts").  listed_agent_role(Schema,
% X): X bound and the holder of a literal outside its quantifiers, so an
% agent role too.  guard_not_role(Schema, Name): a guard no agent variable of
% the schema ("G a set of agent variables of it", def:schema).

procedure sas_fapp(Faults?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_fapp([], T, T?).
sas_fapp([F|Fs], T, [F?|R?]) :- sas_fapp(Fs?, T?, R).

% The atoms whose holder is no name and no bound variable.
procedure sas_holder_faults(SAtoms?, Constant?, Names?, PNames?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_holder_faults([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_holder_faults([A|As], Nm, Ns, Xs, T, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?), ground(Xs?) |
    sas_atom_named(A?, Ns?, Xs?, Ok),
    sas_holder_faults(As?, Nm?, Ns?, Xs?, T?, R1),
    sas_holder_fault(Ok?, Nm?, A?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_atom_named(SAtom?, Names?, PNames?, Ans).
sas_atom_named(atom(_, []), _, _, no).
sas_atom_named(atom(_, [H|_]), Ns, Xs, R?) :- ground(H?), ground(Ns?), ground(Xs?) |
    sas_in_names(H?, Ns?, A),
    sas_held_x(H?, Xs?, B),
    or_yes(A?, B?, R).

procedure sas_held_x(SArg?, PNames?, Ans).
sas_held_x(_, [], no).
sas_held_x(H, [X|_], yes) :- H? =?= X? | true.
sas_held_x(H, [_|Xs], R?) :- otherwise | sas_held_x(H?, Xs?, R).

procedure sas_holder_fault(Ans?, Constant?, SAtom?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_holder_fault(yes, _, _, T, T?).
sas_holder_fault(no, Nm, A, T, [not_holder(Nm?, P?)|T?]) :- sas_pred(A?, P).

% The constants of Vars an argument needs (not_in_vars).
procedure sas_arg_vf(SArg?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_arg_vf(own(_), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(ext(_, _), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(num(_), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(real(_), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(sgn(_, _), _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_arg_vf(item_of(Y), E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- sas_bare_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).
sas_arg_vf(C, E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare_vf(C?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).

procedure(X) sas_bare_vf(X?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_bare_vf(C, _, _, _, _, T, T?) :- C? =?= '_' | true.
sas_bare_vf(C, E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- otherwise, ground(C?) |
    sas_look(C?, E?, L),
    sas_var(C?, V?, F),
    sas_bare_vf1(L?, F?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).

procedure sas_bare_vf1(Look?, VFound?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_bare_vf1(lrole(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_bare_vf1(lvar, vfound(_), _, _, T, T?).
sas_bare_vf1(lnone, vfound(_), _, _, T, T?).
sas_bare_vf1(lvar, vnone, Nm, P, T, [not_in_vars(Nm?, P?)|T?]).
sas_bare_vf1(lnone, vnone, Nm, P, T, [not_in_vars(Nm?, P?)|T?]).

procedure sas_args_vf(SArgs?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_args_vf([], _, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_args_vf([A|As], E, V, Nm, P, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?), ground(P?) |
    sas_args_vf(As?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R1),
    sas_arg_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, R1?, R).

% An atom's arguments after its holder, and a multiplicity.
procedure sas_atom_vf(SAtom?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_atom_vf(atom(_, []), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_atom_vf(atom(P, [_|As]), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_args_vf(As?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, T?, R).

procedure sas_mult_vf(SMult?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_mult_vf(atom(P, As), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_atom_vf(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R).
sas_mult_vf(times(K, atom(P, As)), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?), ground(P?) |
    sas_atom_vf(atom(P?, As?), E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_arg_vf(K?, E?, V?, Nm?, P?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_lits_vf(SQLits?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_lits_vf([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_lits_vf([L|Ls], E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(L?), ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_lit_mult(L?, M),
    sas_lits_vf(Ls?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_mult_vf(M?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).

% The atoms and the leaves of the conjuncts and formulas.
procedure sas_atoms_vf(SAtoms?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_atoms_vf([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_atoms_vf([A|As], E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_atoms_vf(As?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_atom_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_leaves_vf(SLits?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_leaves_vf([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_leaves_vf([C|Cs], E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_leaves_vf(Cs?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_cons_vf(C?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_cons_vf(SConstraint?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_cons_vf(true, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_cons_vf(and(A, B), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_cons_vf(B?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_cons_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(or(A, B), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_cons_vf(B?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_cons_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(implies(A, B), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_cons_vf(B?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_cons_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(not(A), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_cons_vf(A?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R).
sas_cons_vf(rel(_, Xs), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_exprs_vf(Xs?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R).
sas_cons_vf(ne(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(eq(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(le(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(lt(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(ge(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(gt(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(succ(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_arg_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R1), sas_arg_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(signed(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_arg_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R1), sas_arg_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(unsigned(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_arg_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R1), sas_arg_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, R1?, R).
sas_cons_vf(program(X), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R).
sas_cons_vf(_, _, _, _, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure sas_expr_vf(SExpr?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_expr_vf(plus(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_expr_vf(minus(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_expr_vf(mul(X, Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_expr_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1), sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).
sas_expr_vf(fn(_, Xs), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_exprs_vf(Xs?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R).
% A cardinality's and a sum's anchor and phi are among the atoms and the
% leaves of the formulas (sas_ana4), and a sum's term is read here.
sas_expr_vf(cardinality(_, _, _), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(sum(Xs, _, _, U), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :-
    sas_papp(Xs?, V?, V1),
    sas_expr_vf(U?, E?, V1?, Nm?, T?, R).
sas_expr_vf(own(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(ext(_, _), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(num(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(real(_), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(sgn(_, _), _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_expr_vf(author_of(Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_bare_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R).
sas_expr_vf(item_of(Y), E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- sas_bare_vf(Y?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R).
sas_expr_vf(C, E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- otherwise | sas_bare_vf(C?, E?, V?, Nm?, constraint, T?, R).

procedure sas_exprs_vf(SExprs?, REnts?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_exprs_vf([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_exprs_vf([X|Xs], E, V, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(E?), ground(V?), ground(Nm?) |
    sas_exprs_vf(Xs?, E?, V?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_expr_vf(X?, E?, V?, Nm?, R1?, R).

% The atoms each role deletes that it does not require.
procedure sas_del_faults(REnts?, Constant?, SCtx?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_del_faults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_del_faults([ar(N, I)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- ground(Nm?), ground(C?) |
    sas_rs(N?, C?, _, M),
    sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R1),
    sas_mfaults(M?, Nm?, I?, R1?, R).
sas_del_faults([lr(N, I)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- ground(Nm?), ground(C?) |
    sas_crs(N?, C?, _, M),
    sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R1),
    sas_mfaults(M?, Nm?, I?, R1?, R).
sas_del_faults([av(_)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R).
sas_del_faults([qv(_)|Ts], Nm, C, T, R?) :- sas_del_faults(Ts?, Nm?, C?, T?, R).

procedure sas_mfaults(Mults?, Constant?, Integer?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_mfaults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_mfaults([M|Ms], Nm, I, T, [deleted_not_required(Nm?, I?, A?)|R?]) :-
    ground(M?), ground(Nm?), integer(I?) |
    plain_mult(M?, A),
    sas_mfaults(Ms?, Nm?, I?, T?, R).

% The bound variables, each once.
procedure sas_qvars(Bnds?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_qvars([], T, T?).
sas_qvars([bnd(Xs, _)|Bs], T, R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(T?) |
    sas_qvars0(Xs?, T?, T1),
    sas_qvars(Bs?, T1?, R).

procedure sas_qvars0(PNames?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_qvars0([], T, T?).
sas_qvars0([X|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(T?) |
    sas_in(X?, T?, A),
    sas_qvars1(A?, X?, Xs?, T?, R).

procedure sas_qvars1(Ans?, Constant?, PNames?, PNames?, PNames).
sas_qvars1(yes, _, Xs, T, R?) :- sas_qvars0(Xs?, T?, R).
sas_qvars1(no, X, Xs, T, R?) :- sas_qvars0(Xs?, [X?|T?], R).

% X occurs in the anchor of every binder among Bs, after its holder.
procedure sas_cond_occ(Bnds?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_cond_occ([], _, yes).
sas_cond_occ([bnd(_, atom(_, []))|_], _, no).
sas_cond_occ([bnd(_, atom(_, [_|As]))|Bs], X, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(X?), ground(Bs?) |
    sas_occ(As?, X?, A),
    sas_cond_occ1(A?, Bs?, X?, R).

procedure sas_cond_occ1(Ans?, Bnds?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_cond_occ1(no, _, _, no).
sas_cond_occ1(yes, Bs, X, R?) :- sas_cond_occ(Bs?, X?, R).

% The binders among Bs have one anchor.
procedure sas_cond_same(Bnds?, Ans).
sas_cond_same([], yes).
sas_cond_same([bnd(_, C)|Bs], R?) :- ground(C?), ground(Bs?) | sas_cond_same1(Bs?, C?, R).

procedure sas_cond_same1(Bnds?, SAtom?, Ans).
sas_cond_same1([], _, yes).
sas_cond_same1([bnd(_, C)|Bs], C0, R?) :- C? =?= C0?, ground(C0?) | sas_cond_same1(Bs?, C0?, R).
sas_cond_same1(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% What def:role asks of a variable X of the binders Over binding it: it
% occurs in each anchor; where it holds an atom, so a listed role, the anchors
% are one.
procedure sas_cond_ok(Ans?, Bnds?, Constant?, Ans).
sas_cond_ok(H, Over, X, R?) :- ground(H?), ground(Over?), ground(X?) |
    sas_cond_occ(Over?, X?, A),
    sas_cond_ok1(H?, Over?, A?, R).

procedure sas_cond_ok1(Ans?, Bnds?, Ans?, Ans).
sas_cond_ok1(_, _, no, no).
sas_cond_ok1(no, _, yes, yes).
sas_cond_ok1(yes, Over, yes, R?) :- sas_cond_same(Over?, R).

% The holders of the anchors of a listed role are agent roles.
procedure sas_chfaults(Ans?, Bnds?, Constant?, REnts?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_chfaults(no, _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_chfaults(yes, [], _, _, T, T?).
sas_chfaults(yes, [bnd(_, C)|Bs], Nm, E, T, R?) :- ground(C?), ground(Nm?), ground(E?), ground(Bs?) |
    sas_atom_ar(C?, E?, I),
    sas_pred(C?, P),
    sas_chfaults(yes, Bs?, Nm?, E?, T?, R1),
    sas_chfault(I?, Nm?, P?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_chfault(Integer?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_chfault(I, _, _, T, T?) :- I? > 0 | true.
sas_chfault(I, Nm, P, T, [condition_holder(Nm?, P?)|T?]) :- I? =:= 0 | true.

procedure sas_qfaults(PNames?, Constant?, SA?, REnts?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qfaults([], _, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qfaults([X|Xs], Nm, S, E, T, R?) :-
    ground(X?), ground(Nm?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    sas_qfaults(Xs?, Nm?, S?, E?, T?, F0),
    sas_qfault(S?, X?, Nm?, E?, F0?, R).

procedure sas_qfault(SA?, Constant?, Constant?, REnts?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qfault(sa(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, PP, _, _, AA, Bs, _, _), X, Nm, E, T, R?) :-
    ground(PP?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?), ground(X?), ground(Nm?), ground(E?) |
    sas_over(Bs?, X?, Over),
    sas_over(Bs?, X?, Over2),
    sas_aheld(AA?, X?, H),
    sas_cond_ok(H?, Over?, X?, C),
    sas_holds(PP?, X?, A),
    sas_chfaults(H?, Over2?, Nm?, E?, T?, F0),
    sas_qf1(C?, Nm?, X?, F0?, F1),
    sas_qf2(A?, Nm?, X?, F1?, R).

procedure sas_qf1(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qf1(yes, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qf1(no, Nm, X, T, [quantified_condition(Nm?, X?)|T?]).

procedure sas_qf2(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_qf2(no, _, _, T, T?).
sas_qf2(yes, Nm, X, T, [listed_agent_role(Nm?, X?)|T?]).

% A formula of the head that is no literal and no quantified conjunct.
procedure sas_hffaults(SLits?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_hffaults([], _, T, T?).
sas_hffaults([_|Fs], Nm, T, [head_formula(Nm?)|R?]) :- ground(Nm?) | sas_hffaults(Fs?, Nm?, T?, R).

% The guards, each an agent variable of the schema: a name of it.
procedure sas_gfaults(PNames?, Constant?, REnts?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_gfaults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_gfaults([G|Gs], Nm, E, T, R?) :- ground(G?), ground(Nm?), ground(E?) |
    sas_look(G?, E?, L),
    sas_gfaults(Gs?, Nm?, E?, T?, R1),
    sas_gfault(L?, Nm?, G?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_gfault(Look?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_gfault(lrole(_), _, _, T, T?).
sas_gfault(lvar, _, _, T, T?).
sas_gfault(lnone, Nm, G, T, [guard_not_role(Nm?, G?)|T?]).

% The faults of the reading of a schema written as a clause, in the order:
% the holders, the variables, the deleted atoms, the bound variables, the
% head's formulas, the guards.
procedure sas_faults(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SLits?, SLits?, SConstraint?, PNames?, Faults).
sas_faults(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G, R?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?), ground(G?) |
    sas_ana(H?, B?, Cn?, A),
    sas_faults0(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, A?, G?, R).

procedure sas_faults0(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SA?, PNames?, Faults).
sas_faults0(Nm, Ns, Vs, A, G, R?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(A?), ground(G?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_table_of(Ns?, A?, G?, E),
    sas_faults1(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, A?, G?, E?, R).

procedure sas_faults1(Constant?, Names?, PNames?, SA?, PNames?, REnts?, Faults).
sas_faults1(Nm, Ns, Vs, A, G, E, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(G?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?) |
    sas_sctx(A?, G?, E?, Vs?, Cx),
    sas_faults2(Nm?, Ns?, A?, Cx?, R).

procedure sas_faults2(Constant?, Names?, SA?, SCtx?, Faults).
sas_faults2(Nm, Ns, sa(HP, HQ, HF, BP, BQ, BF, Cn, PP, AQ, CQ, AA, Bs, Cs, Ks),
            sctx(HP1, HQ1, BP1, BQ1, G, E, Vs, IC, Vq, Bs1, Smp), R?) :-
    ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?), ground(HP?), ground(HQ?), ground(HF?), ground(BP?), ground(BQ?), ground(BF?),
    ground(Cn?), ground(PP?), ground(AQ?), ground(CQ?), ground(AA?), ground(Bs?), ground(Cs?), ground(Ks?),
    ground(HP1?), ground(HQ1?), ground(BP1?), ground(BQ1?), ground(G?), ground(E?), ground(Vs?), ground(IC?),
    ground(Vq?), ground(Bs1?), ground(Smp?) |
    sas_qvars(Bs?, [], Xs),
    sas_qvars(Bs?, [], Xs2),
    sas_vk3(num, AA?, Cs?, Ks?, Nn),
    sas_vk3(real, AA?, Cs?, Ks?, Nr),
    sas_type_faults(Nn?, Nr?, Nm?, [], F7),
    sas_gfaults(G?, Nm?, E?, F7?, F6),
    sas_hffaults(HF?, Nm?, F6?, F5),
    sas_qfaults(Xs?, Nm?, sa(HP?, HQ?, HF?, BP?, BQ?, BF?, Cn?, PP?, AQ?, CQ?, AA?, Bs?, Cs?, Ks?), E?, F5?, F4),
    sas_del_faults(E?, Nm?, sctx(HP1?, HQ1?, BP1?, BQ1?, G?, E?, Vs?, IC?, Vq?, Bs1?, Smp?), F4?, F3),
    sas_cons_vf(Cn?, E?, Vs?, Nm?, F3?, F2c),
    sas_leaves_vf(CQ?, E?, Vq?, Nm?, F2c?, F2b),
    sas_atoms_vf(AQ?, E?, Vq?, Nm?, F2b?, F2),
    sas_lits_vf(PP?, E?, Vs?, Nm?, F2?, F1),
    sas_holder_faults(AA?, Nm?, Ns?, Xs2?, F1?, R).

% A value variable written num(X) and real(X) both, of two types, is a fault
% value_type(Schema, X): "a value variable of a schema has a type, which the
% schema's term form writes" (GSC 8b1460f, the appendix "Values in
% Speech-Act Schemas").
procedure sas_type_faults(PNames?, PNames?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_type_faults([], _, _, T, T?).
sas_type_faults([X|Xs], Rl, Nm, T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Xs?), ground(Rl?), ground(Nm?), ground(T?) |
    sas_in(X?, Rl?, A),
    sas_in(X?, Xs?, D),
    flip(D?, Last),
    both_yes(A?, Last?, B),
    sas_type_faults(Xs?, Rl?, Nm?, T?, R1),
    sas_type_fault(B?, X?, Nm?, R1?, R).

procedure sas_type_fault(Ans?, Constant?, Constant?, Faults?, Faults).
sas_type_fault(no, _, _, T, T?).
sas_type_fault(yes, X, Nm, T, [value_type(Nm?, X?)|T?]).

% The faults of the reading of a contract: those of each schema written as a
% clause, none of a schema written in the checker's form.
procedure wsch_faults(WSchema?, Faults).
wsch_faults(sas(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G), R?) :- sas_faults(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, H?, B?, Cn?, G?, R).
wsch_faults(_, []) :- otherwise | true.

procedure wcontract_faults(WContract?, Faults).
wcontract_faults([], []).
wcontract_faults([S|Ss], R?) :-
    wsch_faults(S?, F1),
    wcontract_faults(Ss?, F2),
    sas_fapp(F1?, F2?, R).

procedure wbody_faults(WBody?, Faults).
wbody_faults([], []).
wbody_faults([S|Ss], R?) :- wcontract_faults([S?|Ss?], R).
wbody_faults(reflexive(_, Ss), R?) :- wcontract_faults(Ss?, R).

procedure read_faults(WDeclared?, Faults).
read_faults([], []).
read_faults([S|Ss], R?) :- wcontract_faults([S?|Ss?], R).
read_faults(reflexive(_, Ss), R?) :- wcontract_faults(Ss?, R).
read_faults(environment(_, B), R?) :- wbody_faults(B?, R).

% --- The image of a binding (def:schema, def:binding) ----------------------
% People and speech acts are numbered; person(0) and person(1) are the two
% the conditions quantify over.  signed(S, P) is the image of a signed term,
% the pair of the speech act S and the person P in its role
% (def:binding).  undef marks a variable that a partial substitution leaves
% unbound and occurs in no completed one.  nval(N) is the image of a value
% argument that is the number N, or a value variable a binding sends to N;
% nfree(X) is the image of the value variable X of the introductory act,
% whose value its introduction chooses (def:binding-numbers): a match that
% meets it records the equation it rests on (Eqs, below), which the values
% chosen must satisfy (unobstructed.glp).  A value names no agent (GSC,
% Section 3.2), so neither names anyone.  vany is the image of the wildcard
% in an atom the act requires or forbids, which any argument meets
% (def:binding, "matches").  utt(S) is the image of an item item(y), the
% utterance under the signatures of the speech act a binding sends y to, S
% that speech act with its signatures over it removed, signed(S, P) carrying
% the utterance S carries (GSC 4401dd6: "a binding sends item(y) to the
% utterance beta(y) carries, so an item holds the same program, or the same
% post, whoever signed it over"); an utterance names no agent.
Val   ::= person(Integer) ; speech(Integer) ; signed(Val, Val) ; undef
        ; nval(Constant) ; nfree(Constant) ; vany ; utt(Val).
Vals  ::= [] ; [Val | Vals].
GAtom ::= gatom(Constant, Vals).

Bind     ::= bind(Arg, Val).
Subst    ::= [] ; [Bind | Subst].
Substs   ::= [] ; [Subst | Substs].
Found    ::= bound(Val) ; free.
% match(S, E): the atoms match under S where the equations E between values
% hold, each between two images of value arguments, nval or nfree.
Eq       ::= eqv(Val, Val).
Eqs      ::= [] ; [Eq | Eqs].
MatchRes ::= match(Subst, Eqs) ; nomatch.

% --- What clause 2 of def:unobstructed is decided against ------------------
% The other party of the introduction, and the first unused name index.
Ctx ::= ctx(Val, Integer).

% --- Verdicts --------------------------------------------------------------
Ans   ::= yes ; no.
Ints  ::= [] ; [Integer | Ints].
Preds ::= [] ; [Constant | Preds].
% listed_role(Schema, Role, Atom) is the first part of clause 2 of
% def:unobstructed: the listed role Role of Schema adds Atom, of the
% predicate of an atom the introductory act forbids at a role.
Cause ::= unobtainable ; blocked_by(Constant, Integer, Atom) ; reflexive ; environment
        ; listed_role(Constant, Integer, Atom).
% What GAI's Definition Speech-act schema requires of a signed term, and the atom
% carrying one violates: it occurs in an atom not marked + (not_added), its
% speech-act variable occurs in no atom its role requires (not_required), or
% its role is not an agent role (not_agent_role).
SgnCause ::= not_added ; not_required ; not_agent_role.
% What def:schema requires of the form of a schema, and a schema formed
% otherwise violates: no role adding or deleting an atom (no_role_changes).
% What def:volition requires of a reading role (GSC 0380a8a, 5e014fd), a role
% that is not guarding and adds and deletes nothing: an edge to a guarding role
% from an atom that guarding role requires, or to be a listed role whose base
% is a guarding role; a reading role with neither is a fault
% changes_nothing(Schema, Role) of volition, in a verdict not_grassroots.
% What def:volition requires of a schema with no guarding role and a reading
% role (GSC c100cdc, 5e014fd): signature atoms (def:signature), so one with
% none is a fault no_signature_atom(Schema), and only agent roles as reading
% roles, so
% each listed reading role is a fault listed_reading(Schema, Role), in a
% verdict not_grassroots.  What def:schema requires of a schema's head, its
% variables distinct agent, speech-act and value variables: an entry of the
% head that is not a variable (head_not_variable), an entry listed twice
% (head_repeated), and a variable of the schema not in its head
% (not_in_head).  What def:role requires of a name term, <pi> for an agent
% variable pi of it or sigma.y for a name term sigma of it: one written
% over a role index the schema has not (name_term_base), naming the schema
% and the name term.  What def:role requires of a listed role, and one
% violates: its condition held by an agent role of its schema (listed_base),
% and no signed term (GAI's) in its condition, a signed term occurring only
% in an atom marked + (listed_signed); each names the schema and the listed
% role.  What def:numbers requires of a multiplicity: a positive whole number
% or a value variable, so one that is no value argument is a fault
% multiplicity_not_numeric(Schema, Role, Atom), and one that is a number and
% no positive whole number a fault multiplicity_not_whole(Schema, Role,
% Atom); and on an atom with no wildcard, so one on an atom carrying the
% wildcard is a fault multiplicity_wildcard(Schema, Role, Atom).  A
% constraint is on the schema's value variables, so an argument of it that
% is no value argument, but in eq or ne of two agent variables, is a fault
% constraint_not_numeric(Schema, Arg).  A value variable is a variable of the
% schema, listed in its head like the others (not_in_head, head_repeated),
% and a number in the head is no variable (head_not_variable).  What
% def:numbers requires of a signing condition signed(u, y) or unsigned(u, y)
% (GSC 10fcc92), and of u = v and u != v: u an agent role or agent variable,
% so any other u is a fault signing_not_agent(Schema, U); and y a speech-act
% variable, so any other y is a fault signing_not_speech_act(Schema, Y); a
% variable among them that the head does not list is a fault
% not_in_head(Schema, Var).
Fault ::= no_introductory_act
        ; obstructed(Constant, Integer, Atom, Cause)
        ; untraceable(Preds)
        ; volition(Constant, Integer, Integer)
        ; reflexive(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; signed(Constant, Integer, Atom, SgnCause)
        ; changes_nothing(Constant, Integer)
        ; listed_reading(Constant, Integer)
        ; no_signature_atom(Constant)
        ; no_role_changes(Constant)
        ; head_not_variable(Constant, Arg)
        ; head_repeated(Constant, Arg)
        ; not_in_head(Constant, Arg)
        ; name_term_base(Constant, NameTerm)
        ; listed_base(Constant, Integer)
        ; listed_signed(Constant, Integer)
        ; multiplicity_not_numeric(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; multiplicity_not_whole(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; multiplicity_wildcard(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; constraint_not_numeric(Constant, Arg)
        ; signing_not_agent(Constant, Arg)
        ; signing_not_speech_act(Constant, Arg)
        ; obstructed_jointly(Constant)
        ; not_holder(Constant, Constant)
        ; not_in_vars(Constant, Constant)
        ; deleted_not_required(Constant, Integer, Atom)
        ; condition_holder(Constant, Constant)
        ; head_formula(Constant)
        ; quantified_condition(Constant, Constant)
        ; listed_agent_role(Constant, Constant)
        ; guard_not_role(Constant, Constant)
        ; value_type(Constant, Constant)
        ; item_argument(Constant, Constant).
Faults  ::= [] ; [Fault | Faults].
% What def:signature is decided against (volition.glp): sig(Is, Cj, OA, OD,
% TA, TD), the indices of a schema's agent roles, its conjuncts, the
% predicates of the atoms it adds and of those it deletes or clears, and the
% same of the other schemas with no guarding role.  sb(Some, Bs): whether some
% atom at a role is the only one of its predicate, and the bases of the
% arguments of those that are.
SigCtx  ::= sig(Ints, Conjuncts, Preds, Preds, Preds, Preds).
SigBases ::= sb(Ans, Bases).

% --- What an introduction with wards is made of (GAI, "Contracts with Wards")
% guardianship(M, Iota, G, W, V) is the guardianship (m, iota, g, w, v) of
% def:guardianship; a party of a relay act (def:relay) is a ward role,
% ward(Role, Mark, Guardian), Guardian its guardian role, guardian(Role), or
% no_guardian, a ward role having at most one guardian role (GAI 6b64d3d,
% def:relay, clause 1: "with at most one other role sigma of chi, its guardian
% role"; GnW:3 and GnW:4, agent_acquaint and agents_acquaint, have none), or a
% free role, free(Role); a relay act is named with its two parties.  An introduction with wards
% (def:introduction-wards) names the introductory act unobstructed but for
% the marks, the set of marks, the guardianship of each and the relay acts
% found: for each mark one with a free role, and for each pair of marks, in
% the order of the set, one with a ward role of each; and the leaving marks
% of the contract (def:leaving), in the order of its marks.
Guardianship  ::= guardianship(Constant, Constant, Constant, Constant, Constant).
Guardianships ::= [] ; [Guardianship | Guardianships].
Guardian ::= guardian(Integer) ; no_guardian.
Party  ::= ward(Integer, Constant, Guardian) ; free(Integer).
Parties ::= [] ; [Party | Parties].
Relay  ::= relay(Constant, Party, Party).
Relays ::= [] ; [Relay | Relays].
Wards  ::= introduction_with_wards(Constant, Preds, Guardianships, Relays, Preds)
         ; no_introduction_with_wards.
% h(Schema, Role, H): the relay act Schema requires at its ward role Role an atom of the predicate H that clause 2 of def:relay admits as an atom of h and as nothing else (GSC 410a440).
RelayH  ::= h(Constant, Integer, Constant).
RelayHs ::= [] ; [RelayH | RelayHs].
% The leaving marks of a contract for a set M of marks (def:leaving) depend
% on the guardianship of each mark in M: leaving(Gs, Ls) holds the
% guardianships taken, one per mark, and the leaving marks for them.
Leaving  ::= leaving(Guardianships, Preds).
Leavings ::= [] ; [Leaving | Leavings].

% What the search of wards.glp carries: the sets of marks it tries, the
% guardianship candidates of each mark of a set, the kind of each role of a
% schema put to def:relay -- a ward role of a mark with its guardian role, a
% free role, a guardian role, or none of these -- the kind of party sought,
% and an introductory act unobstructed but for the marks with its predicate e.
PredSets   ::= [] ; [Preds | PredSets].
GuardLists ::= [] ; [Guardianships | GuardLists].
RK   ::= rk_ward(Constant, Guardian) ; rk_free ; rk_guard ; rk_other.
RKs  ::= [] ; [RK | RKs].
Kind ::= free_party ; ward_party(Constant).
IntroE ::= intro(Constant, Constant) ; no_intro.

% syntactically_grassroots is the verdict on a contract that is so by
% def:syntactically-grassroots, of agent roles and listed roles alike (GSC
% ac7ad63).  grassroots_with_wards is the verdict on a contract with no
% listed role and no name term that is grassroots with wards by GAI's
% appendix "Contracts with Wards", and syntactically_grassroots_with_wards
% the verdict on one with them that is syntactically grassroots with wards by
% def:sg-wards of CSSN's paper, naming what grassroots_with_wards names.
Verdict ::= syntactically_grassroots ; not_grassroots(Faults)
          ; syntactically_grassroots_with_wards(Constant, Preds, Guardianships, Relays, Preds)
          ; grassroots_with_wards(Constant, Preds, Guardianships, Relays, Preds)
          ; malformed(Faults).

% The introductory acts of a contract, for inspection (def:introduction,
% def:unobstructed): intro_act(Schema, Status), each schema that is an
% introductory act, Status unobstructed where some introduction of it meets
% def:unobstructed, and obstructed(Faults) otherwise, the faults of its first
% introduction.
IntroStatus ::= unobstructed ; obstructed(Faults).
IntroAct    ::= intro_act(Constant, IntroStatus).
IntroActs   ::= [] ; [IntroAct | IntroActs].

% What an introduction is decided by (unobstructed.glp): an introduction
% meeting def:unobstructed (t_ok), the faults where none does (t_bad), or
% none at all (t_none); the act, its plain form, the contract as written and
% plain, and its reflexive predicates (IntroCtx); and each condition the
% clauses put to its values, with the fault it is where no choice of them
% meets it (Item): an atom required at a role, with the formula saying that
% a schema of arity one supplies it; an atom forbidden at a role, with the
% bindings of other schemas adding it (Blk, each the formula saying where
% it adds it) and the formula saying that none does; or a fault the values
% do not touch.
Try      ::= t_ok ; t_bad(Faults) ; t_none.
IntroCtx ::= ic(Schema, NSchema, NContract, Contract, Preds).
Blk      ::= blk(Constant, Integer, Atom, DNF).
Blks     ::= [] ; [Blk | Blks].
Item     ::= it_req(Integer, Atom, DNF) ; it_forb(Integer, Atom, Blks, DNF)
           ; it_fault(Fault).
Items    ::= [] ; [Item | Items].
% How the value variables of another schema's binding are named: those of a
% schema of arity one supplying the atom Is names, or those of a schema
% whose bindings are eliminated (Name, below).  Two images are equal where
% the atoms of a conjunction hold, or never (eqr_no).
Tg       ::= tg_sv(Ints) ; tg_bv.
EqR      ::= eqr(Conj) ; eqr_no.
Cand    ::= none ; some(Faults).
Missing ::= missing(Integer) ; all_reached.

% --- Linear arithmetic over the values (linear.glp) ------------------------
% A variable over the values: q(N) ranges over the rationals and z(N) over
% the whole numbers, a multiplicity carrying its bound N >= 1 as an atom.
% Its name: iv(X), the value variable X of the introductory act; sv(Is, X),
% the value variable X of a schema of arity one supplying the atom Is names;
% bv(X), the value variable X of a schema whose bindings are eliminated
% (linear.glp, elim_block); and nv(X) and fv(X), the whole and the
% fractional parts of the act's rational value X.  A linear form is
% lin(Terms, C), the sum of each term's coefficient times its variable,
% plus C, all whole numbers; an atom is geq(L), L >= 0, grt(L), L > 0,
% equ(L), L = 0, or dvd(M, L), M divides L; a conjunction is a list of atoms
% and a formula a list of conjunctions, their disjunction.
Name      ::= iv(Constant) ; sv(Ints, Constant) ; bv(Constant) ; nv(Constant)
            ; fv(Constant).
Var       ::= q(Name) ; z(Name).
Vars      ::= [] ; [Var | Vars].
Term      ::= t(Var, Integer).
Terms     ::= [] ; [Term | Terms].
Lin       ::= lin(Terms, Integer).
LAtom     ::= geq(Lin) ; grt(Lin) ; equ(Lin) ; dvd(Integer, Lin).
Conj      ::= [] ; [LAtom | Conj].
DNF       ::= [] ; [Conj | DNF].
DNFs      ::= [] ; [DNF | DNFs].
Constants ::= [] ; [Constant | Constants].
% What linear.glp carries: a conjunction simplified, or false; the truth of
% an atom, settled or open; an expression, the form divided by a positive
% whole number, or none where it is not linear; the variables a constraint's
% value variables are read as; an equation found, with the rest of its
% conjunction; the kind of variable sought; a bound on V' = d.V of Cooper's
% method, Sign.V' + t of its kind; a value of the ceiling, the floor or the
% value of a sum of fractional parts, with the atoms that say so; and the
% direction a bound is met from.
CS        ::= cs(Conj) ; cs_false.
LTv       ::= lt_true ; lt_false ; lt_open.
Ex        ::= ex(Lin, Integer) ; ex_bad.
% cd(D, W): the formula D over the values, and whether all of the constraint
% it stands for was read (cons_cd).
Cd        ::= cd(DNF, Ans).
VBind     ::= vb(Constant, Var).
VEnv      ::= [] ; [VBind | VEnv].
FoundEq   ::= fe(Lin, Conj) ; fe_none(Conj).
VSel      ::= sel_q ; sel_z ; sel_bq ; sel_bz.
VPick     ::= pick(Var) ; pick_none.
BKind     ::= b_geq ; b_grt ; b_dvd(Integer).
Bd        ::= bd(BKind, Integer, Lin).
Bds       ::= [] ; [Bd | Bds].
QKind     ::= ceil_case ; floor_case ; eq_case.
QCase     ::= qc(Integer, Conj).
QCases    ::= [] ; [QCase | QCases].
Dir       ::= low ; up.

% --- What def:grounded is decided against, for one schema ----------------
% The bases of its roles, the bases of the arguments of the atoms of Phi_E it
% requires, the speech-act variables occurring in those atoms, and the
% speech-act variables occurring in any atom it requires.
PCtx ::= pctx(Bases, Bases, Args, Args).

% --- The LaTeX of a compiled schema (def:compile) -------------------------
% GLP has no string concatenation, so a display is carried as its tokens and
% printed one to a line; a newline is whitespace to LaTeX, so the lines are
% the display.  ChunkLists holds the conjuncts of the proviso, each a display
% of its own, before they are joined.
Chunks     ::= [] ; [Constant | Chunks].
ChunkLists ::= [] ; [Chunks | ChunkLists].
FoundS     ::= found(Schema) ; not_found.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Booleans
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure both_yes(Ans?, Ans?, Ans).
both_yes(yes, A, A?).
both_yes(no, _, no).

procedure or_yes(Ans?, Ans?, Ans).
or_yes(yes, _, yes).
or_yes(no, A, A?).

procedure flip(Ans?, Ans).
flip(yes, no).
flip(no, yes).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Lists
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure args_app(Args?, Args?, Args).
args_app([], T, T?).
args_app([A|As], T, [A?|R?]) :- args_app(As?, T?, R).

procedure atoms_app(Atoms?, Atoms?, Atoms).
atoms_app([], T, T?).
atoms_app([A|As], T, [A?|R?]) :- atoms_app(As?, T?, R).

procedure preds_app(Preds?, Preds?, Preds).
preds_app([], T, T?).
preds_app([P|Ps], T, [P?|R?]) :- preds_app(Ps?, T?, R).

procedure nterms_app(NameTerms?, NameTerms?, NameTerms).
nterms_app([], T, T?).
nterms_app([N|Ns], T, [N?|R?]) :- nterms_app(Ns?, T?, R).

procedure bases_app(Bases?, Bases?, Bases).
bases_app([], T, T?).
bases_app([B|Bs], T, [B?|R?]) :- bases_app(Bs?, T?, R).

procedure faults_app(Faults?, Faults?, Faults).
faults_app([], T, T?).
faults_app([F|Fs], T, [F?|R?]) :- faults_app(Fs?, T?, R).

procedure contract_app(Contract?, Contract?, Contract).
contract_app([], T, T?).
contract_app([S|Ss], T, [S?|R?]) :- contract_app(Ss?, T?, R).

procedure preds_len(Preds?, Integer).
preds_len([], 0).
preds_len([_|Xs], N?) :- preds_len(Xs?, M), N := M? + 1.

procedure roles_len(RoleSpecs?, Integer).
roles_len([], 0).
roles_len([_|Xs], N?) :- roles_len(Xs?, M), N := M? + 1.

procedure ints_len(Ints?, Integer).
ints_len([], 0).
ints_len([_|Xs], N?) :- ints_len(Xs?, M), N := M? + 1.

procedure pred_member(Constant?, Preds?, Ans).
pred_member(_, [], no).
pred_member(P, [Q|_], yes) :- P? =?= Q? | true.
pred_member(P, [_|Qs], R?) :- otherwise | pred_member(P?, Qs?, R).

procedure args_member(Args?, Arg?, Ans).
args_member([], _, no).
args_member([A|_], U, yes) :- A? =?= U? | true.
args_member([_|As], U, R?) :- otherwise | args_member(As?, U?, R).

procedure base_member(Bases?, Base?, Ans).
base_member([], _, no).
base_member([B|_], C, yes) :- B? =?= C? | true.
base_member([_|Bs], C, R?) :- otherwise | base_member(Bs?, C?, R).

procedure nt_member(NameTerms?, NameTerm?, Ans).
nt_member([], _, no).
nt_member([N|_], M, yes) :- N? =?= M? | true.
nt_member([_|Ns], M, R?) :- otherwise | nt_member(Ns?, M?, R).

procedure vals_member(Vals?, Val?, Ans).
vals_member([], _, no).
vals_member([V|_], W, yes) :- V? =?= W? | true.
vals_member([_|Vs], W, R?) :- otherwise | vals_member(Vs?, W?, R).

procedure ints_member(Ints?, Integer?, Ans).
ints_member([], _, no).
ints_member([I|_], J, yes) :- I? =:= J? | true.
ints_member([_|Is], J, R?) :- otherwise | ints_member(Is?, J?, R).

% args_remove(As, A, R): every occurrence of A dropped from As.
procedure args_remove(Args?, Arg?, Args).
args_remove([], _, []).
args_remove([B|As], A, R?) :- B? =?= A? | args_remove(As?, A?, R).
args_remove([B|As], A, [B?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(B?) | args_remove(As?, A?, R).

procedure args_dedup(Args?, Args).
args_dedup([], []).
args_dedup([A|As], [A?|R?]) :- ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    args_remove(As?, A?, As1),
    args_dedup(As1?, R).

procedure preds_remove(Preds?, Constant?, Preds).
preds_remove([], _, []).
preds_remove([Q|Ps], P, R?) :- Q? =?= P? | preds_remove(Ps?, P?, R).
preds_remove([Q|Ps], P, [Q?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(Q?) | preds_remove(Ps?, P?, R).

procedure preds_dedup(Preds?, Preds).
preds_dedup([], []).
preds_dedup([P|Ps], [P?|R?]) :- ground(P?), ground(Ps?) |
    preds_remove(Ps?, P?, Ps1),
    preds_dedup(Ps1?, R).

% preds_diff(Ps, E, R): the members of Ps not in E, in the order of Ps.
procedure preds_diff1(Ans?, Constant?, Preds?, Preds?, Preds).
preds_diff1(yes, _, Ps, E, R?) :- ground(Ps?), ground(E?) | preds_diff(Ps?, E?, R).
preds_diff1(no, P, Ps, E, [P?|R?]) :- ground(Ps?), ground(E?) | preds_diff(Ps?, E?, R).

procedure preds_diff(Preds?, Preds?, Preds).
preds_diff([], _, []).
preds_diff([P|Ps], E, R?) :- ground(P?), ground(Ps?), ground(E?) |
    pred_member(P?, E?, A),
    preds_diff1(A?, P?, Ps?, E?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Substitutions
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure subst_lookup(Subst?, Arg?, Found).
subst_lookup([], _, free).
subst_lookup([bind(A, V)|_], B, bound(V?)) :- A? =?= B? | true.
subst_lookup([bind(_, _)|S], B, R?) :- otherwise | subst_lookup(S?, B?, R).

procedure subst_app(Subst?, Subst?, Subst).
subst_app([], T, T?).
subst_app([B|Bs], T, [B?|R?]) :- subst_app(Bs?, T?, R).

procedure unwrap_val(Found?, Val).
unwrap_val(bound(V), V?).
unwrap_val(free, undef).

% apply_arg/apply_atom: the image under a binding, written beta(phi) in
% Section 3.  A completed substitution binds every variable of the schema, so
% undef never reaches an atom.  The image of a signed term is the pair of the
% speech act its variable maps to and the person in its role (def:binding).
procedure apply_arg(Subst?, Arg?, Val).
apply_arg(S, sgn(Y, J), signed(SV?, PV?)) :- ground(S?), ground(Y?), integer(J?) |
    apply_arg(S?, svar(Y?), SV),
    apply_arg(S?, role(J?), PV).
apply_arg(S, num(X), V?) :- ground(S?), ground(X?) | apply_num(S?, X?, V).
apply_arg(_, any, vany).
apply_arg(S, item_of(Y), V?) :- ground(S?), ground(Y?) |
    apply_arg(S?, Y?, W),
    item_val(W?, V).
apply_arg(S, A, V?) :- otherwise, ground(S?), ground(A?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, A?, F),
    unwrap_val(F?, V).

% The item of a speech act: the utterance under its signatures (utt, Val).
procedure item_val(Val?, Val).
item_val(signed(S, _), V?) :- item_val(S?, V).
item_val(W, utt(W?)) :- otherwise | true.

% The image of a value argument (GSC, Section 3.2): the number itself, or
% what the binding sends the value variable to; one the binding leaves free
% is written nfree, as a value not yet chosen.
procedure apply_num(Subst?, Constant?, Val).
apply_num(_, X, nval(X?)) :- number(X?) | true.
apply_num(S, X, V?) :- otherwise, ground(S?), ground(X?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, num(X?), F),
    unwrap_num(F?, X?, V).

procedure unwrap_num(Found?, Constant?, Val).
unwrap_num(bound(V), _, V?).
unwrap_num(free, X, nfree(X?)).

procedure apply_args(Subst?, Args?, Vals).
apply_args(_, [], []).
apply_args(S, [A|As], [V?|Vs?]) :- ground(S?), ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    apply_arg(S?, A?, V),
    apply_args(S?, As?, Vs).

procedure apply_atom(Subst?, Atom?, GAtom).
apply_atom(S, atom(P, As), gatom(P?, Vs?)) :- ground(S?), ground(P?), ground(As?) |
    apply_args(S?, As?, Vs).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Matching a schema's atom against a ground one
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% match_atom(Psi, G, Rs, S, R): the bindings extending S under which Psi
% becomes G, if any, Rs being the roles of Psi's schema.  A binding sends
% roles and party variables to people, two roles to one person only if
% neither of them adds or deletes an atom naming the other, and speech-act
% variables to speech acts (def:binding); kind_ok and binding_ok below are
% exactly those requirements.

procedure kind_ok(Arg?, Val?, Ans).
kind_ok(role(_), person(_), yes).
kind_ok(role(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(role(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(role(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(role(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(role(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(role(_), utt(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), person(_), yes).
kind_ok(pvar(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(pvar(_), utt(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), speech(_), yes).
kind_ok(svar(_), signed(_, _), yes).
kind_ok(svar(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(svar(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(svar(_), utt(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(nterm(_), utt(_), no).
% A signed term is matched by its two parts (match_sgn below), never here.
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), person(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), signed(_, _), yes).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), undef, no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), nval(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), nfree(_), no).
kind_ok(sgn(_, _), utt(_), no).
% A value argument matches a number and nothing else (match_num below).
kind_ok(num(_), nval(_), yes).
kind_ok(num(_), nfree(_), yes).
kind_ok(num(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(num(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(num(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(num(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(num(_), utt(_), no).
kind_ok(real(_), nval(_), yes).
kind_ok(real(_), nfree(_), yes).
kind_ok(real(_), person(_), no).
kind_ok(real(_), speech(_), no).
kind_ok(real(_), signed(_, _), no).
kind_ok(real(_), undef, no).
kind_ok(real(_), utt(_), no).
% The wildcard and an item are matched by match_one, never here.
kind_ok(any, _, no).
kind_ok(item_of(_), _, no).

% roles_at(S, V, Js): the indices of the roles S sends to V.  Clause 2 of
% def:unobstructed asks of the other party that one of them be no reading
% role (some_not_reading).
procedure roles_at(Subst?, Val?, Ints).
roles_at([], _, []).
roles_at([bind(role(J), W)|S], V, [J?|R?]) :- W? =?= V? | roles_at(S?, V?, R).
roles_at([bind(_, _)|S], V, R?) :- otherwise | roles_at(S?, V?, R).

% args_name_role(As, J, R): the arguments As name role J -- it is among them
% or is the role of a signed term among them (Section 3.1, what an atom
% names in a schema).
procedure arg_names_role(Arg?, Integer?, Ans).
arg_names_role(role(I), J, yes) :- I? =:= J? | true.
arg_names_role(sgn(_, I), J, yes) :- I? =:= J? | true.
arg_names_role(A, _, no) :- otherwise, ground(A?) | true.

procedure args_name_role1(Ans?, Args?, Integer?, Ans).
args_name_role1(yes, _, _, yes).
args_name_role1(no, As, J, R?) :- ground(As?), integer(J?) | args_name_role(As?, J?, R).

procedure args_name_role(Args?, Integer?, Ans).
args_name_role([], _, no).
args_name_role([A|As], J, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?), integer(J?) |
    arg_names_role(A?, J?, A1),
    args_name_role1(A1?, As?, J?, R).

% names_role(Phis, J, R): some atom of Phis names role J.
procedure names_role1(Ans?, Atoms?, Integer?, Ans).
names_role1(yes, _, _, yes).
names_role1(no, Xs, J, R?) :- ground(Xs?), integer(J?) | names_role(Xs?, J?, R).

procedure names_role(Atoms?, Integer?, Ans).
names_role([], _, no).
names_role([atom(_, As)|Xs], J, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(Xs?), integer(J?) |
    args_name_role(As?, J?, A),
    names_role1(A?, Xs?, J?, R).

% atoms_member(Phis, Phi, R): Phi is one of Phis.
procedure atoms_member(Atoms?, Atom?, Ans).
atoms_member([], _, no).
atoms_member([A|_], B, yes) :- A? =?= B? | true.
atoms_member([_|As], B, R?) :- otherwise | atoms_member(As?, B?, R).

% role_names(RS, J, R): the role adds or deletes an atom naming role J.  A
% cleared atom naming J, as unfriend's listed(Bob, *) at Alice, deletes every
% atom it matches (def:schema), each naming J, so it counts as deleting one.
procedure role_names(RoleSpec?, Integer?, Ans).
role_names(RS, J, R?) :- ground(RS?), integer(J?) |
    rs_add(RS?, P),
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    names_role(P?, J?, A1),
    names_role(M?, J?, A2),
    or_yes(A1?, A2?, R).

% may_share(Rs, J, K, R): a binding may send roles J and K to one person:
% neither of them adds or deletes an atom naming the other (def:binding).
procedure may_share(RoleSpecs?, Integer?, Integer?, Ans).
may_share(Rs, J, K, R?) :- ground(Rs?), integer(J?), integer(K?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, J?, RJ),
    nth_rs(Rs?, K?, RK),
    role_names(RJ?, K?, A1),
    role_names(RK?, J?, A2),
    or_yes(A1?, A2?, A),
    flip(A?, R).

procedure all_share1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Ints?, Integer?, Ans).
all_share1(no, _, _, _, no).
all_share1(yes, Rs, Js, K, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(Js?), integer(K?) |
    all_share(Rs?, Js?, K?, R).

% all_share(Rs, Js, K, R): role K may take the person of every role in Js.
procedure all_share(RoleSpecs?, Ints?, Integer?, Ans).
all_share(_, [], _, yes).
all_share(Rs, [J|Js], K, R?) :- ground(Rs?), integer(J?), ground(Js?), integer(K?) |
    may_share(Rs?, J?, K?, A),
    all_share1(A?, Rs?, Js?, K?, R).

% A role may take V when every role S already sends to V may share it.
procedure binding_ok(Arg?, Val?, Subst?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
binding_ok(role(K), V, S, Rs, R?) :- integer(K?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(Rs?) |
    roles_at(S?, V?, Js),
    all_share(Rs?, Js?, K?, R).
binding_ok(pvar(_), _, _, _, yes).
binding_ok(svar(_), _, _, _, yes).
binding_ok(nterm(_), _, _, _, yes).
% A signed term is no variable and is matched by its parts (match_sgn).
binding_ok(sgn(_, _), _, _, _, no).
% A value argument is matched by match_num, never here.
binding_ok(num(_), _, _, _, no).
binding_ok(real(_), _, _, _, no).
binding_ok(any, _, _, _, no).
binding_ok(item_of(_), _, _, _, no).

procedure match_bind(Ans?, Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_bind(yes, A, V, S, E, match([bind(A?, V?)|S?], E?)).
match_bind(no, _, _, _, _, nomatch).

procedure val_same(Val?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
val_same(W, V, S, E, match(S?, E?)) :- W? =?= V? | true.
val_same(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure match_one1(Found?, Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_one1(free, A, V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(A?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    kind_ok(A?, V?, K),
    binding_ok(A?, V?, S?, Rs?, I),
    both_yes(K?, I?, Ok),
    match_bind(Ok?, A?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_one1(bound(W), _, V, S, E, _, R?) :- ground(W?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    val_same(W?, V?, S?, E?, R).

% A signed term sgn(y, pi) matches a signed value by its two parts, the
% speech-act variable against the speech act and the role against the person
% (def:binding: beta(sgn(y, pi)) := (beta(y), beta(pi))), and matches no
% person and no speech act: the speech acts of an introduction are taken
% signed once (README, "One thing to know about the reading").
procedure match_sgn(Constant?, Integer?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_sgn(Y, J, signed(SV, PV), S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(Y?), integer(J?), ground(SV?), ground(PV?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_one(svar(Y?), SV?, S?, E?, Rs?, R1),
    match_rest(R1?, [role(J?)], [PV?], Rs?, R).
match_sgn(_, _, person(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, speech(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, undef, _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, nval(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, nfree(_), _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, vany, _, _, _, nomatch).
match_sgn(_, _, utt(_), _, _, _, nomatch).

% A value argument num(X) matches a value by equality (def:unobstructed, at
% a binding of its schema; def:binding-numbers): the number X matches the
% number equal to it, and the value variable X is sent to the value it meets,
% or matches it if the binding sends X to it already.  Where one side is a
% value of the introductory act (nfree), whose value its introduction
% chooses, the match holds where the two are equal, and records the
% equation (eqv), which unobstructed.glp puts to the values.
procedure match_num(Constant?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_num(X, V, S, E, R?) :- number(X?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    match_lit(X?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_num(X, V, S, E, R?) :- otherwise, ground(X?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, num(X?), F),
    match_nvar(F?, X?, V?, S?, E?, R).

procedure match_lit(Constant?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_lit(X, nval(N), S, E, R?) :- number(N?), ground(S?), ground(E?) | num_eq(X?, N?, S?, E?, R).
match_lit(X, nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nval(X?), nfree(Y?))|E?])).
match_lit(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure num_eq(Constant?, Constant?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
num_eq(X, N, S, E, match(S?, E?)) :- X? =:= N? | true.
num_eq(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure match_nvar(Found?, Constant?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_nvar(free, X, nval(N), S, E, match([bind(num(X?), nval(N?))|S?], E?)).
match_nvar(free, X, nfree(Y), S, E, match([bind(num(X?), nfree(Y?))|S?], E?)).
match_nvar(bound(W), _, V, S, E, R?) :- ground(W?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    num_same(W?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_nvar(_, _, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure num_same(Val?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
num_same(nval(M), nval(N), S, E, R?) :- number(M?), number(N?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    num_eq(M?, N?, S?, E?, R).
num_same(nfree(Z), nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, E?)) :- Z? =?= Y? | true.
num_same(nval(M), nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nval(M?), nfree(Y?))|E?])).
num_same(nfree(Z), nval(N), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nfree(Z?), nval(N?))|E?])).
num_same(nfree(Z), nfree(Y), S, E, match(S?, [eqv(nfree(Z?), nfree(Y?))|E?])) :-
    otherwise | true.
num_same(_, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

% The wildcard is a variable of its own (def:schema), and any argument meets
% the image of one (def:binding, "matches").
procedure match_one(Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_one(_, vany, S, E, _, match(S?, E?)).
match_one(any, _, S, E, _, match(S?, E?)).
match_one(sgn(Y, J), V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(Y?), integer(J?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_sgn(Y?, J?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).
match_one(num(X), V, S, E, _, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    match_num(X?, V?, S?, E?, R).
match_one(item_of(Y), V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(Y?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_item(Y?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).
match_one(A, V, S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    otherwise, ground(A?), ground(V?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, A?, F),
    match_one1(F?, A?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).

procedure match_rest(MatchRes?, Args?, Vals?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_rest(nomatch, _, _, _, nomatch).
match_rest(match(S, E), As, Vs, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(As?), ground(Vs?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_args(As?, Vs?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).

procedure match_args(Args?, Vals?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_args([], [], S, E, _, match(S?, E?)).
match_args([], [_|_], _, _, _, nomatch).
match_args([_|_], [], _, _, _, nomatch).
match_args([A|As], [V|Vs], S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(A?), ground(V?), ground(As?), ground(Vs?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_one(A?, V?, S?, E?, Rs?, R1),
    match_rest(R1?, As?, Vs?, Rs?, R).

% An item item(y) matches an utterance (utt, Val): where the binding sends y
% to a speech act already, the utterance it carries; and otherwise y is sent
% to the speech act the utterance is, which carries it (item_val), as some
% binding does (def:binding-numbers, GSC 4401dd6: "a binding sends item(y)
% to the utterance beta(y) carries").  It matches nothing else but the
% wildcard's image (match_one).
procedure match_item(Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_item(Y, utt(B), S, E, Rs, R?) :-
    ground(Y?), ground(B?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, Y?, F),
    match_item1(F?, Y?, B?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).
match_item(_, _, _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

procedure match_item1(Found?, Arg?, Val?, Subst?, Eqs?, RoleSpecs?, MatchRes).
match_item1(bound(W), _, B, S, E, _, R?) :- ground(W?), ground(B?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    item_val(W?, U),
    val_same(U?, utt(B?), S?, E?, R).
match_item1(free, Y, B, S, E, Rs, R?) :- ground(Y?), ground(B?), ground(S?), ground(E?), ground(Rs?) |
    match_one(Y?, B?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).

% The arguments of an atom with their values, the items last, so that a
% speech-act variable the atom carries is bound before its item is matched
% (match_item).
procedure items_last(Args?, Vals?, Args, Vals).
items_last(As, Vs, A1?, V1?) :- ground(As?), ground(Vs?) |
    split_items(As?, Vs?, NA, NV, IA, IV),
    args_app(NA?, IA?, A1),
    vals_app(NV?, IV?, V1).

procedure split_items(Args?, Vals?, Args, Vals, Args, Vals).
split_items([], [], [], [], [], []).
split_items([item_of(Y)|As], [V|Vs], NA?, NV?, [item_of(Y?)|IA?], [V?|IV?]) :-
    split_items(As?, Vs?, NA, NV, IA, IV).
split_items([A|As], [V|Vs], [A?|NA?], [V?|NV?], IA?, IV?) :- otherwise |
    split_items(As?, Vs?, NA, NV, IA, IV).
split_items(As, Vs, As?, Vs?, [], []) :- otherwise | true.

procedure vals_app(Vals?, Vals?, Vals).
vals_app([], T, T?).
vals_app([V|Vs], T, [V?|R?]) :- vals_app(Vs?, T?, R).

% match_atom(Psi, G, Rs, S, E, R): the match of Psi against G extending the
% binding S and the equations E, its items matched last (items_last).
procedure match_atom(Atom?, GAtom?, RoleSpecs?, Subst?, Eqs?, MatchRes).
match_atom(atom(P, As), gatom(Q, Vs), Rs, S, E, R?) :-
    P? =?= Q?, ground(As?), ground(Vs?), ground(Rs?), ground(S?), ground(E?) |
    items_last(As?, Vs?, As1, Vs1),
    match_args(As1?, Vs1?, S?, E?, Rs?, R).
match_atom(atom(_, _), gatom(_, _), _, _, _, nomatch) :- otherwise | true.

% A positive whole number, the value of a multiplicity (def:numbers,
% def:binding-numbers).
procedure pos_whole(Constant?, Ans).
pos_whole(X, yes) :- number(X?), X? >= 1, X? =:= floor(X?) | true.
pos_whole(_, no) :- otherwise | true.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The variables of a schema
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

procedure atoms_args(Atoms?, Args?, Args).
atoms_args([], T, T?).
atoms_args([atom(_, As)|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(Xs?), ground(T?) |
    atoms_args(Xs?, T?, R1),
    args_app(As?, R1?, R).

procedure rolespecs_args(RoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
rolespecs_args([], T, T?).
rolespecs_args([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    rs_add(RS?, P),
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    rs_keep(RS?, K),
    rs_forb(RS?, N),
    rolespecs_args(Rs?, T?, R1),
    atoms_args(N?, R1?, R2),
    atoms_args(K?, R2?, R3),
    atoms_args(M?, R3?, R4),
    atoms_args(P?, R4?, R).

% The arguments of a conjunct's anchor, of its phi and of its literals, and
% of the safe formulas of a body, their holders among them, a constraint
% giving those constraint_args gives.
procedure conjs_args(Conjuncts?, Args?, Args).
conjs_args([], T, T?).
conjs_args([conjunct(Xs, _, atom(_, As), Phi, _, _, L)|Cs], T, R?) :-
    ground(Xs?), ground(As?), ground(Phi?), ground(L?), ground(T?), ground(Cs?) |
    conjs_args(Cs?, T?, R1),
    forms_args([Phi?|L?], R1?, R2),
    args_app(As?, R2?, R).

procedure forms_args(Forms?, Args?, Args).
forms_args([], T, T?).
forms_args([F|Fs], T, R?) :- ground(F?), ground(Fs?), ground(T?) |
    forms_args(Fs?, T?, R1),
    form_args(F?, R1?, R).

procedure form_args(Form?, Args?, Args).
form_args(fa(H, M), T, [H?|R?]) :- ground(M?), ground(T?) |
    plain_mult(M?, A),
    atoms_args([A?], T?, R).
form_args(fnot(F), T, R?) :- form_args(F?, T?, R).
form_args(fand(A, B), T, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(B?), ground(T?) | forms_args([A?, B?], T?, R).
form_args(for(A, B), T, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(B?), ground(T?) | forms_args([A?, B?], T?, R).
form_args(fexists(_, H, atom(_, As), F), T, [H?|R?]) :- ground(As?), ground(F?), ground(T?) |
    form_args(F?, T?, R1),
    args_app(As?, R1?, R).
form_args(fforall(_, H, atom(_, As), F, G), T, [H?|R?]) :- ground(As?), ground(F?), ground(G?), ground(T?) |
    forms_args([F?|G?], T?, R1),
    args_app(As?, R1?, R).
form_args(fcons(C), T, R?) :- constraint_args(C?, T?, R).

% The anchored safe formulas of a constraint or a formula.  A cardinality and
% a sum bind "as the anchored quantifiers of Definition Role do" (def:numbers),
% so each is read here as the quantifier fexists(Xs, H, A, Phi), a sum's
% numeric term u beside its phi as the constraint rel(numeric, [U]), and the
% checks of a quantifier then ask of them what they ask of a quantifier
% (num_schema1, nsch_occ_vars).  No condition reads them: schema_args does not.
procedure cons_anchored(Constraint?, Forms?, Forms).
cons_anchored(and(X, Y), T, R?) :- cons_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), cons_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(or(X, Y), T, R?) :- cons_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), cons_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(implies(X, Y), T, R?) :- cons_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), cons_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(not(X), T, R?) :- cons_anchored(X?, T?, R).
cons_anchored(eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(ne(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(le(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(lt(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(ge(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(gt(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
cons_anchored(rel(_, Xs), T, R?) :- exprs_anchored(Xs?, T?, R).
cons_anchored(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure expr_anchored(Expr?, Forms?, Forms).
expr_anchored(plus(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
expr_anchored(minus(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
expr_anchored(mul(X, Y), T, R?) :- expr_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
expr_anchored(fn(_, Xs), T, R?) :- exprs_anchored(Xs?, T?, R).
expr_anchored(cardinality(Xs, H, A, F), T, [fexists(Xs?, H?, A?, F?)|R?]) :-
    ground(F?) |
    form_anchored(F?, T?, R).
expr_anchored(sum(Xs, H, A, F, U), T, [fexists(Xs?, H?, A?, fand(F?, fcons(rel(numeric, [U?]))))|R?]) :-
    ground(F?), ground(U?) |
    expr_anchored(U?, T?, R1),
    form_anchored(F?, R1?, R).
expr_anchored(_, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure exprs_anchored(Exprs?, Forms?, Forms).
exprs_anchored([], T, T?).
exprs_anchored([X|Xs], T, R?) :- exprs_anchored(Xs?, T?, R1), expr_anchored(X?, R1?, R).

procedure form_anchored(Form?, Forms?, Forms).
form_anchored(fa(_, _), T, T?).
form_anchored(fnot(F), T, R?) :- form_anchored(F?, T?, R).
form_anchored(fand(X, Y), T, R?) :- form_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), form_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
form_anchored(for(X, Y), T, R?) :- form_anchored(Y?, T?, R1), form_anchored(X?, R1?, R).
form_anchored(fexists(_, _, _, F), T, R?) :- form_anchored(F?, T?, R).
form_anchored(fforall(_, _, _, F, G), T, R?) :- forms_anchored(G?, T?, R1), form_anchored(F?, R1?, R).
form_anchored(fcons(C), T, R?) :- cons_anchored(C?, T?, R).

procedure forms_anchored(Forms?, Forms?, Forms).
forms_anchored([], T, T?).
forms_anchored([F|Fs], T, R?) :- forms_anchored(Fs?, T?, R1), form_anchored(F?, R1?, R).

% The safe formulas of a schema: Fs, and each conjunct's phi and literals.
procedure conj_forms(Conjuncts?, Forms?, Forms).
conj_forms([], T, T?).
conj_forms([conjunct(_, _, _, Phi, _, _, L)|Cs], T, [Phi?|R?]) :- ground(L?), ground(Cs?), ground(T?) |
    conj_forms(Cs?, T?, R1),
    forms_app(L?, R1?, R).

procedure forms_app(Forms?, Forms?, Forms).
forms_app([], T, T?).
forms_app([F|Fs], T, [F?|R?]) :- forms_app(Fs?, T?, R).

% Those of a schema: of its constraint, its conjuncts and its formulas.
procedure nsch_anchored(NSchema?, Forms).
nsch_anchored(S, R?) :- ground(S?) |
    nsch_constraint(S?, Cn),
    nsch_conjs(S?, Cj),
    nsch_forms(S?, Fs),
    conj_forms(Cj?, Fs?, All),
    forms_anchored(All?, [], R1),
    cons_anchored(Cn?, R1?, R).

procedure schema_args(Schema?, Args).
schema_args(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    sch_conjs(Sc?, Cj),
    sch_forms(Sc?, Fs),
    rolespecs_args(Rs?, [], R1),
    conjs_args(Cj?, R1?, R2),
    forms_args(Fs?, R2?, R).

% The party and speech-act variables a name term carries (def:role).
procedure nt_pvars(NameTerm?, Args).
nt_pvars(own(_), []).
nt_pvars(own_var(X), [pvar(X?)]).
nt_pvars(ext(S, _), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_pvars(S?, R).
nt_pvars(ext_any(S), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_pvars(S?, R).

procedure nt_svars(NameTerm?, Args).
nt_svars(own(_), []).
nt_svars(own_var(_), []).
nt_svars(ext(S, Y), R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Y?) |
    nt_svars(S?, R1),
    args_app(R1?, [svar(Y?)], R).
% The wildcard in place of the speech-act variable of Sigma.* is no variable.
nt_svars(ext_any(S), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_svars(S?, R).

% A signed term sgn(y, pi) carries the speech-act variable y and no party
% variable (def:schema).
procedure filter_pvars(Args?, Args).
filter_pvars([], []).
filter_pvars([pvar(X)|As], [pvar(X?)|R?]) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([role(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([svar(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([sgn(_, _)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([num(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([real(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([any|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([item_of(_)|As], R?) :- filter_pvars(As?, R).
filter_pvars([nterm(S)|As], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(As?) |
    nt_pvars(S?, Ps),
    filter_pvars(As?, R1),
    args_app(Ps?, R1?, R).

procedure filter_svars(Args?, Args).
filter_svars([], []).
filter_svars([svar(X)|As], [svar(X?)|R?]) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([role(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([pvar(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([sgn(Y, _)|As], [svar(Y?)|R?]) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([num(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([real(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([any|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
% An item names no agent and has no base (Arg), so the speech-act variable
% inside it is not read as one the atom carries.
filter_svars([item_of(_)|As], R?) :- filter_svars(As?, R).
filter_svars([nterm(S)|As], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(As?) |
    nt_svars(S?, Ss),
    filter_svars(As?, R1),
    args_app(Ss?, R1?, R).

% The value variables among arguments: num(X) with X a name, a number being
% no variable (GSC, Section 3.2).
procedure filter_nvars(Args?, Args).
filter_nvars([], []).
filter_nvars([num(X)|As], R?) :- number(X?), ground(As?) | filter_nvars(As?, R).
filter_nvars([num(X)|As], [num(X?)|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(X?), ground(As?) |
    filter_nvars(As?, R).
filter_nvars([A|As], R?) :- otherwise, ground(A?), ground(As?) | filter_nvars(As?, R).

procedure schema_pvars(Schema?, Args).
schema_pvars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    filter_pvars(As?, Ps),
    args_dedup(Ps?, R).

procedure schema_svars(Schema?, Args).
schema_svars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    filter_svars(As?, Ss),
    args_dedup(Ss?, R).

% role_args(I, K, R): role(I) .. role(K).
procedure role_args(Integer?, Integer?, Args).
role_args(I, K, []) :- I? > K? | true.
role_args(I, K, [role(I?)|R?]) :- I? =< K?, integer(I?), integer(K?) |
    I1 := I? + 1,
    role_args(I1?, K?, R).

% Every variable of a schema: its roles, then its party and speech-act
% variables in order of first occurrence.
procedure schema_vars(Schema?, Args).
schema_vars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    roles_len(Rs?, K),
    role_args(1, K?, RA),
    schema_pvars(Sc?, PV),
    schema_svars(Sc?, SV),
    args_app(SV?, [], SV1),
    args_app(PV?, SV1?, PS),
    args_app(RA?, PS?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Completing a partial substitution with fresh names
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A match constrains only the variables it meets.  The rest take names no
% other binding in play uses: clause 2 of def:unobstructed excuses a binding
% that sends a role to the other party, and a variable the match left free can
% be sent elsewhere, so the fresh completion is the binding that decides it.

procedure fresh_val(Arg?, Integer?, Val).
fresh_val(role(_), N, person(N?)).
fresh_val(pvar(_), N, person(N?)).
fresh_val(svar(_), N, speech(N?)).
fresh_val(nterm(_), _, undef).
fresh_val(sgn(_, _), _, undef).
fresh_val(num(X), _, nfree(X?)).
fresh_val(real(X), _, nfree(X?)).
fresh_val(any, _, undef).
fresh_val(item_of(_), _, undef).

procedure complete1(Found?, Arg?, Args?, Subst?, Integer?, Subst).
complete1(bound(_), _, As, S, N, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    complete_vars(As?, S?, N?, R).
complete1(free, A, As, S, N, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    fresh_val(A?, N?, V),
    N1 := N? + 1,
    complete_vars(As?, [bind(A?, V?)|S?], N1?, R).

procedure complete_vars(Args?, Subst?, Integer?, Subst).
complete_vars([], S, _, S?).
complete_vars([A|As], S, N, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    subst_lookup(S?, A?, F),
    complete1(F?, A?, As?, S?, N?, R).

procedure complete(Schema?, Subst?, Integer?, Subst).
complete(Sc, S, N, R?) :- ground(Sc?), ground(S?), integer(N?) |
    schema_vars(Sc?, Vs),
    complete_vars(Vs?, S?, N?, R).

% The first name index no binding of the introductory act uses: person(0) and
% person(1) are its two people and speech(0)..speech(m-1) its speech acts.
procedure fresh_base(Schema?, Integer).
fresh_base(Sc, N?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_svars(Sc?, SV),
    args_len(SV?, M),
    N := M? + 2.

procedure args_len(Args?, Integer).
args_len([], 0).
args_len([_|As], N?) :- args_len(As?, M), N := M? + 1.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Atoms a role requires (def:schema: the atoms =(i) and -(i))
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% atoms_witness(Phis, U, E, R): some atom of Phis has its predicate in E and U
% among its arguments.
procedure atoms_witness1(Ans?, Atoms?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
atoms_witness1(yes, _, _, _, yes).
atoms_witness1(no, Xs, U, E, R?) :- ground(Xs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    atoms_witness(Xs?, U?, E?, R).

procedure atoms_witness(Atoms?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
atoms_witness([], _, _, no).
atoms_witness([atom(Q, As)|Xs], U, E, R?) :-
    ground(Q?), ground(As?), ground(Xs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    pred_member(Q?, E?, A1),
    args_member(As?, U?, A2),
    both_yes(A1?, A2?, B),
    atoms_witness1(B?, Xs?, U?, E?, R).

% req_names(Role, U, E, R): the role requires an atom with predicate in E and
% U among its arguments.
procedure req_names(RoleSpec?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
req_names(RS, U, E, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    rs_del(RS?, M),
    rs_keep(RS?, K),
    atoms_witness(M?, U?, E?, A1),
    atoms_witness(K?, U?, E?, A2),
    or_yes(A1?, A2?, R).

procedure any_req_names1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
any_req_names1(yes, _, _, _, yes).
any_req_names1(no, Rs, U, E, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    any_req_names(Rs?, U?, E?, R).

procedure any_req_names(RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Preds?, Ans).
any_req_names([], _, _, no).
any_req_names([RS|Rs], U, E, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(U?), ground(E?) |
    req_names(RS?, U?, E?, A),
    any_req_names1(A?, Rs?, U?, E?, R).

% req_occurs(Role, Y, R): the speech-act variable Y occurs in an atom the role
% requires, whatever its predicate -- as an argument or inside a name-term
% argument (def:grounded: "occurs in no atom required
% at a role").
procedure req_occurs(RoleSpec?, Arg?, Ans).
req_occurs(RS, Y, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Y?) |
    rs_req(RS?, Req),
    atoms_args(Req?, [], As),
    filter_svars(As?, SV),
    args_member(SV?, Y?, R).

procedure any_req_occurs1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Ans).
any_req_occurs1(yes, _, _, yes).
any_req_occurs1(no, Rs, Y, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(Y?) |
    any_req_occurs(Rs?, Y?, R).

procedure any_req_occurs(RoleSpecs?, Arg?, Ans).
any_req_occurs([], _, no).
any_req_occurs([RS|Rs], Y, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(Y?) |
    req_occurs(RS?, Y?, A),
    any_req_occurs1(A?, Rs?, Y?, R).

% nth_rs(Rs, I, R): the I-th role of a schema, counting from one.  The empty
% case is out of range and cannot arise; it answers with a role that requires
% nothing, so that a caller reports a fault rather than passing.
procedure nth_rs(RoleSpecs?, Integer?, RoleSpec).
nth_rs([], _, rs(unguarded, [], [], [], [])).
nth_rs([X|_], I, X?) :- I? =:= 1 | true.
nth_rs([_|Xs], I, R?) :- I? > 1, integer(I?), ground(Xs?) |
    I1 := I? - 1,
    nth_rs(Xs?, I1?, R).

procedure guard_marked(Guard?, Ans).
guard_marked(guarded, yes).
guard_marked(unguarded, no).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Reflexive predicates (GAI's appendix "Contracts with Wards")
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% The predicates a contract declares reflexive, and its schemas.
procedure decl_reflexive(Declared?, Preds).
decl_reflexive([], []).
decl_reflexive([_|_], []).
decl_reflexive(reflexive(Rf, _), Rf?).

procedure decl_schemas(Declared?, Contract).
decl_schemas([], []).
decl_schemas([S|Ss], [S?|Ss?]).
decl_schemas(reflexive(_, C), C?).

% own_reflexive(Phi, I, Rf, R): Phi is the atom of a reflexive predicate, one
% of Rf, naming the role I.
procedure own_reflexive(Atom?, Integer?, Preds?, Ans).
own_reflexive(atom(P, [role(J)]), I, Rf, R?) :-
    J? =:= I?, ground(P?), ground(Rf?) |
    pred_member(P?, Rf?, R).
own_reflexive(atom(_, _), _, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% refl_keep(Phis, I, Rf, W, R): the atoms of Phis for which own_reflexive
% answers W, in order: W = yes keeps the atoms of a reflexive predicate naming
% the role I, and W = no the others.
procedure refl_keep1(Ans?, Ans?, Atom?, Atoms?, Integer?, Preds?, Atoms).
refl_keep1(B, W, A, Xs, I, Rf, [A?|R?]) :-
    B? =?= W?, ground(Xs?), integer(I?), ground(Rf?) |
    refl_keep(Xs?, I?, Rf?, W?, R).
refl_keep1(_, W, _, Xs, I, Rf, R?) :-
    otherwise, ground(W?), ground(Xs?), integer(I?), ground(Rf?) |
    refl_keep(Xs?, I?, Rf?, W?, R).

procedure refl_keep(Atoms?, Integer?, Preds?, Ans?, Atoms).
refl_keep([], _, _, _, []).
refl_keep([A|Xs], I, Rf, W, R?) :-
    ground(A?), ground(Xs?), integer(I?), ground(Rf?), ground(W?) |
    own_reflexive(A?, I?, Rf?, B),
    refl_keep1(B?, W?, A?, Xs?, I?, Rf?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Roles, bases and name terms (def:role)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A schema is written schema(Name, Vars, Roles), or cschema(Name, Vars, [],
% Roles); a role is written rs(...) where it is an agent role and
% crs(Kind, ...) where it is a listed role.  The accessors below read
% either.

procedure sch_name(Schema?, Constant).
sch_name(schema(Nm, _, _), Nm?).
sch_name(cschema(Nm, _, _, _), Nm?).
sch_name(qschema(Nm, _, _, _, _, _, _), Nm?).

% The conjuncts of a schema its listed roles do not hold whole.
procedure sch_conjs(Schema?, Conjuncts).
sch_conjs(schema(_, _, _), []).
sch_conjs(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
sch_conjs(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, Cj, _), Cj?).

procedure nsch_conjs(NSchema?, Conjuncts).
nsch_conjs(schema(_, _, _), []).
nsch_conjs(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
nsch_conjs(nschema(_, _, _, _), []).
nsch_conjs(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, Cj, _), Cj?).

procedure sch_forms(Schema?, Forms).
sch_forms(schema(_, _, _), []).
sch_forms(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
sch_forms(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, _, Fs), Fs?).

procedure nsch_forms(NSchema?, Forms).
nsch_forms(schema(_, _, _), []).
nsch_forms(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
nsch_forms(nschema(_, _, _, _), []).
nsch_forms(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, _, Fs), Fs?).

% The names a schema's quantifiers bind, each as a variable of each kind.
procedure nsch_bound(NSchema?, Args).
nsch_bound(schema(_, _, _), []).
nsch_bound(cschema(_, _, _, _), []).
nsch_bound(nschema(_, _, _, _), []).
nsch_bound(qschema(_, _, Bd, _, _, _, _), Bd?).

% A schema has literals for its body and head, no conjunct and no formula, a
% listed role's being crs (def:introduction, def:unobstructed).
procedure nsch_literal(NSchema?, Ans).
nsch_literal(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, _, _), no).
nsch_literal(_, yes) :- otherwise | true.

% The variables of a schema, in the order of its head.
procedure sch_vars(Schema?, Args).
sch_vars(schema(_, Vs, _), Vs?).
sch_vars(cschema(_, Vs, _, _), Vs?).
sch_vars(qschema(_, Vs, _, _, _, _, _), Vs?).

procedure sch_roles(Schema?, RoleSpecs).
sch_roles(schema(_, _, Rs), Rs?).
sch_roles(cschema(_, _, _, Rs), Rs?).
sch_roles(qschema(_, _, _, _, Rs, _, _), Rs?).

procedure rs_guard(RoleSpec?, Guard).
rs_guard(rs(G, _, _, _, _), G?).
rs_guard(crs(_, G, _, _, _, _), G?).

procedure rs_add(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_add(rs(_, P, _, _, _), P?).
rs_add(crs(_, _, P, _, _, _), P?).

% A role's atoms marked -, as the term form writes them: -(i), those with no
% wildcard, and *(i), its cleared atoms, those with one (def:schema, GSC
% 327e035).
procedure rs_marked_del(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_marked_del(rs(_, _, M, _, _), M?).
rs_marked_del(crs(_, _, _, M, _, _), M?).

% -(i): the atoms the role deletes, marked - with no wildcard.
procedure rs_del(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_del(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    atoms_cleared(M?, no, R).

% *(i): the role's cleared atoms, marked - with a wildcard.
procedure rs_clear(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_clear(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    atoms_cleared(M?, yes, R).

% Whether an atom carries the wildcard: among its arguments, or in place of
% the speech-act variable of a name term among them (def:schema).
procedure nt_wild(NameTerm?, Ans).
nt_wild(own(_), no).
nt_wild(own_var(_), no).
nt_wild(ext(S, _), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_wild(S?, R).
nt_wild(ext_any(_), yes).

procedure arg_wild(Arg?, Ans).
arg_wild(any, yes).
arg_wild(nterm(S), R?) :- ground(S?) | nt_wild(S?, R).
arg_wild(A, no) :- otherwise, ground(A?) | true.

procedure args_wild1(Ans?, Args?, Ans).
args_wild1(yes, _, yes).
args_wild1(no, As, R?) :- ground(As?) | args_wild(As?, R).

procedure args_wild(Args?, Ans).
args_wild([], no).
args_wild([A|As], R?) :- ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    arg_wild(A?, W),
    args_wild1(W?, As?, R).

procedure atom_wild(Atom?, Ans).
atom_wild(atom(_, As), R?) :- ground(As?) | args_wild(As?, R).

% atoms_cleared(Phis, W, R): the atoms of Phis carrying the wildcard (W = yes)
% or not carrying it (W = no), in order.
procedure atoms_cleared1(Ans?, Ans?, Atom?, Atoms?, Atoms).
atoms_cleared1(B, W, A, Xs, [A?|R?]) :- B? =?= W?, ground(Xs?) |
    atoms_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).
atoms_cleared1(_, W, _, Xs, R?) :- otherwise, ground(W?), ground(Xs?) |
    atoms_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).

procedure atoms_cleared(Atoms?, Ans?, Atoms).
atoms_cleared([], _, []).
atoms_cleared([A|Xs], W, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Xs?), ground(W?) |
    atom_wild(A?, B),
    atoms_cleared1(B?, W?, A?, Xs?, R).

% matches_cleared(Phi, Psi, R): the atom Phi is obtained from the cleared atom
% Psi by replacing its wildcards, each by an argument, a speech-act variable
% where the wildcard is in a name term (def:schema, def:binding).
procedure nt_wild_match(NameTerm?, NameTerm?, Ans).
nt_wild_match(ext_any(S), ext(T, _), R?) :- ground(S?), ground(T?) |
    nt_wild_match(S?, T?, R).
nt_wild_match(ext(S, Y), ext(T, Z), R?) :- Y? =?= Z?, ground(S?), ground(T?) |
    nt_wild_match(S?, T?, R).
nt_wild_match(S, T, yes) :- otherwise, S? =?= T? | true.
nt_wild_match(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure arg_wild_match(Arg?, Arg?, Ans).
arg_wild_match(any, _, yes).
arg_wild_match(nterm(S), nterm(T), R?) :- ground(S?), ground(T?) |
    nt_wild_match(S?, T?, R).
arg_wild_match(A, B, yes) :- otherwise, A? =?= B? | true.
arg_wild_match(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure args_wild_match1(Ans?, Args?, Args?, Ans).
args_wild_match1(no, _, _, no).
args_wild_match1(yes, Ps, As, R?) :- ground(Ps?), ground(As?) |
    args_wild_match(Ps?, As?, R).

procedure args_wild_match(Args?, Args?, Ans).
args_wild_match([], [], yes).
args_wild_match([P|Ps], [A|As], R?) :- ground(P?), ground(Ps?), ground(A?), ground(As?) |
    arg_wild_match(P?, A?, M),
    args_wild_match1(M?, Ps?, As?, R).
args_wild_match(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure matches_cleared(Atom?, Atom?, Ans).
matches_cleared(atom(P, As), atom(Q, Bs), R?) :-
    P? =?= Q?, ground(As?), ground(Bs?) |
    args_wild_match(Bs?, As?, R).
matches_cleared(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% matches_some_cleared(Phi, Psis, R): Phi is obtained from some atom of Psis.
procedure matches_some1(Ans?, Atom?, Atoms?, Ans).
matches_some1(yes, _, _, yes).
matches_some1(no, A, Cs, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Cs?) | matches_some_cleared(A?, Cs?, R).

procedure matches_some_cleared(Atom?, Atoms?, Ans).
matches_some_cleared(_, [], no).
matches_some_cleared(A, [C|Cs], R?) :- ground(A?), ground(C?), ground(Cs?) |
    matches_cleared(A?, C?, M),
    matches_some1(M?, A?, Cs?, R).

procedure rs_keep(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_keep(rs(_, _, _, K, _), K?).
rs_keep(crs(_, _, _, _, K, _), K?).

procedure rs_forb(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_forb(rs(_, _, _, _, N), N?).
rs_forb(crs(_, _, _, _, _, N), N?).

% The atoms a role requires: =(i) u -(i) (def:schema), a cleared atom
% requiring none.
procedure rs_req(RoleSpec?, Atoms).
rs_req(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_del(RS?, M),
    rs_keep(RS?, K),
    atoms_app(K?, M?, R).

procedure is_party_role(RoleSpec?, Ans).
is_party_role(rs(_, _, _, _, _), yes).
is_party_role(crs(_, _, _, _, _, _), no).

procedure is_guarding(RoleSpec?, Ans).
is_guarding(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    rs_guard(RS?, G),
    guard_marked(G?, R).

% A reading role (def:schema, GSC 0380a8a): a role that is not a guarding
% role and has +(i) u -(i) empty, -(i) the atoms marked - with no wildcard,
% so a cleared atom is no change.
procedure reading_role(RoleSpec?, Ans).
reading_role(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    is_guarding(RS?, G),
    rs_add(RS?, P),
    rs_del(RS?, M),
    reading_role1(G?, P?, M?, R).

procedure reading_role1(Ans?, Atoms?, Atoms?, Ans).
reading_role1(no, [], [], yes).
reading_role1(_, _, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

% Some role among the indices Js is no reading role.  Clause 2 of
% def:unobstructed asks it of the roles a binding sends the other agent to.
procedure some_not_reading(Ints?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
some_not_reading([], _, no).
some_not_reading([J|Js], Rs, R?) :- integer(J?), ground(Js?), ground(Rs?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, J?, RS),
    reading_role(RS?, A),
    some_not_reading1(A?, Js?, Rs?, R).

procedure some_not_reading1(Ans?, Ints?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
some_not_reading1(no, _, _, yes).
some_not_reading1(yes, Js, Rs, R?) :- ground(Js?), ground(Rs?) |
    some_not_reading(Js?, Rs?, R).

procedure nt_base(NameTerm?, Base).
nt_base(own(I), b_role(I?)).
nt_base(own_var(X), b_pvar(X?)).
nt_base(ext(S, _), B?) :- ground(S?) | nt_base(S?, B).
% <pi>.* in a cleared atom is a name term with its speech-act variable
% replaced by the wildcard (def:schema), its base that of <pi>.
nt_base(ext_any(S), B?) :- ground(S?) | nt_base(S?, B).

procedure arg_base(Arg?, Base).
arg_base(role(I), b_role(I?)).
arg_base(pvar(X), b_pvar(X?)).
arg_base(svar(X), b_svar(X?)).
arg_base(nterm(S), B?) :- ground(S?) | nt_base(S?, B).
% A signed term sgn(y, pi) counts as the two arguments y and pi
% (def:grounded): this is the base of pi, an agent role, and
% filter_svars gives y.
arg_base(sgn(_, J), b_role(J?)).
arg_base(num(_), b_num).
arg_base(real(_), b_num).
arg_base(any, b_any).
% An item, an utterance, has no base, as a value has none (Arg).
arg_base(item_of(_), b_num).

procedure role_base(RoleSpec?, Integer?, Base).
role_base(rs(_, _, _, _, _), I, b_role(I?)).
% The base of a listed role pi[rho(*, u_2, ..., u_r)] is the agent role pi
% (def:role, GSC 8064cfb).
role_base(crs(listed(I, _, _), _, _, _, _, _), _, b_role(I?)).
role_base(crs(qlisted(I, _, _, _), _, _, _, _, _), _, b_role(I?)).

procedure nth_base(RoleSpecs?, Integer?, Base).
nth_base(Rs, I, B?) :- ground(Rs?), integer(I?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, I?, RS),
    role_base(RS?, I?, B).

% The bases of arguments (def:grounded at GSC 1934846): an agent role, an
% agent variable and a name term have one; a value and a speech-act variable
% have none, a value naming no agent (the appendix "Values in Speech-Act Schemas").
procedure args_bases(Args?, Bases?, Bases).
args_bases([], T, T?).
args_bases([num(_)|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([svar(_)|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([any|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([item_of(_)|As], T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).
args_bases([A|As], T, [B?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    arg_base(A?, B),
    args_bases(As?, T?, R).

% The bases of the arguments of the atoms of Phi_E among a list of atoms
% (def:grounded, def:volition).
procedure phi_bases1(Ans?, Args?, Bases?, Bases).
phi_bases1(no, _, T, T?).
phi_bases1(yes, As, T, R?) :- ground(As?), ground(T?) | args_bases(As?, T?, R).

procedure phi_bases(Atoms?, Preds?, Bases?, Bases).
phi_bases([], _, T, T?).
phi_bases([atom(Q, As)|Xs], E, T, R?) :-
    ground(Q?), ground(As?), ground(Xs?), ground(E?), ground(T?) |
    pred_member(Q?, E?, M),
    phi_bases(Xs?, E?, T?, R1),
    phi_bases1(M?, As?, R1?, R).

% The arguments of a listed role's condition, but its holder, and for one
% written listed/3 its own place (def:role); an agent role has none.
procedure rs_kind_args(RoleSpec?, Args).
rs_kind_args(rs(_, _, _, _, _), []).
rs_kind_args(crs(listed(_, _, As), _, _, _, _, _), As?).
rs_kind_args(crs(qlisted(_, _, As, _), _, _, _, _, _), As?).

procedure rolespecs_kind_args(RoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
rolespecs_kind_args([], T, T?).
rolespecs_kind_args([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    rs_kind_args(RS?, As),
    rolespecs_kind_args(Rs?, T?, R1),
    args_app(As?, R1?, R).


% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The name terms of a schema (def:role)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Those among the arguments of its listed roles, and those among the
% arguments of its atoms, in that order.

procedure nts_of_args(Args?, NameTerms?, NameTerms).
nts_of_args([], T, T?).
nts_of_args([nterm(S)|As], T, [S?|R?]) :- ground(S?), ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    nts_of_args(As?, T?, R).
nts_of_args([A|As], T, R?) :- otherwise, ground(A?), ground(As?), ground(T?) |
    nts_of_args(As?, T?, R).

procedure nts_of_roles(RoleSpecs?, NameTerms?, NameTerms).
nts_of_roles([], T, T?).
nts_of_roles([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    rs_kind_args(RS?, KA),
    nts_of_roles(Rs?, T?, R1),
    nts_of_args(KA?, R1?, R).

procedure sch_nts(Schema?, NameTerms).
sch_nts(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    nts_of_roles(Rs?, [], N1),
    nts_of_args(As?, N1?, R).

% The agent and speech-act variables occurring in a schema: in its atoms,
% within their name terms and signed terms, and in the arguments of its
% listed roles.
procedure sch_occ_vars1(Args?, Args).
sch_occ_vars1(All, R?) :- ground(All?) |
    filter_pvars(All?, Ps),
    filter_svars(All?, Ss),
    args_app(Ps?, Ss?, PS),
    args_dedup(PS?, R).

procedure sch_occ_vars(Schema?, Args).
sch_occ_vars(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    sch_occ_vars2(Rs?, As?, R).

procedure sch_occ_vars2(RoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
sch_occ_vars2(Rs, As, R?) :- ground(Rs?), ground(As?) |
    rolespecs_kind_args(Rs?, [], KAs),
    args_app(As?, KAs?, All),
    sch_occ_vars1(All?, R).

procedure nts_empty(NameTerms?, Ans).
nts_empty([], yes).
nts_empty([_|_], no).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The contract as written, with numbers (GSC, def:numbers)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A contract is read as written, of the types N..., and its plain form is
% the one traceable provenance and volition are decided on: each
% multiplicity dropped, leaving its atom, and the constraint of an nschema
% dropped, leaving a schema with the same name, variables and roles.  A
% number names no agent, so those conditions do not concern numbers (GSC,
% Section 3.2): a value argument stays in its atom, where it names no one.
% def:unobstructed asks that an atom be added at a binding of a schema, and
% is decided on the contract as written, its constraint unread
% (unobstructed.glp), the number of a value argument matched by equality
% (apply_arg, match_num).  The form of a schema is decided on the plain form
% too, an atom with a multiplicity being an atom added or deleted
% (def:schema), and the head and the numbers on the contract as written
% (check.glp).

procedure plain_mult(Mult?, Atom).
plain_mult(atom(P, As), atom(P?, As?)).
plain_mult(times(_, A), A?).
plain_mult(rest(_, _, A), A?).

% rest(K, J, A) is dropped: the plain form's Del keeps the copies deleted,
% and the copies beyond them are a multiplicity, which the plain form drops.
procedure plain_mults(Mults?, Atoms).
plain_mults([], []).
plain_mults([rest(_, _, _)|Ms], R?) :- plain_mults(Ms?, R).
plain_mults([M|Ms], [A?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(M?), ground(Ms?) |
    plain_mult(M?, A),
    plain_mults(Ms?, R).

procedure plain_role(NRoleSpec?, RoleSpec).
plain_role(rs(G, P, M, K, N), rs(G?, P1?, M1?, K1?, N1?)) :-
    ground(P?), ground(M?), ground(K?), ground(N?) |
    plain_mults(P?, P1),
    plain_mults(M?, M1),
    plain_mults(K?, K1),
    plain_mults(N?, N1).
plain_role(crs(Kd, G, P, M, K, N), crs(Kd?, G?, P1?, M1?, K1?, N1?)) :-
    ground(P?), ground(M?), ground(K?), ground(N?) |
    plain_mults(P?, P1),
    plain_mults(M?, M1),
    plain_mults(K?, K1),
    plain_mults(N?, N1).

procedure plain_roles(NRoleSpecs?, RoleSpecs).
plain_roles([], []).
plain_roles([RS|Rs], [R1?|R?]) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?) |
    plain_role(RS?, R1),
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).

procedure plain_schema(NSchema?, Schema).
plain_schema(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, R?)) :- ground(Rs?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).
plain_schema(cschema(Nm, Vs, Nl, Rs), cschema(Nm?, Vs?, Nl?, R?)) :- ground(Rs?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).
plain_schema(nschema(Nm, Vs, _, Rs), schema(Nm?, Vs?, R?)) :- ground(Rs?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R).
plain_schema(qschema(Nm, Vs, Bd, _, Rs, Cj, Fs), qschema(Nm?, Vs?, Bd?, true, R?, C?, Fs?)) :- ground(Rs?), ground(Cj?) |
    plain_roles(Rs?, R),
    plain_conjs(Cj?, C).

procedure plain_conjs(Conjuncts?, Conjuncts).
plain_conjs([], []).
plain_conjs([conjunct(Xs, I, A, Phi, P, M, L)|Cs], [conjunct(Xs?, I?, A?, Phi?, P1?, M1?, L?)|R?]) :-
    ground(P?), ground(M?) |
    plain_hms(P?, P1),
    plain_hms(M?, M1),
    plain_conjs(Cs?, R).

procedure plain_hms(HMults?, HMults).
plain_hms([], []).
plain_hms([hm(J, M)|Ms], [hm(J?, A?)|R?]) :- ground(M?) |
    plain_mult(M?, A),
    plain_hms(Ms?, R).

procedure plain_contract(NContract?, Contract).
plain_contract([], []).
plain_contract([S|Ss], [P?|R?]) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    plain_schema(S?, P),
    plain_contract(Ss?, R).

procedure plain_decl(NDeclared?, Declared).
plain_decl([], []).
plain_decl([S|Ss], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | plain_contract([S?|Ss?], R).
plain_decl(reflexive(Rf, C), reflexive(Rf?, R?)) :- ground(C?) | plain_contract(C?, R).

% The schemas of a contract as written, and the predicates it declares
% reflexive.
procedure ndecl_schemas(NDeclared?, NContract).
ndecl_schemas([], []).
ndecl_schemas([S|Ss], [S?|Ss?]).
ndecl_schemas(reflexive(_, C), C?).

procedure ndecl_reflexive(NDeclared?, Preds).
ndecl_reflexive([], []).
ndecl_reflexive([_|_], []).
ndecl_reflexive(reflexive(Rf, _), Rf?).

% num_ctx(NSc, nc(C, Pw)): the constraint of a schema as written, true where
% it has none, and the value variables it uses as multiplicities.
procedure num_ctx(NSchema?, NumCtx).
num_ctx(NSc, nc(C?, Pw?)) :- ground(NSc?) |
    nsch_constraint(NSc?, C),
    nsch_roles(NSc?, Rs),
    nroles_margs(Rs?, [], Ms),
    filter_nvars(Ms?, Ms1),
    args_dedup(Ms1?, Pw).

% The parts of a schema as written.  The constraint of a schema with none is
% true.
procedure nsch_name(NSchema?, Constant).
nsch_name(schema(Nm, _, _), Nm?).
nsch_name(cschema(Nm, _, _, _), Nm?).
nsch_name(nschema(Nm, _, _, _), Nm?).
nsch_name(qschema(Nm, _, _, _, _, _, _), Nm?).

procedure nsch_vars(NSchema?, Args).
nsch_vars(schema(_, Vs, _), Vs?).
nsch_vars(cschema(_, Vs, _, _), Vs?).
nsch_vars(nschema(_, Vs, _, _), Vs?).
nsch_vars(qschema(_, Vs, _, _, _, _, _), Vs?).

procedure nsch_roles(NSchema?, NRoleSpecs).
nsch_roles(schema(_, _, Rs), Rs?).
nsch_roles(cschema(_, _, _, Rs), Rs?).
nsch_roles(nschema(_, _, _, Rs), Rs?).
nsch_roles(qschema(_, _, _, _, Rs, _, _), Rs?).

procedure nsch_constraint(NSchema?, Constraint).
nsch_constraint(schema(_, _, _), true).
nsch_constraint(cschema(_, _, _, _), true).
nsch_constraint(nschema(_, _, C, _), C?).
nsch_constraint(qschema(_, _, _, C, _, _, _), C?).

% The constraints of a contract's schemas as written, in their order, which
% its plain form drops (plain_schema) and traceable provenance reads
% (def:grounded, GSC 7324ec7).
procedure ncontract_constraints(NContract?, Constraints).
ncontract_constraints([], []).
ncontract_constraints([S|Ss], [C?|R?]) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    nsch_constraint(S?, C),
    ncontract_constraints(Ss?, R).

procedure nrs_guard(NRoleSpec?, Guard).
nrs_guard(rs(G, _, _, _, _), G?).
nrs_guard(crs(_, G, _, _, _, _), G?).

procedure nrs_add(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_add(rs(_, P, _, _, _), P?).
nrs_add(crs(_, _, P, _, _, _), P?).

% A role's atoms marked -, as written: -(i), those with no wildcard, and
% *(i), its cleared atoms (def:schema, GSC 327e035).
procedure nrs_marked_del(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_marked_del(rs(_, _, M, _, _), M?).
nrs_marked_del(crs(_, _, _, M, _, _), M?).

procedure nrs_del(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_del(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    mults_cleared(M?, no, R).

procedure nrs_clear(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_clear(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    mults_cleared(M?, yes, R).

procedure mult_wild(Mult?, Ans).
mult_wild(atom(P, As), R?) :- ground(P?), ground(As?) | atom_wild(atom(P?, As?), R).
mult_wild(times(_, A), R?) :- ground(A?) | atom_wild(A?, R).
mult_wild(rest(_, _, A), R?) :- ground(A?) | atom_wild(A?, R).

procedure mults_cleared1(Ans?, Ans?, Mult?, Mults?, Mults).
mults_cleared1(B, W, A, Xs, [A?|R?]) :- B? =?= W?, ground(Xs?) |
    mults_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).
mults_cleared1(_, W, _, Xs, R?) :- otherwise, ground(W?), ground(Xs?) |
    mults_cleared(Xs?, W?, R).

procedure mults_cleared(Mults?, Ans?, Mults).
mults_cleared([], _, []).
mults_cleared([A|Xs], W, R?) :- ground(A?), ground(Xs?), ground(W?) |
    mult_wild(A?, B),
    mults_cleared1(B?, W?, A?, Xs?, R).

procedure nrs_keep(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_keep(rs(_, _, _, K, _), K?).
nrs_keep(crs(_, _, _, _, K, _), K?).

procedure nrs_forb(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_forb(rs(_, _, _, _, N), N?).
nrs_forb(crs(_, _, _, _, _, N), N?).

procedure mults_app(Mults?, Mults?, Mults).
mults_app([], T, T?).
mults_app([M|Ms], T, [M?|R?]) :- mults_app(Ms?, T?, R).

% The atoms a role requires, as written: =(i) u -(i), each rest(K, J, A) of
% Keep written K.A with the J copies of A it stands beside taken from -(i)
% (rest, above).
procedure nrs_req(NRoleSpec?, Mults).
nrs_req(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_del(RS?, M),
    nrs_keep(RS?, K),
    mults_rest(K?, M?, K1, M1),
    mults_app(K1?, M1?, R).

% Keep and -(i), each rest(K, J, A) of Keep made K.A and the J copies of A
% taken from -(i).
procedure mults_rest(Mults?, Mults?, Mults, Mults).
mults_rest([], D, [], D?).
mults_rest([rest(K, J, A)|Ks], D, R?, D1?) :- ground(K?), ground(J?), ground(A?), ground(D?), ground(Ks?) |
    mults_take_x(J?, D?, A?, D0),
    mults_rest(Ks?, D0?, R1, D1),
    expr_copies(K?, A?, R1?, R).
mults_rest([M|Ks], D, [M?|R?], D1?) :- otherwise, ground(D?) |
    mults_rest(Ks?, D?, R, D1).

% K.A, K a sum of arguments, as an atom with a multiplicity per summand.
procedure expr_copies(Expr?, Atom?, Mults?, Mults).
expr_copies(plus(X, Y), A, T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(A?), ground(T?) |
    expr_copies(Y?, A?, T?, R1),
    expr_copies(X?, A?, R1?, R).
expr_copies(num(1), A, T, [A?|T?]).
expr_copies(num(K), A, T, [times(num(K?), A?)|T?]) :- otherwise | true.
expr_copies(_, _, T, T?) :- otherwise | true.

% Mults less the copies of the atom A that the sum J counts.
procedure mults_take_x(Expr?, Mults?, Atom?, Mults).
mults_take_x(plus(X, Y), D, A, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(D?), ground(A?) |
    mults_take_x(X?, D?, A?, R1),
    mults_take_x(Y?, R1?, A?, R).
mults_take_x(num(0), D, _, D?).
mults_take_x(num(J), D, A, R?) :- otherwise | mults_take_j(D?, num(J?), A?, R).
mults_take_x(_, D, _, D?) :- otherwise | true.

% Mults less J copies of the atom A, written A where J is 1, or J.A.
procedure mults_take_j(Mults?, Arg?, Atom?, Mults).
mults_take_j([], _, _, []).
mults_take_j([M|Ms], J, A, Ms?) :- M? =?= A?, J? =?= num(1) | true.
mults_take_j([times(K, M)|Ms], J, A, Ms?) :- M? =?= A?, K? =?= J? | true.
mults_take_j([times(num(K), M)|Ms], num(J), A, Ms?) :- M? =?= A?, number(K?), number(J?), K? =:= J? | true.
mults_take_j([M|Ms], J, A, [M?|R?]) :- otherwise, ground(J?), ground(A?) | mults_take_j(Ms?, J?, A?, R).

procedure n_is_guarding(NRoleSpec?, Ans).
n_is_guarding(RS, R?) :- ground(RS?) |
    nrs_guard(RS?, G),
    guard_marked(G?, R).

% The arguments of a constraint's linear equalities and inequalities, and the
% multiplicities among a multiset as written.  A signing condition is over an
% agent and a speech act, not over values, and gives none, and neither does an
% equality of agent variables, speech-act variables or name terms (name_eq).
procedure constraint_args(Constraint?, Args?, Args).
constraint_args(true, T, T?).
constraint_args(and(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_args(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_args(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_args(eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) |
    name_eq(X?, Y?, A),
    eq_args(A?, X?, Y?, T?, R).
constraint_args(ne(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) |
    name_eq(X?, Y?, A),
    eq_args(A?, X?, Y?, T?, R).
constraint_args(not(C), T, R?) :- constraint_args(C?, T?, R).
constraint_args(implies(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_args(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_args(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_args(rel(_, Xs), T, R?) :- exprs_args(Xs?, T?, R).
constraint_args(le(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(lt(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(ge(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(gt(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
constraint_args(succ(X, Y), T, [X?, Y?|T?]).
constraint_args(or(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_args(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_args(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_args(signed(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_args(unsigned(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_args(program(X), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(T?) |
    utterance(X?, A),
    program_args(A?, X?, T?, R).

% program(X) is a condition on an utterance, the item of a speech act
% (def:numbers: "a decidable condition on that utterance that its type
% provides"), over no value, its speech-act variable asked of by
% signing_faults (check.glp); on anything else its arguments are no value
% arguments, each constraint_not_numeric.
procedure utterance(Expr?, Ans).
utterance(item_of(_), yes).
utterance(X, no) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | true.

procedure program_args(Ans?, Expr?, Args?, Args).
program_args(yes, _, T, T?).
program_args(no, X, T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?], T?, R).

% An equality or an inequality of two agent variables, two speech-act
% variables or two name terms is over no value (def:numbers, GSC 6f0bda1).
% A wildcard stands in an atom (def:schema), so a name term with one is none
% of these.
procedure name_eq(Expr?, Expr?, Ans).
name_eq(X, Y, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?) |
    arg_kind(X?, A),
    arg_kind(Y?, B),
    kind_same(A?, B?, R).

ArgKind ::= k_agent ; k_speech ; k_name ; k_author ; k_item ; k_other.
procedure arg_kind(Expr?, ArgKind).
arg_kind(role(_), k_agent).
arg_kind(pvar(_), k_agent).
arg_kind(svar(_), k_speech).
arg_kind(nterm(S), R?) :- ground(S?) |
    nt_wild(S?, W),
    nterm_kind(W?, R).
arg_kind(author_of(_), k_author).
arg_kind(item_of(_), k_item).
arg_kind(X, k_other) :- otherwise, ground(X?) | true.

procedure nterm_kind(Ans?, ArgKind).
nterm_kind(no, k_name).
nterm_kind(yes, k_other).

procedure kind_same(ArgKind?, ArgKind?, Ans).
kind_same(k_agent, k_agent, yes).
kind_same(k_speech, k_speech, yes).
kind_same(k_name, k_name, yes).
kind_same(k_author, k_agent, yes).
kind_same(k_agent, k_author, yes).
kind_same(k_item, k_item, yes).
kind_same(_, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure eq_args(Ans?, Expr?, Expr?, Args?, Args).
eq_args(yes, _, _, T, T?).
eq_args(no, X, Y, T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).

% The agent and speech-act variables among the arguments of signing
% conditions.
procedure sargs_vars(Args?, Args).
sargs_vars(Ss, R?) :- ground(Ss?) |
    filter_pvars(Ss?, Ps),
    filter_svars(Ss?, Ys),
    args_app(Ps?, Ys?, R).

% The arguments of a constraint's signing conditions, u and y of each
% signed(u, y) and unsigned(u, y) (def:numbers, GSC 10fcc92), and of its
% equalities over no value (name_eq), whose variables the head lists too.
procedure constraint_sargs(Constraint?, Args?, Args).
constraint_sargs(true, T, T?).
constraint_sargs(and(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_sargs(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_sargs(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_sargs(or(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_sargs(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_sargs(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_sargs(eq(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) |
    name_eq(X?, Y?, A),
    eq_sargs(A?, X?, Y?, T?, R).
constraint_sargs(ne(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) |
    name_eq(X?, Y?, A),
    eq_sargs(A?, X?, Y?, T?, R).
constraint_sargs(not(C), T, R?) :- constraint_sargs(C?, T?, R).
constraint_sargs(implies(C1, C2), T, R?) :- ground(C1?), ground(C2?), ground(T?) |
    constraint_sargs(C2?, T?, R1),
    constraint_sargs(C1?, R1?, R).
constraint_sargs(rel(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(le(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(lt(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(ge(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(gt(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(succ(_, _), T, T?).
constraint_sargs(signed(U, Y), T, [U?, Y?|T?]).
constraint_sargs(unsigned(U, Y), T, [U?, Y?|T?]).
constraint_sargs(program(X), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?], T?, R).

procedure eq_sargs(Ans?, Expr?, Expr?, Args?, Args).
eq_sargs(no, _, _, T, T?).
eq_sargs(yes, X, Y, T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).

% The arguments an expression is made of; a cardinality's and a sum's are
% their own (cons_anchored).
procedure expr_args(Expr?, Args?, Args).
expr_args(fn(_, Xs), T, R?) :- exprs_args(Xs?, T?, R).
expr_args(cardinality(_, _, _, _), T, T?).
expr_args(sum(_, _, _, _, _), T, T?).
expr_args(plus(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
expr_args(minus(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
expr_args(mul(X, Y), T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Y?), ground(T?) | exprs_args([X?, Y?], T?, R).
expr_args(num(X), T, [num(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(real(X), T, [num(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(role(I), T, [role(I?)|T?]).
expr_args(pvar(X), T, [pvar(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(svar(X), T, [svar(X?)|T?]).
expr_args(nterm(N), T, [nterm(N?)|T?]).
expr_args(sgn(Y, J), T, [sgn(Y?, J?)|T?]).
expr_args(any, T, [any|T?]).
expr_args(author_of(Y), T, [Y?|T?]).
expr_args(item_of(Y), T, [Y?|T?]).

procedure exprs_args(Exprs?, Args?, Args).
exprs_args([], T, T?).
exprs_args([X|Xs], T, R?) :- ground(X?), ground(Xs?), ground(T?) |
    exprs_args(Xs?, T?, R1),
    expr_args(X?, R1?, R).

procedure mults_margs(Mults?, Args?, Args).
mults_margs([], T, T?).
mults_margs([atom(_, _)|Ms], T, R?) :- ground(Ms?), ground(T?) | mults_margs(Ms?, T?, R).
mults_margs([times(K, _)|Ms], T, [K?|R?]) :- ground(Ms?), ground(T?) | mults_margs(Ms?, T?, R).
mults_margs([rest(K, J, _)|Ms], T, R?) :- ground(K?), ground(J?), ground(Ms?), ground(T?) |
    mults_margs(Ms?, T?, R1),
    exprs_args([K?, J?], R1?, R).

procedure nroles_margs(NRoleSpecs?, Args?, Args).
nroles_margs([], T, T?).
nroles_margs([RS|Rs], T, R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?), ground(T?) |
    nrs_add(RS?, P),
    nrs_marked_del(RS?, M),
    nrs_keep(RS?, K),
    nrs_forb(RS?, N),
    nroles_margs(Rs?, T?, R1),
    mults_margs(N?, R1?, R2),
    mults_margs(K?, R2?, R3),
    mults_margs(M?, R3?, R4),
    mults_margs(P?, R4?, R).

% The variables occurring in a schema as written: its agent and speech-act
% variables (sch_occ_vars of its plain form), then those of its signing
% conditions that its atoms do not carry, then its value variables, in its
% atoms, its multiplicities and its constraint.
procedure nsch_occ_vars(NSchema?, Args).
nsch_occ_vars(NSc, R?) :- ground(NSc?) |
    plain_schema(NSc?, Sc),
    nsch_roles(NSc?, NRs),
    nsch_constraint(NSc?, Cn),
    nsch_anchored(NSc?, An),
    nsch_occ_vars1(Sc?, NRs?, Cn?, An?, R).

procedure nsch_occ_vars1(Schema?, NRoleSpecs?, Constraint?, Forms?, Args).
nsch_occ_vars1(Sc, NRs, Cn, An, R?) :- ground(Sc?), ground(NRs?), ground(Cn?), ground(An?) |
    sch_occ_vars(Sc?, PS0),
    constraint_sargs(Cn?, [], Ss),
    forms_args(An?, Ss?, Ss1),
    sargs_vars(Ss1?, SV),
    args_app(PS0?, SV?, PSV),
    args_dedup(PSV?, PS),
    schema_args(Sc?, As),
    nroles_margs(NRs?, [], Ms),
    forms_args(An?, [], AA),
    constraint_args(Cn?, AA?, Cs),
    args_app(Ms?, Cs?, MC),
    args_app(As?, MC?, All),
    filter_nvars(All?, Ns),
    args_dedup(Ns?, Ns1),
    args_app(PS?, Ns1?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A contract with community roles
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A contract with a listed role, a name term or a schema written cschema has
% community roles.  def:syntactically-grassroots is one definition for every
% contract (GSC ac7ad63), and the distinction is the wards': GAI's appendix
% "Contracts with Wards" is written over the schemas of agent roles with no
% name term, and CSSN's def:sg-wards over those of an agent-named contract
% (check.glp; wards/).

procedure roles_community1(Ans?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
roles_community1(yes, _, yes).
roles_community1(no, Rs, R?) :- ground(Rs?) | roles_community(Rs?, R).

procedure roles_community(RoleSpecs?, Ans).
roles_community([], no).
roles_community([RS|Rs], R?) :- ground(RS?), ground(Rs?) |
    is_party_role(RS?, P),
    flip(P?, A),
    roles_community1(A?, Rs?, R).

procedure sch_community(Schema?, Ans).
sch_community(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), R?) :- ground(Nm?), ground(Vs?), ground(Rs?) |
    roles_community(Rs?, A1),
    sch_nts(schema(Nm?, Vs?, Rs?), Ns),
    nts_empty(Ns?, A2),
    flip(A2?, A3),
    or_yes(A1?, A3?, R).
sch_community(cschema(_, _, _, _), yes).
sch_community(qschema(_, _, _, _, _, _, _), yes).

procedure has_community1(Ans?, Contract?, Ans).
has_community1(yes, _, yes).
has_community1(no, Ss, R?) :- ground(Ss?) | has_community(Ss?, R).

procedure has_community(Contract?, Ans).
has_community([], no).
has_community([S|Ss], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    sch_community(S?, A),
    has_community1(A?, Ss?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The base of a name term (def:role)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A name term of a schema is <pi> for an agent role pi of it, or sigma.y for
% a name term sigma of it (def:role), so its base is an agent role of that
% schema; check.glp refuses a contract with a name term whose base is not
% (name_term_base).  A contract every name term of which is so is
% agent-named in the sense of CSSN's def:agent-named, which def:sg-wards
% asks of a contract with wards and listed roles.

% The base B is an agent role of the schema whose roles are Rs.
procedure base_agent_role1(Integer?, Integer?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
base_agent_role1(I, K, Rs, R?) :- I? >= 1, I? =< K?, ground(Rs?) |
    nth_rs(Rs?, I?, RS),
    is_party_role(RS?, R).
base_agent_role1(_, _, _, no) :- otherwise | true.

procedure base_agent_role(Base?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
base_agent_role(b_role(I), Rs, R?) :- integer(I?), ground(Rs?) |
    roles_len(Rs?, K),
    base_agent_role1(I?, K?, Rs?, R).
base_agent_role(B, _, no) :- otherwise, ground(B?) | true.

procedure nts_agent_based1(Ans?, NameTerms?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
nts_agent_based1(no, _, _, no).
nts_agent_based1(yes, Ns, Rs, R?) :- ground(Ns?), ground(Rs?) | nts_agent_based(Ns?, Rs?, R).

procedure nts_agent_based(NameTerms?, RoleSpecs?, Ans).
nts_agent_based([], _, yes).
nts_agent_based([S|Ns], Rs, R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ns?), ground(Rs?) |
    nt_base(S?, B),
    base_agent_role(B?, Rs?, A),
    nts_agent_based1(A?, Ns?, Rs?, R).

procedure sch_agent_named(Schema?, Ans).
sch_agent_named(Sc, R?) :- ground(Sc?) |
    sch_roles(Sc?, Rs),
    sch_nts(Sc?, Ns),
    nts_agent_based(Ns?, Rs?, R).

procedure agent_named1(Ans?, Contract?, Ans).
agent_named1(no, _, no).
agent_named1(yes, Ss, R?) :- ground(Ss?) | agent_named(Ss?, R).

procedure agent_named(Contract?, Ans).
agent_named([], yes).
agent_named([S|Ss], R?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    sch_agent_named(S?, A),
    agent_named1(A?, Ss?, R).

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Entry points
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% The directory's interface: each entry point is forwarded to the module that
% defines it (manual 19.6).  check.glp composes the three conjuncts of
% def:syntactically-grassroots.  A contract is given as a term, printed by
% contract_named/2 in a REPL session on its owner's file (contracts.glp, the
% header); contracts.glp holds the checker's fixtures, by name, and its
% variants of a contract, by name and the contract's term.

imported procedure check#check_env(NDeclared?, Preds?, Verdict).
exported procedure check(WDeclared?, Verdict).
check(C, V?) :- ground(C?) |
    read_faults(C?, F),
    check_read(F?, C?, V).

% A contract whose reading has faults is malformed, with them; one whose
% reading has none is decided on what it reads to.
procedure check_read(Faults?, WDeclared?, Verdict).
check_read([], C, V?) :- ground(C?) |
    unnamed(C?, D),
    env_preds(C?, Ev),
    check # check_env(D?, Ev?, V).
check_read([F|Fs], _, malformed([F?|Fs?])).

% A contract as the checker reads it, each schema of the clause syntax in
% the checker's form with its roles' names, schema(Name, Names, Vars,
% Roles), cschema(Name, Names, Vars, [], Roles) or nschema(Name, Names,
% Vars, Constraint, Roles), Names the names of its roles in order, a listed
% role named by the variable its quantifier binds (GSC 7324ec7, Section 2: "A
% name in a pragma is the schema's role of that name, the schemas naming
% their roles as the clauses do, a listed role by the variable its quantifier
% binds"); a schema in the checker's form is left as it is.
% A contract in either wrapped form, reflexive(Preds, Contract) or
% environment(Preds, Body), is given in the same wrapper with each schema
% inside as read, descending as unnamed/2 does.  The variants of
% contracts.glp change a contract in the checker's form (contracts.glp, the
% header), and test_gsc.sh makes them on an owner's contract as it reads it.
exported procedure as_read(WDeclared?, WDeclared).
as_read([], []).
as_read([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | as_read_c([S?|Ss?], C).
as_read(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Rf?), ground(Ss?) | as_read_c(Ss?, C).
as_read(environment(Ev, B), environment(Ev?, D?)) :- ground(Ev?), ground(B?) | as_read_b(B?, D).

procedure as_read_b(WBody?, WBody).
as_read_b([], []).
as_read_b([S|Ss], C?) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) | as_read_c([S?|Ss?], C).
as_read_b(reflexive(Rf, Ss), reflexive(Rf?, C?)) :- ground(Rf?), ground(Ss?) | as_read_c(Ss?, C).

procedure as_read_c(WContract?, WContract).
as_read_c([], []).
as_read_c([S|Ss], [S1?|R?]) :- ground(S?), ground(Ss?) |
    as_read_s(S?, S1),
    as_read_c(Ss?, R).

procedure as_read_s(WSchema?, WSchema).
as_read_s(sas(Nm, Ns, Vs, H, B, Cn, G), S?) :-
    ground(Nm?), ground(Ns?), ground(Vs?), ground(H?), ground(B?), ground(Cn?), ground(G?) |
    sas_ana(H?, B?, Cn?, A),
    sas_table_of(Ns?, A?, G?, E),
    sas_schema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, H?, B?, Cn?, G?, S0),
    as_read_n(S0?, E?, S).
as_read_s(S, S?) :- otherwise | true.

procedure as_read_n(NSchema?, REnts?, WSchema).
as_read_n(schema(Nm, Vs, Rs), E, schema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, Rs?)) :- ground(Rs?), ground(E?) |
    as_read_names(Rs?, E?, 1, Ns).
as_read_n(cschema(Nm, Vs, X, Rs), E, cschema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, X?, Rs?)) :- ground(Rs?), ground(E?) |
    as_read_names(Rs?, E?, 1, Ns).
as_read_n(nschema(Nm, Vs, Cn, Rs), E, nschema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, Cn?, Rs?)) :- ground(Rs?), ground(E?) |
    as_read_names(Rs?, E?, 1, Ns).
as_read_n(qschema(Nm, Vs, Bd, Cn, Rs, Cj, Fs), E, qschema(Nm?, Ns?, Vs?, Bd?, Cn?, Rs?, Cj?, Fs?)) :- ground(Rs?), ground(E?) |
    as_read_names(Rs?, E?, 1, Ns).

% The name of each role, numbered from I, as its clause names it: an agent
% role's its own and a listed role's the variable its quantifier binds (GSC
% 7324ec7, Section 2), the table numbering the roles in the order of the
% schema's names.
procedure as_read_names(NRoleSpecs?, REnts?, Integer?, Names).
as_read_names([], _, _, []).
as_read_names([_|Rs], E, I, [N?|R?]) :- ground(Rs?), ground(E?), integer(I?) |
    as_read_name(E?, I?, N),
    I1 := I? + 1,
    as_read_names(Rs?, E?, I1?, R).

% The name of the role numbered I in the table.
procedure as_read_name(REnts?, Integer?, RName).
as_read_name([], _, '_').
as_read_name([ar(N, J)|_], I, N?) :- I? =:= J? | true.
as_read_name([lr(N, J)|_], I, N?) :- I? =:= J? | true.
as_read_name([_|Es], I, R?) :- otherwise, integer(I?) | as_read_name(Es?, I?, R).

imported procedure check#check_named(Constant?, Verdict).
exported procedure check_named(Constant?, Verdict).
check_named(Nm, V?) :- check # check_named(Nm?, V).

imported procedure check#check_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Verdict).
exported procedure check_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Verdict).
check_variant(Nm, B, V?) :- check # check_variant(Nm?, B?, V).

imported procedure check#traceable_of(Constant?, Preds).
exported procedure traceable_of(Constant?, Preds).
traceable_of(Nm, E?) :- check # traceable_of(Nm?, E).

imported procedure check#traceable_preds(NDeclared?, Preds).
exported procedure traceable_preds(WDeclared?, Preds).
traceable_preds(D, E?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # traceable_preds(D0?, E).

imported procedure check#traceable_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Preds).
exported procedure traceable_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Preds).
traceable_variant(Nm, B, E?) :- check # traceable_variant(Nm?, B?, E).

% --- Restriction by its syntactic approximations (restrict.glp) ------------
% GSC, Section "Relations among Contracts": def:stronger and prop:syntactic.
% nd(Name, RoleNames, Schema): a schema as written, the names of its roles
% (wsch_rnames) and its form; rm(I, J), role I of the weaker schema read as
% role J of the stronger, J 0 where it is none, and pm(X, J), its agent
% variable X read as role J; SB, whether the body of one schema is shown
% stronger than another's (def:stronger), with the faults where it is not,
% each of the weaker schema's role I, atom, formula, conjunct of its
% constraint or variable that the condition misses; shape(NoNewRole,
% SameGuards); RStep, a step of prop:syntactic taken from C to C', and
% RFault, why C' is not shown to restrict C; RVerdict, restriction(Steps),
% C' restricting C by them, restriction_given_invariant(Steps, Schemas), the
% same where the invariant of clause (c) holds of each schema named, which
% no syntactic condition decides, or not_shown(Faults).
ND       ::= nd(Constant, NameOfs, NSchema).
NDs      ::= [] ; [ND | NDs].
NDFound  ::= nd_found(ND) ; nd_none.
WFound   ::= ws_found(WSchema) ; ws_none.
OfFound  ::= of(Constant) ; no_of.
RM       ::= rm(Integer, Integer) ; pm(Constant, Integer) ; vm(Arg, Arg).
VMR      ::= vmr(RMs) ; vm_clash.
VFoundA  ::= va_found(Arg) ; va_none.
RMs      ::= [] ; [RM | RMs].
SBFault  ::= role_missing(Integer) ; role_kind(Integer) ; head_differs(Integer)
           ; conjuncts_differ ; not_required(Integer, Mult)
           ; not_forbidden(Integer, Mult) ; formula_missing(Form)
           ; constraint_not_implied(Constraint) ; variable_missing(Arg)
           ; carried_differ ; extra_role(Integer) ; variable_clash(Arg).
SBFaults ::= [] ; [SBFault | SBFaults].
SB       ::= stronger ; not_stronger(SBFaults).
Shape    ::= shape(Ans, Ans).
% What a stronger body is decided on, and what restriction is: the parts of
% the two schemas, and of the two contracts.
SBParts  ::= sbp(NRoleSpecs, NRoleSpecs, Conjuncts, Conjuncts, Forms, Forms,
                 Constraint, Constraint, Args, Args, NumCtx).
RParts   ::= rp(Verdict, Verdict, Preds, Preds, WContract, WContract, Wrap).
RStep    ::= kept(Constant) ; replaced_a(Constant) ; replaced_c(Constant)
           ; added_b(Constant, Constant) ; deleted_a(Constant).
RSteps   ::= [] ; [RStep | RSteps].
RFault   ::= not_sg(Constant, Verdict) ; preds_not_in_base(Preds)
           ; body_not_stronger(Constant, SBFaults) ; guards_differ(Constant)
           ; roles_differ(Constant) ; added_guarded(Constant)
           ; no_schema_of(Constant) ; deleted_unguarded(Constant)
           ; step_not_sg(RStep, Verdict) ; no_simple_unguarded(Constant).
RFaults  ::= [] ; [RFault | RFaults].
RVerdict ::= restriction(RSteps) ; restriction_given_invariant(RSteps, Constants)
           ; not_shown(RFaults).
Wrap     ::= w_list ; w_refl(Preds) ; w_env(Preds) ; w_env_refl(Preds, Preds).

imported procedure restrict#restricts(WDeclared?, WDeclared?, RVerdict).
% restricts(C', C, V): whether C' restricts C by prop:syntactic (restrict.glp).
exported procedure restricts(WDeclared?, WDeclared?, RVerdict).
restricts(R, B, V?) :- restrict # restricts(R?, B?, V).

imported procedure restrict#stronger_body(WSchema?, WSchema?, SB).
% stronger_body(Tau', Tau, SB): whether the body of Tau' is shown stronger than
% that of Tau, by the checker's sufficient condition for def:stronger.
exported procedure stronger_body(WSchema?, WSchema?, SB).
stronger_body(S, T, V?) :- restrict # stronger_body(S?, T?, V).

% The introductory acts of a contract, for inspection (def:introduction,
% def:unobstructed): each unobstructed, or obstructed with its faults.
imported procedure check#intro_acts(NDeclared?, IntroActs).
exported procedure intro_acts(WDeclared?, IntroActs).
intro_acts(D, A?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # intro_acts(D0?, A).

imported procedure check#intro_acts_variant(Constant?, WContract?, IntroActs).
exported procedure intro_acts_variant(Constant?, WContract?, IntroActs).
intro_acts_variant(Nm, B, A?) :- check # intro_acts_variant(Nm?, B?, A).

% The introduction with wards (GAI, "Contracts with Wards"), for inspection:
% what the search found, or that there is none; the guardianships for a set
% of marks; and the leaving marks for it, with each choice of a guardianship
% per mark.
imported procedure check#wards_of(Constant?, Wards).
exported procedure wards_of(Constant?, Wards).
wards_of(Nm, W?) :- check # wards_of(Nm?, W).

imported procedure check#wards(NDeclared?, Wards).
exported procedure wards(WDeclared?, Wards).
wards(D, W?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # wards(D0?, W).

imported procedure check#wards_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Wards).
exported procedure wards_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Wards).
wards_variant(Nm, B, W?) :- check # wards_variant(Nm?, B?, W).

imported procedure check#guardianships(NDeclared?, Preds?, Guardianships).
exported procedure guardianships(WDeclared?, Preds?, Guardianships).
guardianships(D, M, G?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # guardianships(D0?, M?, G).

% The atoms the relay acts of the introduction with wards require at their ward roles as atoms of h, by clause 2 of def:relay and by none of its other alternatives (GSC 410a440), of a contract given as a term.
imported procedure check#relay_h(NDeclared?, RelayHs).
exported procedure relay_h(WDeclared?, RelayHs).
relay_h(D, H?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # relay_h(D0?, H).

% The leaving marks of a contract for a set of marks (def:leaving), for each
% choice of a guardianship of each mark, of a contract given as a term and
% of a fixture by name.
imported procedure check#leaving(NDeclared?, Preds?, Leavings).
exported procedure leaving(WDeclared?, Preds?, Leavings).
leaving(D, M, L?) :- unnamed(D?, D0), check # leaving(D0?, M?, L).

imported procedure check#leaving_of(Constant?, Preds?, Leavings).
exported procedure leaving_of(Constant?, Preds?, Leavings).
leaving_of(Nm, M, L?) :- check # leaving_of(Nm?, M?, L).

imported procedure contracts#contract(Constant?, NDeclared).
exported procedure contract_named(Constant?, NDeclared).
contract_named(Nm, C?) :- contracts # contract(Nm?, C).

imported procedure contracts#variant(Constant?, WContract?, WDeclared).
exported procedure variant(Constant?, WContract?, WDeclared).
variant(Nm, B, C?) :- contracts # variant(Nm?, B?, C).

imported procedure compile#compile_named(Constant?).
exported procedure compile_named(Constant?).
compile_named(Nm) :- compile # compile_named(Nm?).

imported procedure compile#compile_contract(Constant?, NDeclared?).
exported procedure compile_contract(Constant?, WDeclared?).
compile_contract(Nm, D) :- ground(D?) |
    read_faults(D?, F),
    compile_read(F?, Nm?, D?).

imported procedure compile#compile_malformed(Constant?, Faults?).
procedure compile_read(Faults?, Constant?, WDeclared?).
compile_read([], Nm, D) :- unnamed(D?, D0), compile # compile_contract(Nm?, D0?).
compile_read([F|Fs], Nm, _) :- compile # compile_malformed(Nm?, [F?|Fs?]).

imported procedure compile#compile_variant(Constant?, WContract?).
exported procedure compile_variant(Constant?, WContract?).
compile_variant(Nm, B) :- compile # compile_variant(Nm?, B?).

imported procedure compile#compile_schema(Constant?, Constant?).
exported procedure compile_schema(Constant?, Constant?).
compile_schema(Nm, Sn) :- compile # compile_schema(Nm?, Sn?).

imported procedure compile#compile_schema_in(Constant?, NDeclared?, Constant?).
exported procedure compile_schema_in(Constant?, WDeclared?, Constant?).
compile_schema_in(Nm, D, Sn) :- ground(D?) |
    read_faults(D?, F),
    compile_s_read(F?, Nm?, D?, Sn?).

procedure compile_s_read(Faults?, Constant?, WDeclared?, Constant?).
compile_s_read([], Nm, D, Sn) :- unnamed(D?, D0), compile # compile_schema_in(Nm?, D0?, Sn?).
compile_s_read([F|Fs], Nm, _, _) :- compile # compile_malformed(Nm?, [F?|Fs?]).

imported procedure compile#compile_schema_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Constant?).
exported procedure compile_schema_variant(Constant?, WContract?, Constant?).
compile_schema_variant(Nm, B, Sn) :- compile # compile_schema_variant(Nm?, B?, Sn?).

imported procedure notation#notation_contract(WDeclared?).
exported procedure notation_contract(WDeclared?).
notation_contract(D) :- notation # notation_contract(D?).
